   127	### C. Summarized events put on the page (≈46,000)
   128	
   129	- **The cold months (131st–264th)** [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] (≈14,000). The first week of ice. The pricing scene at the inn. The cold-term board [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6]. The fence trip. The river becoming a road. Hesk and Vell's letters gone west on the last ferry, with the answers pending. Karis's back room. The long dark. The thaw. Pike in his room. The source's log entries become scenes, and the log stays as punctuation between them.
   130	- **The week before the ferry (270th–276th)** (≈4,000). Tents return to the meadow. Teague's crew prepares for the road after the thaw. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] Oryn's first Lowmarch stop: patients at the plank, seen from the outside.
   131	- **Treswick's days** (≈8,000). The outer district as a mechanism: brokers' tally boards, the smith's two forges, the ring road at night. The undramatized chamber days.
