   727	- **Pike (44:101–163).** The twelfth line: *Clearance; the cut below the shoulder hold. Eight. Twenty; paid.* The thirteenth is the protected line, its last two columns empty and said to be empty. **The season line is dated:** a day in its ruled space by his own book's reckoning, nothing printed; "Eleventh. And dated." **As repaired, Cael reads the line as it is written without marking where he stands; Pike's "You're on my side." comes after the season line, and Cael then sees that he has read two leaves the right way up over the stump of an arm.**
