   749	### State at movement end (author; governed by the rulings above and by the surviving prose)
   750	*(Refreshed after repair r1. No fact of the calendar, the purse, the loads, the bodies or the counts changed in repair; what changed is noted in italics.)*
   751	
   752	**Calendar.** First light on the **two hundred and ninety-ninth day past the Line**, at the head of the notch above Millrace. Days on the page: 294, 295, 296, 297, 298, 299 (dawn). No season, month or weekday name; no figure for the technician's date; no date printed for Pike's season line; no count of years since the Kindling.
   753	
   754	**Where everyone is.** Twelve and a mule, in file: Seln ahead; the tall man; Teague, with Cael at his left shoulder a stride back; Lira; the young one; Karis, the two healers and the brown mule in the middle; Brom; Vastin a stride behind him; the bow last. Cleon is under Treswick with the leaf, the chronicle and the board. Pike is at Lowmarch.
   755	
   756	**Cael.** Nineteen. **Twelve fragments. Deployment thirty-two.** He was a lamp for ten days and has entered it. He did not look back at the crown from the bridge. He has told Oryn the two self-readings of the 281st, the eleventh and the twelfth. He has told nobody the two words (*still*; *set*), the warning, or the date. He holds Oryn's finding word for word and has not written it; he has written that one thing came under her hands, unasked, and four reasons for not writing what. He has told Lira that something came and that he has no name for it. He walks at Teague's left and has said aloud that the field is Teague's. He lent the dividers twice and did not open them. *He has marked, beside the protected log, which of its claims are the paper's and which are his own.* The eleventh's debt stands. Body: sound; the eyes paid on the night of the 298th.
   757	
   758	**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. No burst. The arm is "an arm" (day thirty-three out of the wool on the 298th); Oryn: she listened the second time it told her. She said "Sixth chair." She offered the leaf and was declined. *She knows from his eyes that the twelfth looked at something on the night of the 298th; she did not see him change on the plank.* She has agreed to wait.
   759	
   760	**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. No grey. Left shoulder mended by Oryn; right re-tied by the older healer in two yards; both arms come up to his shoulders on the 299th. *He said "Held," in the cut.* The rope debt is paid; the thumbed slip is with Pike. **The purse: a hundred and twenty-seven.**
   761	
   762	**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three; no point struck. She holds her own copy of the leaf's back and Cleon's drawn copy. She has the fourth line (the mark; those who are kindled; what is set; three), the three boxes with the first empty, *the four series years (61, 94, 138, 206: years counted from the first sheet that the office holds for each place)*, a fifth place of the two-bar mark with no figure, and the office's run to it. She has not said the compass point or the figure in lengths aloud; five lines of the list are unturned. Left palm: stitches drawn, in Oryn's linen; she writes and draws with it. The hide has a clean sheet pinned to its eastern edge, with a prick at the divider's point and a line ruled a hand's breadth past it.
   763	
   764	**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze. Out front. He has seen a horseman who behaves as a watcher would, and a riderless horse; he puts it no higher. *He has said only that he had supposed the survey to be six years old.* The case is on him, shut; not mentioned.
   765	
   766	**Vastin.** No office; no age stated. **Right knee: day twenty of thirty on the 299th**; Oryn's linen and two new laths; the month as counted. He rode on the level and walked every hill, the cut and the notch. *"Here," and "Two words. Both of them ours." are his;* he stood on the leg once with the stick up. He kept and signed the tally. He sat before the six and laid no copper. He took Oryn's "Stand there." without a clause, gave her "Nineteen days," and stood an hour. He has said "Noted" twice (the grade; the knee). *He put stake thirty-two back into the tarred case, which he carries.* He is on Teague's count as one of "your six"; that is a count for a contract; he has not asked to join and nobody has spoken of it. *The factor made him no offer.* He does not know the mechanism, the eleventh, the twelfth, the two words, the date, or what is under the bar; he knows that he is not told, and that it is "six people's".
   767	
   768	**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four, provisional. Nobody has died under her hands. She has read Brom, Lira, Karis and Vastin, each asked first, and Cael, asked first, for forty minutes, to her own floor; her finding is given (46:189), standing. She knows of twelve and whose the eleventh and twelfth were; she felt "something turn over, out at the edge" and thought nothing of it. **She has not heard the leaf** and has not been shown the grade. *She has three holds owed yet on this round; her road lies with theirs for a day and some and then turns;* she is on nobody's count and is sent by nobody; she has sat in the sixth place.
   769	
   770	**Teague and his crew.** The contract is taken: ten on the count; shares and costs by the count; the field his; the reading Karis's. *"The wall's still the wall." and the Force line are his.* His wrist was used once, on a cart, and is wrapped in linen under the leather. He has not said "Noted." The tall man, the bow and the older healer have said nothing to the six. What his four have been told: that an office's survey was read at Treswick and gave a bearing; that the wall has a month on it; the four figures on the hide and "three days past the iron". Not told: the leaf, the list, the mechanism, any fragment, the date, who Vastin was.
   771	
   772	**Pike's book and the cloth.** Thirteen lines; the thirteenth with its last two columns empty. The season line is dated (a day; no figure). Eleventh on the cloth.
   773	
   774	**Cleon.** Rune, Bronze. He turned the skin, drew its back, gave Karis his copy, took his lamp back, and said his two lines at the iron. He did not look at Cael. He is not above ground.
   775	
   776	**The faction.** One horseman, unidentified, on the 296th; a riderless horse on the western bank on the 297th. Nothing east of the river in these chapters.
   777	
   778	**Objects and money.** **130 → 128** (the 295th: the rope, two marks) **→ 127** (the 298th: meal and a flitch, one mark). Coppers are small money: Vastin's three to the dray's carter; the ferry's fare waived. The reserve sealed in the third box. The rope debt is paid. On the mule: three boxes, the flat, a sack of meal, Oryn's pannier and canvas. With Karis: the hide with its pinned sheet, the Ternhall brass, her notebook, Cleon's roll, the sheet of three boxes, Vastin's copied page. With Cael: Hesk's book, the dividers shut in it, the fair copy of the leaf. With Vastin: the tarred kit case, *with stake thirty-two back in it, never driven*.
   779	
   780	**Who knows what.** The mechanism: six, as before; Cleon knows how one fragment came. The twelfth: the six (Oryn now among them) and Cleon. The eleventh: Cael, Lira (the log) and Oryn; not Vastin. The warning: Cael and Cleon. **The two words: Cael alone.** That something came on the plank: Cael; Lira (by his eyes and his word); Oryn only as "one of yours, in its sleep". The leaf: unchanged (not Oryn, Teague or Pike). The list's fourth line and the grade: the six and Vastin; Teague in part. The date: Cael and Seln, each alone.
   781	
   782	**Open threads.** Two findings that do not agree, and one of them in nobody's book. A warning that has begun to lean. A box ruled for a mark that no sheet carries. A fifth place with no figure and two signs unread in its corner. Five lines of a list spelled and not turned. A compass point and a measure that Karis has not said aloud. A line ruled past a point. A debt to a man who walks a stride behind Brom. A horse in the alders. A wrist in linen. Oryn's road, which runs with theirs for a day and some.
