   529	### State at movement end (author; governed by the rulings above and by the surviving prose)
   530	**Calendar.** The night of the **two hundred and ninetieth day past the Line**, in the long loft at Treswick. Days on the page: 284 (the Deepstacks), 285 (the hatch; the lamp), 286 (the dray; the board; Seln's roof at night), 287 (the morning log; the figures; four times; Cleon's week and close; the parapet), 288 (the test; ten letters; "We are looked at"), 289 (the loft paid; the ladders; thirteen), 290 (fourteen; the alley; the loft). No season, month or weekday name; no figure for the technician's date; no count of years since the Kindling.
   531	
   532	**Where everyone is.** Six in the loft: Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Vastin (on a pallet under the blanketed gable window, unable to stand), and Seln on the ladder's head. Cleon is under the registry with fifty-two sheets on three tables, the board against the third, and tomorrow's card written and given. The clerk has written *the same* on six days. Oryn and the brown mule are north on her round (not on the page in this movement). Teague's five are east of the river (not on the page).
   533	
   534	**Cael.** Nineteen. **Eleven fragments. Deployment thirty-two.** He has stood unfiled in the middle gallery. He has been the lamp since the 285th and has knelt two feet from Rune in use for five days; nothing has come of that. He has begun to put the light where the looking will go. He wanted the Path tried on himself, wrote that he had not said so, and has not said so. He has the eleventh (Iron-Wall-adjacent), has read its lines, has told it no three times, and has not used it. **He has not told Vastin**, and holds that he cannot without telling the mechanism, which is the six's. He has not set foot on the square or its steps and has not looked at the crown; he has walked the lane with its four alleys fourteen times. He has ruled that the cut is not climbed at dusk again and has ruled nothing else for the morning. Body: sound; a tarred case struck his ear.
   535	
   536	**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. No burst. **Arm: day twenty-five out of the wool on the 290th.** It held a lamp-ring, a ladder's rail and a belt; she has practised dropping off a ladder with it tucked (eleven times before the 289th) and came off a landing so in the alley. **Right shoulder bruised on a wall; the arm took nothing.** Her knife is sound. Her registry paper has not been touched. She keeps the square's side of Cael in the lane. She has read the 285th's log and the 290th's.
   537	
   538	**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. **No grey at any point.** Toes done on the 289th. **Left shoulder wrenched under the dray on the 286th and made worse by the slab on the 290th; he cannot raise either arm above the elbow.** He has carried his box on the bound right shoulder since the 286th and took two falling people on that arm on the 290th: owed to two healers at the mill, entered by Cael as his own debt as much as Brom's. He was offered the broker's post and has, in his own mind, turned it down (the factor has been told only "I'll think on it"). **The purse: a hundred and thirty-four.** He sewed Karis's hand. He means to buy the rope going out.
   539	
   540	**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three; no point struck since the fork. She has said "Older than [UNBOUND]" once, at Cleon's table. She has heard Cleon say, of himself, what being believed is, and has known it for her own as well; she told Brom what had believed him (her fifty-two sheets agree with the thing on his shelf). She asked the five for his week and was given it. **Fourteen letters of twenty-three; she can read the cutter's figures and number-words and nothing else, and will not guess.** She knows that seven kinds bear, twenty-three are carried and eleven are nothing; that a bearer heads every run; that the board and the floors carry the same rows. She has not asked for the bundle. **Vastin's page is in her coat, unshown; the title on it has not been spoken.** She holds the flat, the hide, the ledger, her notebook and the day's card. **Left palm: seven stitches, bound in a strip of Brom's shirt.** Three days of Cleon's week remain.
   541	
   542	**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze. A clerk of the Treswick registry knows his face and has heard him speak. He watches from the roof over the cut. He has looked at the registry, its three doors and the station's light from a roof, with the case on him, and has ruled nothing. **The case is on him, shut; its contents are not named in this movement.** He has the better half of his cord and the stave. He has seen the same boots three times.
   543	
   544	**Vastin.** No office; no age stated. **He stood a wall on the eleventh day of thirty.** The knee let go sideways when he released it; one lath cracked; Brom has bound it again with a slat; it is twice its size; he cannot stand or hold a bowl on the night of the 290th. He knows what Oryn said it would cost. He gave his name, rank and office at the yard hatch on the 285th and was not written. He has apologised to Seln and been told to be nobody. He has asked for the wall to be entered and has been told that it is. **He does not know** the mechanism, what Cael carries, that anything was taken from him, the sum, or what is under the bar; he does not know what the six in hoods hoped to see and has said that he does not ask. He has not asked to join and nobody has spoken of it. Whether he heard Seln speak of the roof is not known.
   545	
   546	**Cleon.** Rune Path, Bronze; shown from outside only. He has said that he knows the hand; has shown the board; has said what bears, what is carried and what is nothing; has given the limit in both its parts; has said what being believed is to him and asked for a week (the 284th); has re-set that week to run from the 287th with his own page put by; has spoken his close; has Karis's name and has used it once. **He has taken no notice of Cael.** He does not know that anybody was set upon in the cut.
   547	
   548	**The clerk.** Unnamed. One question asked ("The same?"). He has heard a name, a rank and an office said at his hatch and has written none of them.
   549	
   550	**The faction.** Six, hooded, unnamed, faceless. It reached inside the third wall, opened no Path, took nobody and nothing, and saw a wall, a rock, a knife in a stave and a boy standing on a step. **It saw nothing of what Cael carries.** It saw Vastin's face uncovered and an Iron Wall. It knows the loft, and has shown that it knows.
   551	
   552	**Objects and money.** **134 marks** (136 less two for the loft's second week, paid on the 289th; the loft is theirs to the 295th). The reserve sealed in the third box. Three boxes, the kit case, the flat and the hide are in the loft. The fifty-two first copies are on Cleon's tables. In the loft besides: a shortened watchman's stave with a knife-cut in it; the card for the 291st. Two bolts were left lying in the cut. Still owed: sixty yards of four-strand to the Lowmarch ferryman.
   553	
   554	**Who knows what.** The mechanism: six, as before; not Vastin, Cleon or the clerk. The eleventh: Cael and Lira (from the log). The sum: Cael and Seln, each alone. Cael's wish to be read: Cael and his book (Lira reads the book).
   555	
   556	**Open threads.** A debt to a man who cannot be told. A knee that may have bought a stick. Two shoulders and a hand for two healers at a mill. A bundle that nobody has untied, and a page that has not been shown. Nine letters to find, and one word covered with a glove. A boy who knows which way a lamp will be wanted. A question that he has not asked, of a man who has not looked up. A case that has been looked at. A clerk who has heard a name. Boots under a lamp. A stair that will not be climbed at dusk, and no ruling yet on what is to be climbed instead.
   557	
   558	### Next-movement inheritance (Sol plan audit §8; also written into the next packet)
   559	Packet 006 carries the 291st, borrowed handcart, Karis's bound left hand, eleven fragments, and the fact that three clerk questions remain unasked (`MOVEMENT-006.md:26–28`). Its author must additionally inherit the following surviving particulars:
   560	
   561	- **Deepstacks geography and custody.** Inside the iron door: black sliding bar; twenty-seven dark-stone steps in three flights; a short cross-way; three side-by-side galleries. Middle gallery: roughly 110 strides, shelving to the roof, old sorting tables from ninety strides, Cleon's sloped desk and fixed lamp at the end, with cup/jar/brown-taped bundle/board shelf above. Eastern gallery: tall old-town ledgers and ladders. Western gallery: quarry material, where the board was found. Fifty-two first copies remain on three tables; the board is against the third and the bundle remains tied on the shelf (`chapter-27.md:5–121`; `chapter-30.md:263–273`; `chapter-33.md:305`).
   562	- **What has been deciphered and by whom.** Karis alone has fourteen of twenty-three letters; she can read figures and number-words only. She knows seven kinds bear, twenty-three are carried and eleven are ornament/nothing, that a bearer heads a run, and that board and floors repeat the same rows. She has covered one tempting six-sign group and has not guessed it. Vastin's copied page remains in her coat, unshown to Cleon (`chapter-31.md:63–189,319–339`; `chapter-32.md:3–19`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:111`).
   563	- **Cleon's knowledge and statements.** Cleon knows Karis's name and has used it once; he knows the hand, has externally demonstrated bearer/carried/ornament and “orders,” has stated both limits, has matched the same make, and has delivered the documentation/built-twice close. His week runs from the 287th through the 293rd. He has not noticed Cael, learned of the alley, shown the inside/lean, or acquired knowledge of the mechanism (`chapter-27.md:187–199`; `chapter-29.md:193–289`; `chapter-30.md:253–279`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:117`).
   564	- **The eleventh and its entry.** Iron-Wall-adjacent, from Vastin, partial/held/defensive/rooted, tier equivalent unknown, deployment none. Cael has read it, refused its *This far?* three times, deployed nothing, and told only the log; Lira has therefore read it. Vastin has not been told. Cael recorded both Vastin's requested wall entry and more than Vastin knows (`chapter-32.md:237–257`; `chapter-33.md:149–175,205–227,291–299`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:105,125`).
   565	- **Vastin.** Right knee, original day eleven of thirty: gone sideways again, re-lathed with one slat from Brom's box, twice its former size; on the night of the 290th he cannot stand or hold a bowl. He knowingly heard and broke Oryn's no-wall order and asks that she be told he heard. He has no office on the page, no stated age, and still knows nothing of the mechanism or eleventh (`chapter-33.md:129–145,185–227,285`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:115`).
   566	- **Karis.** Left palm has a long shallow cut and seven stitches, bound in a strip of Brom's shirt; she writes right-handed. No healer inside the gate has seen her. She has three days left of Cleon's week (`chapter-33.md:63–125,277,305`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:111`).
   567	- **Brom.** Toes are done. The older right shoulder remains bound; the left/good shoulder was wrenched under the dray and worsened by the alley slab, leaving neither arm raisable above the elbow. He carries his box on the bound right shoulder. He has effectively rejected the broker's four-marks-and-found guard post, but the factor heard only `I'll think on it.` Cael has entered the shoulders as a debt for the mill's healers (`chapter-29.md:45–147`; `chapter-31.md:265–271`; `chapter-32.md:117–137`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:109`).
   568	- **What the faction knows.** It knows the loft and has deliberately shown that knowledge. It saw Vastin's uncovered face and Iron Wall, plus a rock/knife/still boy, but no Path from another crew member, no face of its own was secured, and it saw nothing of quiet ground or Cael's fragments. Seln's finding is that it wanted a visible declaration and a carried box and avoided being entered itself (`chapter-33.md:247–289`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:121`).
   569	- **Inn, purse, count and day.** Six are in the long loft over the stable; it is paid through the 295th, with pot at dusk and seven bowls. Purse 134, reserve sealed in the third box. The below-ground daily count remains Karis as bearer plus four hands; Seln is never one of them. Night of day 290 is complete; Movement 6 opens day 291. The cut will not be climbed at dusk again, but no further route ruling has been made (`chapter-31.md:265–267`; `chapter-33.md:277–305`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:101–103,123`).
   570	- **Lira and remaining objects.** Lira is day twenty-five out of wool, has a bruised right shoulder, and the left arm took nothing. Three boxes, kit case, flat and hide are in the loft; the 291st card is there; the shortened watchman's stave is with Seln; two plain bolts remain in the cut; sixty yards of four-strand are still owed and Brom means to buy them going out (`chapter-33.md:285–307`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:107,123`).
   571	- **Seln and the case.** Seln is at the ladder head/roof watch, knows the same altered boots through three sightings, and has the better half of his cord and the stave. A Treswick clerk knows his face and voice. His case is on him and **shut**; five people know its contents from Book 6, but this movement names none. He looked at the registry/front-yard-returns-door choice and decided nothing (`chapter-30.md:3–151`; `chapter-33.md:183,247–275`; `book-06 chapter-38.md:167`; `book-06 chapter-39.md:5,15,217`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:113`).
   572	
   573	**Movement 5 CLOSED (2026-10-12).** Same-author repair r1 (ch27–31; ch32–33 untouched apart from the eleventh's lines set in italics): the eight coordinator-applied fixes kept and re-joined — **ch27's scene at the Hall's table now turns on Cleon** (Cael's "Then what is it?" goes to Karis, who does not answer; Cleon, eyes shut at his desk, says the "Being believed" unit to himself in the hearing of five; Karis tells Brom who has believed him; Cleon opens his eyes for "Give me a week."; **Karis then asks the five in her own words — "I should like his week" — and Cael says it is hers**); ch30, Cleon re-sets his own week from the 287th (half the first went on his own page each morning; that is put by); ch31's opening keeps only her side of being believed; Seln's line at the hatch whole, with the narration noting that he said nothing that was not in the clerk's own book or at his ledge, "and he had said *we*, which lay in no book at all"; Cleon's close whole with the author's joins. The tracked passage re-ordered (Cleon gives his table orders over his shoulder with his finger on his line; when Cael looks again the chair is empty and the leaf lies face up, unmarked); two physical anchors in the cipher proof; restated method compressed; first-use anchors added. Sol recheck: **CLOSE, no line fixes**; the tracked passage RESOLVED; every binding ruling borne out; the coordinator's ruling on the eleventh's lines (Cael's own cataloguing, in italics, not a system block) treated as settled and consistent on the page. The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report. Final: 35,987 prose words; gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (17 protected). Purse 134 marks; deployment thirty-two; **eleven fragments**; the night of day 290, in the loft at Treswick.
