   132	## Guards (kept open while drafting)
   133	
   134	- §9: the leaf is not quoted; "four hundred" and "the Architect" only inside the 305th close (which is a marker) and "four hundred" not at all in my own prose; the S19 log has neither. No *terminal*, *circuit*, *infrastructure*. Nothing lays the leaf on the lamps finding — not Vastin (his sentence stops), not Karis's night, not Cael, not the narration.
   135	- The date: one silent look on the blanket; nothing said or written.
   136	- No season, month or weekday name; "spring" only as water. No count of years since the Kindling. No possessive before "Path" in narration. No age for Vastin. No noun "bearer" for a sign. No "unopened" or "locked" of the case.
   137	- The tall man and the older healer speak to none of the six. The broad man's only word to them is "Aye" (53.1).
