   132	## Guards (kept open while drafting)
   133	
   134	- §9: the leaf is not quoted; "four hundred" and "the Architect" only inside the 305th close (which is a marker) and "four hundred" not at all in my own prose; the S19 log has neither. No *terminal*, *circuit*, *infrastructure*. Nothing lays the leaf on the lamps finding — not Vastin (his sentence stops), not Karis's night, not Cael, not the narration.
   135	- The date: one silent look on the blanket; nothing said or written.
   136	- No season, month or weekday name; "spring" only as water. No count of years since the Kindling. No possessive before "Path" in narration. No age for Vastin. No noun "bearer" for a sign. No "unopened" or "locked" of the case.
   137	- The tall man and the older healer speak to none of the six. The broad man's only word to them is "Aye" (53.1).
   138	- No wall; no drill under a wall; "behind it" is not said.
   139	- Consent in a word at every reading (the leg; Brom's wrist at the irons).
   140	- Teague's first "Noted" is 49.3. Vastin's third is 52.4. Oryn's "Everybody says that now" is inside the marker at 51.1.
   141	
   142	## Changes made while drafting (written after the draft)
   143	
   144	- **Chapter 50 has six scenes, not five.** The thirteenth's arrival opens the third (after the "Through." marker, which closes the second); the crossing and the sixty strides are the fourth; the pinch and its eleven seconds the fifth; the bed of the sink the sixth.
   145	- **Chapter 53 is titled "The Shale Step".** The thumbnail ring is pressed in 52.3, where the plan lists it ("the point is fixed"); at the close Karis's forefinger goes down beside it.
   146	- **Decision 13 changed: Oryn is not told of the thirteenth in this movement.** At the irons at noon on the 304th she sees that Cael has something and will not be told "across a row of iron"; an old man is five feet off. Lira is told first, in three words (51.1); Brom has it from her and says so behind the step (53.2). Karis and Seln have it from Lira or from the log.
   147	- **Decision 18 changed: "the rows lean along the bearing"** rests on the twelfth's one unbidden glance over fourteen sheets that Karis had already laid as their walls stood, entered by her as his and as unchecked. I dropped her head-west / tail-east proof: it would have made the south wall's runs read from right to left, against the lamp's rule in the closed Deepstacks chapters (all the looking runs from the low left upward to the right).
   148	- **Decision 19 changed: Seln is not at the blanket** (he has gone to look at the gap), so no glance passes between him and Cael over the second row; Cael keeps his third page alone.
   149	- Vastin is not at the blanket for 52.2 (the lean is told to Karis, Lira and Brom only); Karis sends for him in 52.3.
   150	- Decision 8: the tall man goes back down with the boy's two skins while Teague prices Cael's request; no lichen is carried in a cap (that was Seln's, at the fence, in chapter 2). Dry camp two has two small fires, of a dead hold's rafter. Karis's line about the read was cut from 48.6 as a second telling.
   151	- Decision 7: in the lesson on the brow the second man's want is "the old road to watch", not a rope (Teague knows nothing of the fence that Cael unbound there).
   152	- 49.6 gained Lira's "three breaths" in the dark (the left foot). 51.6: Karis keeps one of the new bars from under the hide, by Teague's leave. 51.6: the log's *tomorrow* is looked at and let stand, as the truth about how near the thing has come.
   153	- The old three ribs are low on the LEFT (Book 7 chapter 55); the thirteenth lies "along him" and is given no side.

