    47	He knew the column. He had known it since a spring: the office's abbreviation, every sheet, every year, that Seln had read for them as *not asking* — the sigil going out at the line, every practitioner, every site, the same distance, the same instant. He had known, too, where the sentence went that Karis had begun over that column at the spring and had stopped, with her pencil down and her hand off the sheet and a rule said aloud in the small voice, because he had heard her not go there twice, and had entered the not-going both times.
