    88	
    89	"A directive. Not a survey; an order about the surveys. Six years back, at the head of the file, in the office's ruling hand — the hand that writes the forms and not the hand that fills them." He read it in the register he had once read everything in, which was the register of a man who had been read to all his life by paper and had read back. "*Findings under the fifth column to be held. Not for onward transmission. Not for citation. Not for the seat.* A seal. A rank I'd have saluted, once." He turned the sheet. "And on the back — " He stopped.
