    24	
    25	The skin lay on the slope of the desk.
    26	
    27	It had been taken out from under its jar before they came. The upper board of beech stood against the rock; and the man in the dusty coat was at the desk with the lower board in one hand and a third, which Cael had not seen before, in the other, like a cook who means to turn a cake.
