   116	
   117	It was not the promise. That was paid, and she would hear at a mill that it had been. It was only that he had seen a light go unsteady once, for a count of one, and had written *hold* beneath it. A person who has ruled *hold* does not go back to stare at the thing, to learn whether it will do so again; that is not holding.
