   115	"*Clearance; the cut below the shoulder hold. Eight. Twenty; paid.* That's twelve lines." The stone went back on the leaf. "And then you never came home. You left word with me: the cut, and whatever lay beyond. A crew's been gone eighteen days past its slip, and I've a line to rule for it, and I don't know what to put. Where's beyond?"
