   183	She was on her feet yet, a pace from the plank, with both hands hanging. The count of his breaths lay behind him, a little short of five hundred, and Cael had sat up without knowing that he did it. Lira had come off the bench; she stood at the lean-to's post with a cup of water from the race, held out, which had not been taken.
