   193	Then she felt behind her for the keg, and sat on it heavily, and took the cup. He had seen her grey, and he had not seen her so. Her face in the lantern was the colour of the ash in a dead ring, and her cropped head hung; and it came to him that the forty minutes had not done the whole of that.
