281:It was on the far side of the iron, the side toward the brow, a hand above the turf, and he saw it through the bar, as a person sees a lamp through his own fingers. It was a single point, as big as a fist. Three courses came into it from the south, across the road; and three came into it from the north, round the whole of that great circle, the other end of the same rope. Nothing came out. Everything that held six people in a low place on the hundred and fourteenth day was hauled taut through that one point and belayed there, like the whole of a ship's rigging brought down to a single pin.
293:It went as a breath goes that a person has been holding, and the point was simply not under his palm. The three courses to the south dropped across the old road, and he saw the nearest ten feet of them go, like wet rope falling; and from the north, away round the dark edge of the low ground, he felt the rest come in and go slack and run out through the place where a knot had been, a great deal of it, for as long as it takes to draw a bucket. He had not known how much ground it held until it stopped holding.
