   176	
   177	It came to her as she blotted the line, and she set the pencil down. Being believed had been the thing that she wanted, for all of those years, as a person wants a meal; and a man under a town had told her what it was like when it arrived. He had said it with his eyes shut, in the hearing of five people. He had said that it was the end of being able to be wrong.
   178	
   179	She had not understood him then. She had thought that he was tired.
