   192	
   193	On her right was the notebook itself, open where it had lain open on a blanket. It showed her own second copy of a thing that she had read aloud once. There was an empty box ruled in its fifth line, where four or five letters had been scraped away, and one upright stroke was drawn at the box's left side.
   194	
   195	There was a hand's breadth of bare wood between the two.
   196	
