   217	If she wrote six words tonight, she would have made that thing herself, out of nothing but the wish to have it. It would be a finding by morning, in five heads. One of the five would begin to draft upon it, and he had told her that afternoon that he could feel nine orders waiting. Another had sat across a fire from her in a yard and said what he wanted from the end of this line; and whatever she wrote, he would carry it into the middle of that place with him.
   218	
   219	She would not hand him a guess to stand on.
   220	
   221	She wanted to. She let herself know that as well, since it was true, and since a refusal that costs nothing is only a habit. She had stood for five years on the wrong side of shut presses. She had never in her life been so near to a thing, with a pencil in reach.
