**Deployment and fragments.** Dawn of the 299th: twelve fragments; deployment thirty-two. **One use in earnest:** the read (Iron-adjacent) on the wet ledge at the seep, the 302nd, six breaths, paid in near sight for an hour (48:247–251; logged with the arithmetic at 48:327: "Thirty-two, and that one … thirty-three"). **32 + 1 = 33.** Nothing was opened on the shelf or inside the line on the 304th (logged at 51:349), and nothing on the 305th. **Fragment thirteen** (Force-adjacent, Teague) came at the timbers on the 304th, at a stride (50:119–129); it has not been used. **Not counted, by this edition's rules:** the twelfth's unbidden outward leans — refused at the old iron by the hall's stone (47:287–289) and at the arch (51:215); taken before he could stop it on the west pier's lowest course (51:311–315, *Goes*; the eyes pay at 51:355) and over the laid-out blanket (52:75–83, *Goes*); and the dry stance on the shale (53:89–121; logged "A trial; not counted", 53:273). The twelfth is never turned inward and never on a person. The eleventh asks *This far?* at the fence (49:65) and at the pinch (50:249) and is told no. **Movement end: thirteen fragments; deployment since the Line thirty-three.**

**Every log in the movement:** 47:185–191 (the 299th; thirty-two; Known); 47:299–307 (the 300th; 123; Known; thirty-two); 48:99–105 (the 301st; Known; thirty-two); 48:321–329 (the 302nd; the read; thirty-three; Known); 49:261–271 (the 303rd; Known; thirty-three); 51:335–353 (the 304th: my head line, the S19 log whole at 51:339, then the thirteenth, the count thirty-three, the short row, the crown); 53:265–275 (the 305th; thirteen; thirty-three).

