editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-50.md:301:The crews had removed the watch's ability to hold the approach by making the only safe retreat a line the watch would not cross and the crews would.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-52.md:181:"They fail the way a hundred lamps fail when one wire's cut. Not the way a hundred souls fall silent."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-52.md:239:"*Findings under the fifth column to be held. Not for onward transmission. Not for citation. Not for the seat.*"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-52.md:249:"*Objection entered: the holding of a finding is not the finding's disproof. Refer to the seat.*"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-52.md:261:"Somebody wanted this buried. Somebody else put it in writing that it shouldn't be. That's not a monolith. That's a crack."
