editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:59:**#35 update (coordinator, 2026-10-05, B4 M5 review).** The plan's own protected lines collided: M4's "Six weeks. I'll see you in the final." (closed, published) vs the M5 closing Log's "Semester evaluation in nine weeks." Ruling: the Log now reads "seventeen days" (BOOK_MAP §9 amended). With the final on the nineteenth of Reaping and the evaluation on the twentieth, M6–M7's events fit the seventeen days (semifinal ≈ the tenth, nine days before the final; delegation the twelfth/thirteenth). The one residue is the birthday's month name: "the eleventh of Sowing" falls about sixteen days before the nineteenth of Reaping. The DEFAULT above stands (never state month order or a cross-month day count). Owner options: accept short months / an intercalary feast-week; or move the birthday to "the third of Reaping" (B5's recollection would follow).
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:152:- **Shadow's first Book 7 use** is restaged so Oryn cannot see or attribute it (audit B2). **#23** (sell the cart and gelding in Lowmarch's first week; the money is a sealed reserve) is treated as binding.
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:162:**#50 update (coordinator, 2026-10-11, before B7 Movement 7).** Default confirmed and written into Movement 7's packet: the line stays verbatim and unglossed; no six-year event is invented; the case's twelve years is not stated in that scene. One thing the owner may like to know: the closed Movement 5 has Seln date the registry's survey of the circles at "five years ago by the stake, maybe six" (ch34), so on the page "six years" can be heard as the time since that survey without any change. If the owner prefers option (1) or (2), it is a one-numeral change.
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:165:The protected second pole closes Movement 6 (ch44, written at the well as day 111 breaks): "…We're going to find the other circles. Pike said nobody goes in twice. Tomorrow makes three." On this edition's calendar "tomorrow" is day 112, a road to Lowmarch's board; the next quiet ground entered is the Stair on day 114. The count is also arguable: the six have gone in at the Fallow once as a party (day 96), or twice if the first crossings at the line are counted. Sol's audit found no honest gloss. **Default until ruled: the line stays word for word, where the plan places it, unglossed.** Options: (1) keep as is (the default); (2) keep the words and move the entry to the night of day 113, the eve of the Stair, where "tomorrow" is true (Movement 6 would then close on Oryn's leaving); (3) supply replacement wording. Options 2 and 3 change published chapters.
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:166:- Related, NOT an owner item: the restored protected line "I'll be three days north by the time you're back at the board" beside Oryn at Millrace (one day south of Lowmarch) on day 113 was resolved by the owner on 2026-09-04 (EXC-B7-003: "her circuit brings her round to the Stair-road stop within three days"; BOOK_MAP lists it under "do not reopen"). Movement 7's packet carries a binding note.
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:170:- **#52 (needed before Book 8 Movement 3).** Karis's protected "right for five years or wrong for five years". Book 7 never states her hypothesis and gives it no five-year history. **Default:** the line stays verbatim as Karis's own rounding; narration does not treat five years as a fact. Options: (1) the owner confirms an older private conviction, five years old, distinct from the Book 7 hypothesis; (2) release the clause for wording without a number; (3) the default.
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:180:Applied under standing decisions, and listed old and new in `B7-RECONCILIATION-APPLIED.md` so any can be restored: Book 8's named seasons (#48) and its three "five years" counts since Kindling (#18), the same changes Books 5–7 made.
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:186:Also settled from the same audit, without owner action: Teague CAN read (Book 7's protected line has him read a slip twice; Book 8's plan said he could not); the stroke and bar is on stakes thirty-two and thirty-four only; the court is about fifty cords across, not 159 (159 of Book 7's cords would be about 3,500 yards, against the plan's own 1,107).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:10:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 1 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Teague's spear is a tall MAN** (he / him): the locked Book 7 wrote him so (ch25, ch51, ch52), and Book 8 follows its own edition (OWNER-pending #59). Where the plan says "the tall woman", read "the tall man"; his silence toward the six until his question at the pass stands. (2) **Teague can read** (locked Book 7 ch25: he read a slip twice). Never write that he cannot; if he does not read a sheet it is because it is not in front of him or he has no need. (3) **Lira's asking:** she asked Oryn once about the ankle on the mountain in Book 7 and asked nobody for anything from then until Thornwater; do not call Thornwater her first ask since Norhold. (4) **The stroke and bar** is on stake thirty-two (the Stair's newer stake and the kit's unused one) and on the fourth site's thirty-four ONLY; stakes thirty-one and thirty-three do not carry it. Later records may show the grade on survey SHEETS; the field stakes do not all carry it. (5) **The cord:** the kit's cord is twenty strides, knotted at the fives (four knots to a length); Book 7's Ring was sixty-two cords and twenty strides round. The court is about 1,107 yards across, which is about FIFTY cords, not 159. Give no yardage for a cord. (6) **"West"** was first said aloud at the six-person table on the 268th (Karis's protected "It's west… Treswick…" speech, printed once in ch6). (7) **Deployment since the Line is twenty-nine** at the end of Movement 1 (two uses of the Iron read in earnest); trials are not counted.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:12:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 2 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Vastin's second paper is "the page": a COPY in his own hand** of one line from an old register ("—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—"). It was never cut from anything and is never called a leaf; "the leaf" is the chamber record of Movement 6 only. (2) **The technician's sheet carries a Compact date (a registry year and a day in it) that is NEVER printed as figures** anywhere in this book; whoever reads it reads a date, and the page does not give its numbers. The office filed that sheet at the end of the second row of the records, and it lies there. (3) **The anomaly column:** on every survey abstract, in every hand, for six years, the entry is the one word *Total* — an entry, not a sum. (4) **The Fallow completion report** carries five strokes for a name and a count of six (locked Book 7), not five written names. (5) **What Vastin has told the six about the layer is four things only:** no key (it cannot be reached); the citation; the suppressed records; the technician's line. He has not defined "classification event" and does not know which event is meant. Nothing on the page says that menders, technicians or any office have tried to open it or know more. (6) **Speakers:** "What follows you," was Lira's; "She's right. Go and lie down, and don't take the stairs fast," was Oryn's. (7) **Deployment since the Line is thirty** at the end of Movement 2 (the Iron read at the landing on the 277th). Purse 118 marks. (8) **Teague's spear** has "he/his" on the page from chapter 7 (OWNER-pending #59 as defaulted). (9) Vastin has shown no Iron Wall, has no stated age, has asked only for a bed, and holds Karis's unsealed receipt. Cael has not touched the page and has not read the sheet's date closely.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:14:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 3 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Deployment since the Line is thirty-two** at the end of Movement 3 (one Ember grain and one Wind burst away, both at the cut on the 279th). Ten fragments; the eleventh has not come; nothing came of standing two feet from Vastin's wall. Purse 138 marks. (2) **Iron Wall has been shown once** (the cut): a plane from a line struck with the stick, wall to wall, rooted — he may not lift a foot — loud to anything that hunts a Path, and it spent him to the floor. **Vastin's RIGHT knee** was bitten there; Oryn shut the holes and bound the joint with laths for a month from the 279th (stick; no kneeling, no running, no wall); he said "I cannot undertake" and has kept it to the letter. Brom's right foot, two toes, ten days from the 279th. (3) **The date:** Cael and Seln each know that the technician's sheet carries the day of Cael's Kindling. Neither has said or written it; neither knows what the other made of it; nobody has interpreted the sequence. No figures are ever printed, no span of years is computed, and there is **no second calendar or offset** (one registry reckoning only). Vastin does no date arithmetic and knows nothing of it. (4) **The records at the spring:** Karis has matched FOUR sign-groups to the hide and has given NO number of places; no fifth place has been described. The same stroke and bar stands in a ruled square on all four matched places' sheets (in the field: stake thirty-two and the fourth site's thirty-fours only). The remark "Behaves as device. Cannot be." is on the Stair's sheet in the fourth row; its hand is NOT identified. The instruments column reads true on every line. (5) **Seln has taught one thing, to Vastin** ("Draft nothing. Just look."). Cleon has been named (by Karis) and nothing more is known of him than her protected lines give. (6) **Oryn** went north from the fork on the 281st with the brown mule, her linen and her crossbow with one bolt; Millrace in three weeks; she owes Cael the reading ("the one thing I'm walking up that road owing"); the station term is written in the log. Her past as told at the fork: a house for the sick in a city inside the Line, the column for the patient's tier, a woman from the river sheds mended off the sheet; she has not been through a gate since. (7) **Loads:** boxes on Brom (good shoulder), Lira (both arms) and Cael; the tarred kit case on Vastin, taken up unasked at the fork-stone; Karis the flat and the hide, with the copied page in oilcloth in her coat. **Cael laid his hand on that page once, on the rise.** Vastin has walked beside Cael since the rise. (8) **Stillhounds:** a den that has learned a road runs to where a declaration ends (Karis's sixth line). The sixty yards of four-strand rope are still owed to the Lowmarch ferryman.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:16:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 4 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Who is where on the 284th:** inside the iron door are Cael, Brom, Lira, Vastin and Karis, with three boxes, the tarred kit case, the flat and the hide; Cleon let them in, counted loads and not people, and shut the door. The unnamed yard clerk is outside; **Seln is above ground, NOT on the card or the count**, watching who comes to the door. Oryn is two gates north with the brown mule. (2) **The count:** Karis is the card's unnamed bearer; Cael, Brom, Lira and Vastin are the four hands, entered by count; the clerk asked nothing and wrote *four*. None of the four restricted names has been written anywhere; the asset-restriction is still pending. Cards are good only for the day written on them and are torn at each gate; Iron passes the second wall and Bronze the third by right, on a certificate that is read out and written. The way to the registry's yard is the load lane under the third wall and a cut of **twenty-two steps in five flights, a stride and a half wide, walled three men high with no door or window**; it never crosses the square. Cael has not set foot on the square or its steps and has not looked at the crown; Lira keeps the same discipline unasked. (3) **Cleon's terms** (given at the cook-house on the 283rd): all the sheets, in their places; they come down to him; no names (his is on the card and is never said aloud by him); **nobody tells him what the sheets are or how old until he has looked**; one lamp goes down with them, his, held where he says; no other carried light and no fire of anybody's. He has seen one drawn sheet and knows there are three places and fifty-two sheets, older than what the Compact found; he has not noticed Cael. **His Path has not been shown.** "Rune Path. Bronze." is all that is known of it, from Seln. (4) **Cael:** ten fragments; deployment thirty-two; the fourth and fifth self-readings were made on the 281st, round the still place and not in, uncounted; Tide feels only what flows and returned nothing ("a cord on a stone… *no length*"); he needs an instrument for what does not move, and owes Oryn the telling at the mill. Lira has read the log. (5) **Vastin and Cael:** Vastin has told him why he declined the second reading (the Ostrand case, causal; and a private relief at never learning what a plate would say); Cael has told him that the place was read twice and returned nothing, and nothing of what reads. Ground, not friendship. Vastin carries three sheets under one seal that he will not show; he has sat three times; his right knee is day five of thirty on the 284th (stick; no kneeling, running or wall) and he caught a slip on the steps with his left hand. Brom's two toes: five days left on the 284th. Lira's arm: day nineteen out of wool; her registry paper unshown; the ladder did not pull. (6) **The inn:** the long loft over the stable, by the yard half-door (the painted door has a book), for a week from the 282nd, pot at dusk, seven bowls; **purse 136 marks**. The outer gate counts feet on a bead-frame and writes no name. (7) **Stone:** the grey bridge, the registry's three lowest courses, the undercroft's end and the iron door's frame are one dark dry-laid stone older than the walls; Karis has seen it and stated no conclusion beyond "the bridge was first". The iron door has no lock or handle outside; the clerk knocks. (8) The sixty yards of four-strand were priced at the rope-walk and are to be bought going out.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:18:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 5 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Eleven fragments; deployment since the Line thirty-two; purse 134 marks** at the end of Movement 5 (the night of the 290th). The eleventh, Iron-Wall-adjacent, came from Vastin in the alley's quiet minute; it did not fill, it *set*; its prompt is *This far?*; it has not been deployed and **Vastin has not been told** (Cael holds that as a debt he cannot yet pay; Lira has read the log). (2) **How acquisition lines are printed in this book:** the protected "Fragment eleven" and "Fragment twelve" units are CAEL'S OWN cataloguing of what he reads — set once, in italics, framed as his plain words; they are NOT printed as a system block and take no FRAGMENT ACQUIRED heading or code fence. (3) **The Deepstacks:** an iron door with a sliding bar inside; twenty-seven steps in three flights of nine; three galleries. Middle gallery about 110 strides, Cleon's sloped desk and fixed lamp at its end, a shelf above it with a jar, a tied bundle ("Paper. Not stone.") and the black oak plank's sacking; the fifty-two sheets on three tables, 11/29/12; the plank stands against the third table. Eastern gallery: the old town's tall tally-books. One CARRIED lamp, Cleon's, held "a hand to the left" (Cael holds it and has begun to put it where the eyes are about to go). The boxes go up at the clerk's bell and come down each morning on a fresh card; the clerk writes *The same* and *four*. (4) **Cleon** knows Karis's name (he heard Brom say it and has used it once); his own is on the card and has never been said aloud. He has shown his Path from OUTSIDE only (bear / carried / nothing; "They're orders."; "Same make."; the limit: it does not work on a river, a man or a tree, and costs his eyes for an hour). **His week runs from the 287th to the 293rd.** He has not noticed Cael and knows nothing of the alley or the mechanism. (5) **Karis** has fourteen of twenty-three letters and reads numbers and number-words only; seven kinds bear, twenty-three are carried, eleven are nothing; the bundle is tied and unread; Vastin's copied page is in her coat, unshown to Cleon. Her LEFT palm has seven stitches of Brom's under a strip of his shirt; she writes with the right. (6) **Vastin:** his right knee went again in the alley on the eleventh day of Oryn's thirty (a wall on it against her order, which he heard and asks that she be told); re-splinted with a slat from Brom's box, twice its size; on the night of the 290th he cannot stand or hold a bowl. He gave his name, rank and office aloud at the yard hatch on the 285th; nothing of it was written. He still knows nothing of what Cael carries. (7) **Brom:** the left (good) shoulder wrenched under a dray on the 286th and worse after the alley; he carries his box on the bound right shoulder, a debt entered for the mill's healers; the broker's offer (a guard's post inside the second wall) was answered "I'll think on it." and declined in fact. Lira: day twenty-five out of wool on the 290th; a bruised right shoulder; she drops from heights without the arm. (8) **Seln:** a registry clerk knows his face and voice (the price of a truthful answer at the hatch); he watches from the roof above the cut. His case is **SHUT** — never "unopened" (this edition's Book 6 opened it for the five) — and its contents are named nowhere in this book. He has seen one watcher three times (horseman's boots with the spur-rests cut away). (9) **The faction** (six, hooded, no faces, no Path opened) knows the loft and has shown that it knows; it saw Vastin's wall, a rock, a knife and a boy who stood still, and nothing of quiet ground or the fragments. Cael has ruled that the cut is not climbed at dusk again. The loft is paid to the 295th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:20:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 6 audit, 2026-10-12 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Twelve fragments; deployment since the Line thirty-two.** The twelfth is **Rune-adjacent, from Cleon** ("given, not taken"), acquired at his "There," on the 291st; it gives single words (*goes*, *sits*, *bears*, *nothing*), reads made things only, and costs the eyes afterward. Its lines are Cael's own cataloguing, printed once in italics in Movement 6 and never reprinted. (2) **How it behaves:** it leans at every made thing, unbidden and OUTWARD, and Cael is learning not to look; it has never been used on a person, the crown or the leaf, and **never turned inward**. He refused the inward turn once, deliberately, until Oryn has been asked. **The first inward turn is unbidden, at Millrace, under Oryn's deep reading** (*still*, then *set*); the deliberate inward turn belongs to the plain's edge in Movement 9. (3) **Who knows the twelfth:** Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Cleon. **Not Oryn (owed at the mill, with the readings round the place); not Vastin** (who also still does not know the eleventh or the mechanism). **Cleon's warning** ("If that fragment ever reads something for you that shouldn't be *made* and reads it anyway — …") is known to Cael and Cleon only and is in no book; Cael tells nobody. (4) **The leaf** was read aloud once by Karis and heard by Karis, Cleon, Cael and Vastin; Lira, Brom and Seln read her copy; Oryn has not heard it. **Nobody quotes the leaf's wording again.** The reductions that may be said: *made*; *for a kind*; "the Architect" as a **title** (historical comparison only — "as old as the Architect" — never a present agent); "four hundred years" only where this packet's plan fixes it. (5) **The chronicle's line is marked and nobody speaks of it again**; the hole is never glossed. **Nobody joins the leaf to the lamps, sigils, plates, Arbiters or stations**; no *terminal*, *circuit*, *infrastructure*; no light, plate or instrument is said to attend, notice or want. (6) **Pole two was said aloud at the yard fire and is not in the log.** The line of march from it: "a site at the end of the line that's been quiet since they built the machine" — "I want to stand in the middle of it." (7) **Seln's case is on his chest, shut, contents unnamed; he keeps it "a while longer".** Closed chapter 18 says he has carried it twelve years; print no other count. He will not follow the cut boots again and expects them on the road east. (8) **State at the night of the 293rd:** purse **130**; the reserve sealed in the third box; loft and handcart to the 295th; sixty yards of four-strand still owed to the Lowmarch ferryman; Hesk's dividers and note shut in Hesk's book (never opened on a distance); Karis's fair copy in Cael's coat, the other in her notebook; the skin leaf under Cleon's jar and going to no counter; its back (a list of parts) unread — Cleon's work for the 294th. **Vastin: right knee day fourteen of thirty on the 293rd**, slat-bound, stick, no kneeling, running or Wall; he sleeps in the stable's end stall and rides the handcart. Karis's left palm stitched (Brom's seven); Brom neither arm above the elbow; Lira day twenty-eight out of wool on the 293rd. (9) **Oryn** watched a Kindling at her fourth gate, is two days behind, will not come late to the mill, and means to read Cael "as deep as she went", asked first.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:22:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 7 audit, 2026-10-12 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Twelve fragments; deployment thirty-two; purse 127 marks** at dawn on the 299th (130 less two for the rope, less one for meal at the mill; the rope debt to the Lowmarch ferryman is paid). Force was SEEN on the 298th (Teague, at a sunk salt cart: heel to palm in one line, a body's length, the recoil down the same line to the wrist) and **not acquired**; "Don't put it in front of anything that needs doing twice." is Teague's. (2) **The contract** (all Teague's words: "Ten of us on a wall's count. Your six and my four." … "Contract. Not more than that. I'll not have it called more." / "The wall's still the wall."): the ten are Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Vastin; Teague, the tall man with the spear, the bow (a broad man with a bad hip), the young one. **Neither healer is on it.** Shares and costs by the count; **the field is Teague's**; the reading is Karis's ("You'll be asked."). The wall is under a healer's month and is not stood before the month is out. **Teague's four know:** a survey was read at Treswick and gave a bearing; the four ages and "three days past the iron"; that an old man's wall stood in a cut. **They do NOT know** the mechanism, any fragment, the leaf or the list, the date, or who Vastin was. The tall man, the bow and the older healer (a lean old woman with a staff and a board) have not yet spoken to the six. Teague has not yet said "Noted". (3) **March order (Teague's):** Seln ahead; the tall man; Teague, with **Cael at his left shoulder a stride back**; Lira; the young one, watching her feet; Karis, the two healers and the mule in the middle; Brom; Vastin a stride behind him; the bow last. Four hand-signs, Lira's: flat hand *stand*; fist *seen*; two fingers *come on*; hand turned over empty *nothing*. (4) **Vastin: day twenty of thirty on the 299th**; Oryn's linen and two laths; stick; **he walks in the file from the ford** (he rode a tail-board on the level from the 295th to the 298th and walked the hills and the cut). He has said "Noted" twice (the grade; the knee) — it is Cael's word and he says so. He is on the contract's count as one of "your six"; he has not asked to join the six and nobody has spoken of it. He does not know the mechanism, the eleventh (his own), the twelfth, the two words or the date; he knows that he is not told and that it is "six people's". (5) **The grade:** three marks — a stroke alone (a box ruled and EMPTY; no first-tier site exists on any sheet); a stroke with one bar (the four places; stake thirty-two; the dead surveyor's book); a stroke with two bars (six sheets of a fifth place). "A mark is a grade … what he's *for* … how *old* the thing is" (Karis). **Ages counted from the office's first sheet for each place: the Fallow 61, the Stair 94, the Hall 138, the place behind the iron 206**; the fifth place has two unread signs for its figure ("older than two hundred and six"). **Oldest-last.** The office's run from the fourth place to the fifth is "three days past the iron, a little less"; its compass point and its figure in lengths have not been said aloud. The fourth line of the leaf's list: the mark, over *those who are kindled* and *what is set*, level; *three*. Karis has said none of the list's numbers aloud and five of its nine lines are unturned. **Nothing joins this to lamps, sigils, plates, Arbiters or stations**; "four hundred years" stood once, in Cael's log of the 298th, as his own inference — in this movement it may stand only where this packet's plan fixes it. (6) **Hesk's dividers** have been opened twice, by Karis, on Cael's loan; Cael has never opened them. The hide has a clean sheet pinned to its eastern edge with a prick at the divider's point and the pencil line ruled through it and a hand's breadth past. Stake thirty-two is in the tarred case, never driven. (7) **Oryn** knows the two self-readings, the eleventh and the twelfth; her ruling was "not on my plank". **Her finding** ("There's a place in you I can't read because it isn't *flow* …") is known to Cael and Lira. **Cael's own — the twelfth turned inward unbidden under her hands: *still*, then *set* — is told to NO ONE**, and the next word was not let come; Lira knows only that something unasked came and is waiting; the log holds four reasons and the ruling *hold*. Oryn has not heard the leaf ("Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table."). Cleon's warning has "begun to lean". She walks east in the middle of the file with the mule, on nobody's count: three holds owed on her round; "I'm a stop on my own route." (8) **Bodies at dawn on the 299th:** Brom's left shoulder mended, the right re-tied, both arms to shoulder height; Lira's arm released ("It's an arm."); Karis's stitches out, linen on, "Write. Don't lean."; Teague's right wrist in linen under the leather. (9) **Watchers:** a horseman a mile behind on the 296th and a riderless horse in the western alders on the 297th; nothing seen east of the river; no face, name or base. (10) **Seln's case is "shut"** — never write "unopened" or "locked … unopened" (this packet's cutaway note says so and is overridden here); on his chest; contents unnamed; no count of years printed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:29:  - From `BOOK_MAP.md`: §1 Ending; §2 items 36–40; §3 A (the pass), C (burial; pacing); §5 (the Seln, Oryn and Vastin cutaways); §7.1 (the Force first use; Rune inward; the still place; the instruments; the Arbiter); §8 (the pass); §9; §10 Tier A 19–22 and the S21–S24 Tier C lines, including the closing prose; **§11**; §12 C3, C11; §13; §15.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:34:It is first light on the 306th, at the shale camp below the notch. Seln comes back wet to the ankle from the pass's floor. Twelve and a mule. Vastin is on day 27. The ribs have been quiet since the marsh, and the thirteenth is listening.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:42:  - Seln's reconnaissance. "It's through." Cael draws it and tells the doctrine to Teague's four, once: "Behind it. Noted?" / "Noted." The young one nods with his whole head.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:46:  - The broad man is hit at the slant's high edge. **The young one goes out a stride to drag him and is killed by the sixth volley.** Oryn's hands are on him, and come off with nothing done. Vastin cannot move. The broad man says the name, once. [OWNER-pending #54]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:50:- **Burial and the plain's edge (306th).** Teague's crew builds the cairn in their own order. The six carry at his leave. Lira and Seln recover the mule by the ridge path. **Eleven.** Oryn: "Ribs. May I?" / "Yes." **"That's a line. That's not yours." / "It's mine now."** No term tonight.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:51:- **The still place, read as made (~3,000).** He recalls the warning by heart. Then **the twelfth turned inward on purpose**: still; set; *bones*; *a floor with nothing built on it*; *an instruction with no language*. "The same kind of thing, to that instrument, as the sites were to Cleon's." He tells no one, not Lira, not Oryn, not Karis. The Arbiter is unchanged. **The instruments read wronger**: the cord a stride short, the edges a hair and a half to two out. The trend is up and he draws no line. **The log, verbatim** ("the whole year"). [OWNER-pending #58]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:53:- **At the line (dusk).** Every sigil goes dark at the same stride. Lira: "Right." Brom prices the stump. Karis: "It's the first one." Seln gives the count. Vastin: "This is where they drew it." Oryn steps in one stride and back: "Nothing. Everything, round it. Same as you." It goes unanswered. Teague steps in one stride and back: "Field's mine. This isn't field." The turning begins. **The fixed exchange, then "Wait here."**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:55:- **The line again.** Oryn: "May I?" / "Yes." "The same finding." Lira: "Well?" / "I'll tell you on the road. If there's road." He tells nobody what the centre felt like and gives them the count instead. "Twenty-nine tomorrow." / "Thirty's the month."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:56:- **The ledger, the letter and the dawn (307th night–308th), verbatim.** Teague: "After the next thaw … My crew comes." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] Oryn: "The day I have to." … "After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] "Six. Six and no mule." Vastin is unadmitted. "West." **Closing prose, verbatim.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:59:**Cutaways (~5,800):** Seln, ~1,800, on the ridge with Lira to recover the mule: the swept scree below, the dead pine. Oryn, ~2,000, the night after the first death under her hands. **She has not heard the leaf. No cutaway at the court.** Vastin, ~2,000, at the court's rim at night: the line he never asked about. **He is unadmitted and not asking. There is no hint of Book 9's request.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:60:**Development:** about 15 Cael beats. Supporting: Teague 2, Oryn 2, Lira 2, Vastin 2, Karis 1–2, Seln 1–2, Brom 1.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:69:- Vastin does not ask and is not asked; there is no vote. Oryn has not heard the leaf. Cael is nineteen.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:70:- Count Oryn's days past her road from the cairn (§12 C3). The letter's "Tell Lira's family I said so" stays verbatim (§12 C11). [OWNER-pending #55]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:78:West, six and no mule. Three holds still owe a healer a visit. A captain walks home past a cairn. A marshal with a stick has stood at the line where they drew it and has not asked. Thirteen fragments. A still place read by two instruments and understood by neither. A third sentence waits past *exclude* and *prevent* that he is not ready to write. Book 9 begins with that sentence.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:10:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 1 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Teague's spear is a tall MAN** (he / him): the locked Book 7 wrote him so (ch25, ch51, ch52), and Book 8 follows its own edition (OWNER-pending #59). Where the plan says "the tall woman", read "the tall man"; his silence toward the six until his question at the pass stands. (2) **Teague can read** (locked Book 7 ch25: he read a slip twice). Never write that he cannot; if he does not read a sheet it is because it is not in front of him or he has no need. (3) **Lira's asking:** she asked Oryn once about the ankle on the mountain in Book 7 and asked nobody for anything from then until Thornwater; do not call Thornwater her first ask since Norhold. (4) **The stroke and bar** is on stake thirty-two (the Stair's newer stake and the kit's unused one) and on the fourth site's thirty-four ONLY; stakes thirty-one and thirty-three do not carry it. Later records may show the grade on survey SHEETS; the field stakes do not all carry it. (5) **The cord:** the kit's cord is twenty strides, knotted at the fives (four knots to a length); Book 7's Ring was sixty-two cords and twenty strides round. The court is about 1,107 yards across, which is about FIFTY cords, not 159. Give no yardage for a cord. (6) **"West"** was first said aloud at the six-person table on the 268th (Karis's protected "It's west… Treswick…" speech, printed once in ch6). (7) **Deployment since the Line is twenty-nine** at the end of Movement 1 (two uses of the Iron read in earnest); trials are not counted.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:12:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 2 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Vastin's second paper is "the page": a COPY in his own hand** of one line from an old register ("—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—"). It was never cut from anything and is never called a leaf; "the leaf" is the chamber record of Movement 6 only. (2) **The technician's sheet carries a Compact date (a registry year and a day in it) that is NEVER printed as figures** anywhere in this book; whoever reads it reads a date, and the page does not give its numbers. The office filed that sheet at the end of the second row of the records, and it lies there. (3) **The anomaly column:** on every survey abstract, in every hand, for six years, the entry is the one word *Total* — an entry, not a sum. (4) **The Fallow completion report** carries five strokes for a name and a count of six (locked Book 7), not five written names. (5) **What Vastin has told the six about the layer is four things only:** no key (it cannot be reached); the citation; the suppressed records; the technician's line. He has not defined "classification event" and does not know which event is meant. Nothing on the page says that menders, technicians or any office have tried to open it or know more. (6) **Speakers:** "What follows you," was Lira's; "She's right. Go and lie down, and don't take the stairs fast," was Oryn's. (7) **Deployment since the Line is thirty** at the end of Movement 2 (the Iron read at the landing on the 277th). Purse 118 marks. (8) **Teague's spear** has "he/his" on the page from chapter 7 (OWNER-pending #59 as defaulted). (9) Vastin has shown no Iron Wall, has no stated age, has asked only for a bed, and holds Karis's unsealed receipt. Cael has not touched the page and has not read the sheet's date closely.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:14:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 3 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Deployment since the Line is thirty-two** at the end of Movement 3 (one Ember grain and one Wind burst away, both at the cut on the 279th). Ten fragments; the eleventh has not come; nothing came of standing two feet from Vastin's wall. Purse 138 marks. (2) **Iron Wall has been shown once** (the cut): a plane from a line struck with the stick, wall to wall, rooted — he may not lift a foot — loud to anything that hunts a Path, and it spent him to the floor. **Vastin's RIGHT knee** was bitten there; Oryn shut the holes and bound the joint with laths for a month from the 279th (stick; no kneeling, no running, no wall); he said "I cannot undertake" and has kept it to the letter. Brom's right foot, two toes, ten days from the 279th. (3) **The date:** Cael and Seln each know that the technician's sheet carries the day of Cael's Kindling. Neither has said or written it; neither knows what the other made of it; nobody has interpreted the sequence. No figures are ever printed, no span of years is computed, and there is **no second calendar or offset** (one registry reckoning only). Vastin does no date arithmetic and knows nothing of it. (4) **The records at the spring:** Karis has matched FOUR sign-groups to the hide and has given NO number of places; no fifth place has been described. The same stroke and bar stands in a ruled square on all four matched places' sheets (in the field: stake thirty-two and the fourth site's thirty-fours only). The remark "Behaves as device. Cannot be." is on the Stair's sheet in the fourth row; its hand is NOT identified. The instruments column reads true on every line. (5) **Seln has taught one thing, to Vastin** ("Draft nothing. Just look."). Cleon has been named (by Karis) and nothing more is known of him than her protected lines give. (6) **Oryn** went north from the fork on the 281st with the brown mule, her linen and her crossbow with one bolt; Millrace in three weeks; she owes Cael the reading ("the one thing I'm walking up that road owing"); the station term is written in the log. Her past as told at the fork: a house for the sick in a city inside the Line, the column for the patient's tier, a woman from the river sheds mended off the sheet; she has not been through a gate since. (7) **Loads:** boxes on Brom (good shoulder), Lira (both arms) and Cael; the tarred kit case on Vastin, taken up unasked at the fork-stone; Karis the flat and the hide, with the copied page in oilcloth in her coat. **Cael laid his hand on that page once, on the rise.** Vastin has walked beside Cael since the rise. (8) **Stillhounds:** a den that has learned a road runs to where a declaration ends (Karis's sixth line). The sixty yards of four-strand rope are still owed to the Lowmarch ferryman.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:16:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 4 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Who is where on the 284th:** inside the iron door are Cael, Brom, Lira, Vastin and Karis, with three boxes, the tarred kit case, the flat and the hide; Cleon let them in, counted loads and not people, and shut the door. The unnamed yard clerk is outside; **Seln is above ground, NOT on the card or the count**, watching who comes to the door. Oryn is two gates north with the brown mule. (2) **The count:** Karis is the card's unnamed bearer; Cael, Brom, Lira and Vastin are the four hands, entered by count; the clerk asked nothing and wrote *four*. None of the four restricted names has been written anywhere; the asset-restriction is still pending. Cards are good only for the day written on them and are torn at each gate; Iron passes the second wall and Bronze the third by right, on a certificate that is read out and written. The way to the registry's yard is the load lane under the third wall and a cut of **twenty-two steps in five flights, a stride and a half wide, walled three men high with no door or window**; it never crosses the square. Cael has not set foot on the square or its steps and has not looked at the crown; Lira keeps the same discipline unasked. (3) **Cleon's terms** (given at the cook-house on the 283rd): all the sheets, in their places; they come down to him; no names (his is on the card and is never said aloud by him); **nobody tells him what the sheets are or how old until he has looked**; one lamp goes down with them, his, held where he says; no other carried light and no fire of anybody's. He has seen one drawn sheet and knows there are three places and fifty-two sheets, older than what the Compact found; he has not noticed Cael. **His Path has not been shown.** "Rune Path. Bronze." is all that is known of it, from Seln. (4) **Cael:** ten fragments; deployment thirty-two; the fourth and fifth self-readings were made on the 281st, round the still place and not in, uncounted; Tide feels only what flows and returned nothing ("a cord on a stone… *no length*"); he needs an instrument for what does not move, and owes Oryn the telling at the mill. Lira has read the log. (5) **Vastin and Cael:** Vastin has told him why he declined the second reading (the Ostrand case, causal; and a private relief at never learning what a plate would say); Cael has told him that the place was read twice and returned nothing, and nothing of what reads. Ground, not friendship. Vastin carries three sheets under one seal that he will not show; he has sat three times; his right knee is day five of thirty on the 284th (stick; no kneeling, running or wall) and he caught a slip on the steps with his left hand. Brom's two toes: five days left on the 284th. Lira's arm: day nineteen out of wool; her registry paper unshown; the ladder did not pull. (6) **The inn:** the long loft over the stable, by the yard half-door (the painted door has a book), for a week from the 282nd, pot at dusk, seven bowls; **purse 136 marks**. The outer gate counts feet on a bead-frame and writes no name. (7) **Stone:** the grey bridge, the registry's three lowest courses, the undercroft's end and the iron door's frame are one dark dry-laid stone older than the walls; Karis has seen it and stated no conclusion beyond "the bridge was first". The iron door has no lock or handle outside; the clerk knocks. (8) The sixty yards of four-strand were priced at the rope-walk and are to be bought going out.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:18:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 5 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Eleven fragments; deployment since the Line thirty-two; purse 134 marks** at the end of Movement 5 (the night of the 290th). The eleventh, Iron-Wall-adjacent, came from Vastin in the alley's quiet minute; it did not fill, it *set*; its prompt is *This far?*; it has not been deployed and **Vastin has not been told** (Cael holds that as a debt he cannot yet pay; Lira has read the log). (2) **How acquisition lines are printed in this book:** the protected "Fragment eleven" and "Fragment twelve" units are CAEL'S OWN cataloguing of what he reads — set once, in italics, framed as his plain words; they are NOT printed as a system block and take no FRAGMENT ACQUIRED heading or code fence. (3) **The Deepstacks:** an iron door with a sliding bar inside; twenty-seven steps in three flights of nine; three galleries. Middle gallery about 110 strides, Cleon's sloped desk and fixed lamp at its end, a shelf above it with a jar, a tied bundle ("Paper. Not stone.") and the black oak plank's sacking; the fifty-two sheets on three tables, 11/29/12; the plank stands against the third table. Eastern gallery: the old town's tall tally-books. One CARRIED lamp, Cleon's, held "a hand to the left" (Cael holds it and has begun to put it where the eyes are about to go). The boxes go up at the clerk's bell and come down each morning on a fresh card; the clerk writes *The same* and *four*. (4) **Cleon** knows Karis's name (he heard Brom say it and has used it once); his own is on the card and has never been said aloud. He has shown his Path from OUTSIDE only (bear / carried / nothing; "They're orders."; "Same make."; the limit: it does not work on a river, a man or a tree, and costs his eyes for an hour). **His week runs from the 287th to the 293rd.** He has not noticed Cael and knows nothing of the alley or the mechanism. (5) **Karis** has fourteen of twenty-three letters and reads numbers and number-words only; seven kinds bear, twenty-three are carried, eleven are nothing; the bundle is tied and unread; Vastin's copied page is in her coat, unshown to Cleon. Her LEFT palm has seven stitches of Brom's under a strip of his shirt; she writes with the right. (6) **Vastin:** his right knee went again in the alley on the eleventh day of Oryn's thirty (a wall on it against her order, which he heard and asks that she be told); re-splinted with a slat from Brom's box, twice its size; on the night of the 290th he cannot stand or hold a bowl. He gave his name, rank and office aloud at the yard hatch on the 285th; nothing of it was written. He still knows nothing of what Cael carries. (7) **Brom:** the left (good) shoulder wrenched under a dray on the 286th and worse after the alley; he carries his box on the bound right shoulder, a debt entered for the mill's healers; the broker's offer (a guard's post inside the second wall) was answered "I'll think on it." and declined in fact. Lira: day twenty-five out of wool on the 290th; a bruised right shoulder; she drops from heights without the arm. (8) **Seln:** a registry clerk knows his face and voice (the price of a truthful answer at the hatch); he watches from the roof above the cut. His case is **SHUT** — never "unopened" (this edition's Book 6 opened it for the five) — and its contents are named nowhere in this book. He has seen one watcher three times (horseman's boots with the spur-rests cut away). (9) **The faction** (six, hooded, no faces, no Path opened) knows the loft and has shown that it knows; it saw Vastin's wall, a rock, a knife and a boy who stood still, and nothing of quiet ground or the fragments. Cael has ruled that the cut is not climbed at dusk again. The loft is paid to the 295th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:20:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 6 audit, 2026-10-12 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Twelve fragments; deployment since the Line thirty-two.** The twelfth is **Rune-adjacent, from Cleon** ("given, not taken"), acquired at his "There," on the 291st; it gives single words (*goes*, *sits*, *bears*, *nothing*), reads made things only, and costs the eyes afterward. Its lines are Cael's own cataloguing, printed once in italics in Movement 6 and never reprinted. (2) **How it behaves:** it leans at every made thing, unbidden and OUTWARD, and Cael is learning not to look; it has never been used on a person, the crown or the leaf, and **never turned inward**. He refused the inward turn once, deliberately, until Oryn has been asked. **The first inward turn is unbidden, at Millrace, under Oryn's deep reading** (*still*, then *set*); the deliberate inward turn belongs to the plain's edge in Movement 9. (3) **Who knows the twelfth:** Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Cleon. **Not Oryn (owed at the mill, with the readings round the place); not Vastin** (who also still does not know the eleventh or the mechanism). **Cleon's warning** ("If that fragment ever reads something for you that shouldn't be *made* and reads it anyway — …") is known to Cael and Cleon only and is in no book; Cael tells nobody. (4) **The leaf** was read aloud once by Karis and heard by Karis, Cleon, Cael and Vastin; Lira, Brom and Seln read her copy; Oryn has not heard it. **Nobody quotes the leaf's wording again.** The reductions that may be said: *made*; *for a kind*; "the Architect" as a **title** (historical comparison only — "as old as the Architect" — never a present agent); "four hundred years" only where this packet's plan fixes it. (5) **The chronicle's line is marked and nobody speaks of it again**; the hole is never glossed. **Nobody joins the leaf to the lamps, sigils, plates, Arbiters or stations**; no *terminal*, *circuit*, *infrastructure*; no light, plate or instrument is said to attend, notice or want. (6) **Pole two was said aloud at the yard fire and is not in the log.** The line of march from it: "a site at the end of the line that's been quiet since they built the machine" — "I want to stand in the middle of it." (7) **Seln's case is on his chest, shut, contents unnamed; he keeps it "a while longer".** Closed chapter 18 says he has carried it twelve years; print no other count. He will not follow the cut boots again and expects them on the road east. (8) **State at the night of the 293rd:** purse **130**; the reserve sealed in the third box; loft and handcart to the 295th; sixty yards of four-strand still owed to the Lowmarch ferryman; Hesk's dividers and note shut in Hesk's book (never opened on a distance); Karis's fair copy in Cael's coat, the other in her notebook; the skin leaf under Cleon's jar and going to no counter; its back (a list of parts) unread — Cleon's work for the 294th. **Vastin: right knee day fourteen of thirty on the 293rd**, slat-bound, stick, no kneeling, running or Wall; he sleeps in the stable's end stall and rides the handcart. Karis's left palm stitched (Brom's seven); Brom neither arm above the elbow; Lira day twenty-eight out of wool on the 293rd. (9) **Oryn** watched a Kindling at her fourth gate, is two days behind, will not come late to the mill, and means to read Cael "as deep as she went", asked first.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:22:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 7 audit, 2026-10-12 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Twelve fragments; deployment thirty-two; purse 127 marks** at dawn on the 299th (130 less two for the rope, less one for meal at the mill; the rope debt to the Lowmarch ferryman is paid). Force was SEEN on the 298th (Teague, at a sunk salt cart: heel to palm in one line, a body's length, the recoil down the same line to the wrist) and **not acquired**; "Don't put it in front of anything that needs doing twice." is Teague's. (2) **The contract** (all Teague's words: "Ten of us on a wall's count. Your six and my four." … "Contract. Not more than that. I'll not have it called more." / "The wall's still the wall."): the ten are Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Vastin; Teague, the tall man with the spear, the bow (a broad man with a bad hip), the young one. **Neither healer is on it.** Shares and costs by the count; **the field is Teague's**; the reading is Karis's ("You'll be asked."). The wall is under a healer's month and is not stood before the month is out. **Teague's four know:** a survey was read at Treswick and gave a bearing; the four ages and "three days past the iron"; that an old man's wall stood in a cut. **They do NOT know** the mechanism, any fragment, the leaf or the list, the date, or who Vastin was. The tall man, the bow and the older healer (a lean old woman with a staff and a board) have not yet spoken to the six. Teague has not yet said "Noted". (3) **March order (Teague's):** Seln ahead; the tall man; Teague, with **Cael at his left shoulder a stride back**; Lira; the young one, watching her feet; Karis, the two healers and the mule in the middle; Brom; Vastin a stride behind him; the bow last. Four hand-signs, Lira's: flat hand *stand*; fist *seen*; two fingers *come on*; hand turned over empty *nothing*. (4) **Vastin: day twenty of thirty on the 299th**; Oryn's linen and two laths; stick; **he walks in the file from the ford** (he rode a tail-board on the level from the 295th to the 298th and walked the hills and the cut). He has said "Noted" twice (the grade; the knee) — it is Cael's word and he says so. He is on the contract's count as one of "your six"; he has not asked to join the six and nobody has spoken of it. He does not know the mechanism, the eleventh (his own), the twelfth, the two words or the date; he knows that he is not told and that it is "six people's". (5) **The grade:** three marks — a stroke alone (a box ruled and EMPTY; no first-tier site exists on any sheet); a stroke with one bar (the four places; stake thirty-two; the dead surveyor's book); a stroke with two bars (six sheets of a fifth place). "A mark is a grade … what he's *for* … how *old* the thing is" (Karis). **Ages counted from the office's first sheet for each place: the Fallow 61, the Stair 94, the Hall 138, the place behind the iron 206**; the fifth place has two unread signs for its figure ("older than two hundred and six"). **Oldest-last.** The office's run from the fourth place to the fifth is "three days past the iron, a little less"; its compass point and its figure in lengths have not been said aloud. The fourth line of the leaf's list: the mark, over *those who are kindled* and *what is set*, level; *three*. Karis has said none of the list's numbers aloud and five of its nine lines are unturned. **Nothing joins this to lamps, sigils, plates, Arbiters or stations**; "four hundred years" stood once, in Cael's log of the 298th, as his own inference — in this movement it may stand only where this packet's plan fixes it. (6) **Hesk's dividers** have been opened twice, by Karis, on Cael's loan; Cael has never opened them. The hide has a clean sheet pinned to its eastern edge with a prick at the divider's point and the pencil line ruled through it and a hand's breadth past. Stake thirty-two is in the tarred case, never driven. (7) **Oryn** knows the two self-readings, the eleventh and the twelfth; her ruling was "not on my plank". **Her finding** ("There's a place in you I can't read because it isn't *flow* …") is known to Cael and Lira. **Cael's own — the twelfth turned inward unbidden under her hands: *still*, then *set* — is told to NO ONE**, and the next word was not let come; Lira knows only that something unasked came and is waiting; the log holds four reasons and the ruling *hold*. Oryn has not heard the leaf ("Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table."). Cleon's warning has "begun to lean". She walks east in the middle of the file with the mule, on nobody's count: three holds owed on her round; "I'm a stop on my own route." (8) **Bodies at dawn on the 299th:** Brom's left shoulder mended, the right re-tied, both arms to shoulder height; Lira's arm released ("It's an arm."); Karis's stitches out, linen on, "Write. Don't lean."; Teague's right wrist in linen under the leather. (9) **Watchers:** a horseman a mile behind on the 296th and a riderless horse in the western alders on the 297th; nothing seen east of the river; no face, name or base. (10) **Seln's case is "shut"** — never write "unopened" or "locked … unopened" (this packet's cutaway note says so and is overridden here); on his chest; contents unnamed; no count of years printed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:26:> - **Inventory and order:** twelve fragments; deployment thirty-two; Seln ahead, tall spear, Teague with Cael at his left a stride back, Lira, young one, Karis plus both healers and mule in the middle, Brom, Vastin a stride behind, bow last (`chapter-44.md:281–291`; `chapter-46.md:337–341`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:29:> - **Oryn:** knows both self-readings and why, eleven and twelve and their sources/limits, and that Cael had not deliberately turned the twelfth inward; has not heard the leaf or seen the grade; was refused nothing she was owed, but Cael keeps *still/set*, Cleon's warning and the date. She sensed only “one of yours” turn and dismissed it (`chapter-46.md:9–63,171–175,221–227`). Her own finding is known to Cael and Lira because it was spoken before both (`46:193–219`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:30:> - **Cael's two findings:** Oryn's exact finding is held but not copied; *still* then *set* is Cael's alone; the next word was suppressed; the four reasons and “hold” are in the log without the words (`chapter-46.md:197–211,267–289`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:32:> - **Dividers and stake:** Karis has opened Hesk's dividers twice on the office distance, on Cael's leave; Cael has not opened them and they end shut in his book (`chapter-45.md:129–143`; `chapter-46.md:323–335`). Stake thirty-two is back in Vastin's tarred case and has never been driven.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:33:> - **Bodies/counts at dawn 299:** Vastin day 20 of 30, Oryn's linen/two laths, stick; Brom's left shoulder mended, right re-tied, both arms to shoulder height; Lira's arm released; Karis's stitches out, linen on, scar promised, do not lean; Teague's wrist wrapped; Cael's eyes paid in the dark (`chapter-45.md:295–377`; `chapter-46.md:233–239,299–317`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:34:> - **Money/load:** purse 127; reserve sealed in third box; mule carries three boxes, flat, meal sack, Oryn's pannier and canvas; Cael carries fair leaf copy and dividers; Karis has hide/pinned sheet, notebook, Cleon roll, three-box sheet and Vastin copy (`chapter-45.md:283`; `chapter-46.md:303–307,321–335`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:36:> - **Other live threads:** Cleon remains below with skin leaf, chronicle and board; Seln's case stays shut on his chest, contents unnamed; Vastin's debt and ignorance stand; Pike has thirteen lines and a dated season-space with no printed date; rope debt is paid; Oryn's road is her own and will diverge (`chapter-41.md:213`; `chapter-44.md:137–157,205–211`; `chapter-46.md:31–47,337–341`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:49:It is dawn on the 299th, at Millrace ford. There are twelve and a mule. Teague's wrist is wrapped. Vastin is on day 20. Karis is writing with the bound hand. Oryn's road runs east with them for a day and a half and then it does not.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:53:The leg goes on the page as the place where two crews learn each other, and where the young one becomes someone a reader will grieve. Then the fourth site: a watch-post, a barricade, a captain's line, and a width that wins because the people inside the line have stood there before, with nothing gained by it. The thirteenth arrives. The next night every finding goes onto one blanket, the lamps finding is said aloud and filed on its own page, and a marshal finds a crack he does not pry.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:58:  - **The cairn at noon on the 300th:** Oryn looks once, straight, and walks on east.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:62:- **The crest.** The watch-post: hut, fire, kit under a hide, two timbers, seven hoods, two crossbows, one low practitioner. "They knew." Seln: "That iron's been in the ground years. Not one cold term." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] Teague: "Drawn?" Cael draws it. "Nobody declares. Nobody dies. They're seven people on a posting. Noted?" / Teague's **first "Noted."**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:65:  2. **Teague goes through the middle.** Cael is at his left, a stride back, the whole exchange. **The thirteenth.** The notice renders verbatim. The recoil goes to the wrist, then the elbow: "Through."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:69:  **Win sentence, verbatim.** Oryn sets and knits the leg and is grey for a quarter-hour. The healers nod. Teague's arm: "That's a fact about a line." / "Noted" / "Everybody says that now." Brom's week of colours.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:70:- **The Span itself (noon).** An arch on two piers over the sink. Carvings on the piers' inner faces, copied. No steps: the arch is walked as a road rises. The bearing runs "Through". **Nothing happens on the crown.** The thirteenth listens and the ribs know the cost. **The log, verbatim.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:72:  - **The lamps finding, verbatim.** Vastin: "If a man designed the apparatus, then the sigils —" / the ruler rule. Two pages. Vastin's third "Noted." **Cael does not add his own third page.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:75:  - **Force, dry:** Cael lines his frame on the shale without firing. The thirteenth listens and the ribs warn him.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:80:**Development:** about 15 Cael beats. Supporting: Teague 2, the young one 2, Karis 2, Vastin 2, Seln 1–2, Oryn 2, Brom 1, Lira 1.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:88:- The cairn is on the 300th. Count Oryn's days from it (§12 C3). No cutaway at the court.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:21:- **When/where:** Lowmarch, the hundred and thirty-first morning, after the Book 7 hearth scene at the lower inn. The first snow fell on day 129; the last ferry crossed and its lines were taken in on day 130; Oryn's letter arrived through a hand's depth of snow on day 131. Book 8 continues later that morning. The Book 8 count remains day 131 to day 308. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:22:- **Cael:** nineteen. **There is no birthday in this book.** His own Arbiter woke at Kindling, its plate lit eleven seconds late, the failed-safe word replaced the old name, and it went dark; he has no Path. He has **ten confirmed fragments**: Wind (Lira), Pressure (`the Bronze from Ardenmere` in spoken inventories), Iron (Brom), Compression (Reydan), Ember (Karis), Shadow (Seln; sealed; used exactly twice, at Ring and Stair), Storm (Daeva), Anchor (unnamed; used once each way), Blade (Ephram), and Tide (Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; clinical; *ask first, every time*). Deployment since the Line: **twenty-seven**. **The still place** is not a fragment and is not counted: read three times, told to Oryn and then described to the other four, untouched since Oryn ordered him to write it down and stop touching it. His ribs have been quiet since the morning of day 129. The living purse holds 96 marks. Open accounts are listed below; `nothing owed` is false. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:23:- **The five at Lowmarch:** Lira (Wind, Iron R1 formal) has all eight left-forearm marks whole, but the arm is slung high and holds nothing until Oryn says; the right ankle is taped and unmended. She carries Oryn's crossbow, hook and one bolt and cannot span it herself. Brom (Iron Skin, Copper formal) has the right shoulder mended twice, not a third, held in four yards of webbing by the drover's turn; the older healer says it will do. Karis (Ember, **Iron Rank Three**) has 52 copied sheets (11 Ring / 29 Stair / 12 Hall), the dead surveyor's ledger, the carter's map with four circles and the line off the hide, and the Ternhall straightedge; her voice is whole and her larger hypothesis remains unspoken and unentered. Seln (Shadow, Bronze; fifteen years' service) has his **locked case**, carried shut for twelve years and unopened. Cael has Hesk's brass straightedge and satchel. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:25:- **Letters/animals:** Hesk's brass and note and Oryn's bark have arrived. Letters to Hesk and Vell went west on the last ferry; Ephram's is deferred to the first boat of the thaw. The brown mule is with the five. Oryn has the grey jenny and the thirty-foot three-strand rope. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:26:- **Oryn:** last located at Thornwater, with route work north next. The old debt ran Cael→Oryn and is **PAID**: three self-readings and the full telling. Her withheld answer was never a debt. Her exact letter is: `Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks. After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say. — O.` Lira's arm waits on Oryn's in-person word. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:27:- **Teague's crew:** stays through the cold term at Lowmarch's upper inn: four practitioners plus the older healer of no Path, all unnamed except Teague. His exact term is: `After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes.` / `Noted.` He has the cold road; the five have the axe-head fence. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:30:- **Who knows the integration mechanism:** Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Oryn — six. Oryn knows sources by Path and not by person except those she has touched; she does not know Seln supplied Shadow-adjacent. **Not** Vastin, Teague, Pike or Cleon. All six know the still-place phenomenon; only Cael and Oryn are shown hearing/saying its label. Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln know the fourth-site survey; Oryn, Teague and Pike do not know that result at entry. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:34:- **Cael:** nineteen, with **thirteen confirmed fragments**. Iron Wall came from Vastin in the Treswick alley (entered, **not told**; the debt stands; deployment none). Rune came from Cleon in the chamber (told to Cleon; the warning stands). Force came from Teague at the Span's barricade (first and only use on stone at the pass; the recoil stops in the ribs; never used on a person). **The still place** has been read by two instruments and understood by neither. Tide reads nothing, with everything going round it. Rune reads a shape with bones, a floor with nothing built on it. At the court's centre there was **no edge**: "Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. The same kind of made." **He told no one the Rune finding.** His Arbiter is dark and unchanged. The instruments read wrong in his hands and only his, with the **trend up** (a hair at Lowmarch; a stride short and "a hair and a half, two" at the plain's edge). That fact is unsourced. 123 marks; nothing owed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:35:- **The reveal is delivered once, in the record's voice:** the leaf in the Deepstacks. "The Architect" is the record's title; the name is scraped away; it was about four hundred years ago; the purpose was "that the un-bound should not come again". The chronicle's "went into the ordering he had made, and is in it —" is **marked, not read**.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:39:- **Vastin** is on the stick until the thirtieth day of Oryn's treatment month [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] ("Thirty's the month"). He walks with the five **unadmitted**. He has not asked to join and nobody has asked him.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:40:- **Oryn** turns north on her mule at dawn ("The day I have to." / "After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]). She has **not heard the leaf**. She still owes three holds.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:55:3. **KEEP — The river is a road (161st); the kit on the table.** The cord is knotted at the fives, the stake is number thirty-two, plus the mallet and the field ledger with the radius line. The Stair's designation sits in an unreadable index above the stopped line "third site confirmed on bearing". Karis learns the kit.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:58:6. **KEEP — Thornwater (265th–266th).** The ford in thaw. Oryn's yard. Lira's arm is released ("Five months and twenty days." [OWNER-pending #56] / "That's a season. Take it off."). Lira asks, for the first time since Norhold: "Will you mend it." / "Lie still". The ankle is mended. "Thank you." / "Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks." The map on Thornwater's table: "That's a line." Cael tells her about the cord: "I don't know what that is. Neither do you. Write that down too." Oryn comes down because Lowmarch and Millrace are her first stops after the thaw [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6]. Nobody asked her.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:59:7. **KEEP — Six at Lowmarch (268th).** 118 marks (the mule's shed and the rope-house roof). Karis makes her case to six: the carvings are instructions; the index; west; **Treswick and the Deepstacks named**; the scholars' provision; "a man there who is". Oryn's reservation about the station goes unsaid. **KEEP — the closing log (270th)**, verbatim (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:61:9. **KEEP — The long table (277th midday).** The Seln–Vastin doorway exchange, their first words ever. The short thing: resigned or walked. Brom: "Three hundred miles is a demonstration." The layer: Karis supplies its existence; Vastin's new fact is "Cannot. There is no key." The name is a citation to a designer, and the trail dead-ends at Treswick. Vastin has nothing to do afterwards. "Why us." Oryn on the knee: "Then I still haven't asked." "What follows you": nothing that can cross the Line. Cael remembers the Book 6 sentence and says only: "Ask him the thing you want to ask him." Karis asks; Vastin's close (§10). The ferry goes west.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:64:12. **KEEP — The cut (279th).** Iron Wall is first shown: a plane across the road, rooted, and therefore loud. Brom fights silent with a rock. Lira works the scree. Cael bursts away, then goes still on the scree; the pack turns back and breaks on the wall. The heap. Seln in the heap. Five dead and three into the sink. Costs: Brom's foot; **Vastin's knee**, bound by Oryn for "a month". The lesson: "The wall held the line. And someone else had to be the reason they wanted the line." / "You do now." The log (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:66:14. **KEEP — The fork-stone (280th evening–281st first light).** Oryn's terms: "I'm not an archive person"; the city she left; "Leaving and routing are different verbs." "Three weeks" (Seln). **The promise** is written in the log and read back. She prices everyone. The Millrace rendezvous. "Bring me whatever walks out of that archive with you. All of it." "Not the steps. Not the square." The mule goes north with her. Cael turns at a quarter-mile. Treswick comes into view from the rise; the light on the crown is not looked at.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:74:22. **KEEP — The alley (290th, dusk).** Six faceless attackers: four above with a crossbow, two below with staves, one of the four a signaller on the landing. Vastin roots the cut wall to wall ("there is no round"). Nobody declares. Brom with a rock, Lira's drop, Cael still at the plane's foot ("the reason"), Seln's weighted cord from the roof. The cache was on the roof the whole time. They leave; none taken, no faces. Costs: Karis's left hand (a step's edge), bound by Brom with thread and teeth because no healer inside the gate would touch it; Vastin spent, the knee again. **The Iron-Wall notice** (§10). "I put the wall in front of it anyway. I'd like that entered" / "It's entered." Not told. The log (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:76:24. **KEEP — Dividers (292nd).** Hesk's parcel and note. The meal: four marks, two cups kept for Karis and Oryn, Seln's slip read and burned ("Closed"); 130 marks. Vastin and the cups: "Out here you count who's owed a seat." The first inventory written inside walls (§12 C10). **The station's light is "not steady" for a count of one**: a pressure, "an instrument turning toward him". It becomes the fourth entry on the page. He does not cross; the promise holds at its first cost.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:82:30. **KEEP — The grade cracked (298th morning).** Three marks. Cleon's list puts the mark at the kindling and the mark on a sheet in one line: "A mark is a grade." Ages by first sheet: 61, 94, 138, 206. The third-tier point lies past the fourth, on the line. **Oldest-last.** "It's observation." **Vastin's first "Noted."** Teague: "Oldest last." / "Then that's where we're going." The log (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:83:31. **KEEP — Millrace (298th evening–299th dawn).** "Eleven off the ridge." / "I know." The two healers look at each other and then at Brom's shoulder. Vastin is ordered to stand ("Nineteen days." / "Then it's eleven more.") and takes the order without walking it back. Oryn's terms restated. "Sixth chair." / "On my terms. Which are the only kind." **She asks each patient first ("May I?").** The readings: shoulder, arm ("Once is once more than I priced"), Karis's hand ("Who sewed this."), the knee ("It held in a cut"; "Noted" / "That's new." / "It's a useful word." / "It's his."). **The deep reading**, with consent. **Rune turns inward unbidden: *still*, then *set*.** Withheld. Oryn's finding (§10). The leaf is offered: "Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table." Twelve and a mule at dawn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:84:32. **KEEP — The leg (299th–303rd)**, five dated entries: the Stair's bowl (299th); Oryn's road turning north at a cairn at noon on the 300th, where she walks on east; the Hall's marsh (300th); two camps with no water (301st–302nd); the crest (303rd). "Known" is entered under each.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:85:33. **KEEP — The crest (303rd).** The watch-post: a hut, a fire, kit under a hide, a two-timber barricade, seven hoods, two crossbows, one low practitioner. "They knew." "That iron's been in the ground years. Not one cold term." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] Teague: "Drawn?" "Nobody declares. Nobody dies … Noted?" / Teague's first **"Noted."**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:86:34. **KEEP — The Span (304th).** First exchange: the watch's declaration is unanswered; Brom takes bolts on Iron. Teague goes through the middle (the barricade a body's length back) → **Force acquired** at a stride. Recoil: wrist, then elbow. The watch reforms. **Width:** "Nothing was gained inside" is entered first. "By count": five over stake thirty-four (Cael, Lira, Karis, the young one, Vastin), four on the shelf. They walk to the pinch. Eleven seconds. "You'll die in there." / "We've been in three times." The watch goes east, unpursued. The win sentence (§10). The broad man goes over the sink's edge in the fourth second; Teague does not turn. Oryn sets and knits the leg and is grey for a quarter-hour. The healers' nod. Teague's arm: "That's a fact about a line." / "Noted" / "Everybody says that now." Brom's bill. **The Span** at noon: an arch on two piers over the sink, carvings on the piers' inner faces, the bearing "Through". Nothing happens on the crown. The thirteenth listens. The log (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:88:36. **KEEP — The pass (306th).** Seln's reconnaissance (the shelf, the rig, nine or more, three crossbows). "It's through." The doctrine is told to Teague's four; **the young one's whole-head nod**. **The tall man [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: M1 audit; OWNER-pending #59] speaks to the six for the first time.** [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] The wall is set as a lean-to slant. Brom's forearm is bolted before the wall goes up. The pine and stack fall down the plane and close the mouth behind them. The scree is swept clean. Seln climbs. The broad man is hit at the slant's high edge; the young one drags him and is **killed by the sixth volley**, a stride outside the plane. Oryn's hands on him: the first time they come off with nothing done. The name is said once. [OWNER-pending #54] Seln goes over the lip at the seventh volley. **Cael's first use of Force** on the second stack's brace (stone, along the shelf); the recoil stops in the ribs. Teague takes the stair left-handed. The tall man [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: M1 audit; OWNER-pending #59] reverses her spear. The team breaks east along the ridge, none taken. Vastin goes down; Karis sits with her hand on his shoulder. Teague kneels. "A wall keeps everyone behind it, and one of mine wasn't." At the far mouth Cael understands the line was not drawn in ink.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:89:37. **KEEP — The plain's edge (306th).** The burial at the east mouth by Teague's crew, with the six carrying at his leave. Lira and Seln recover the mule by the ridge path. **Eleven.** Oryn on the ribs: "Ribs. May I?" / "Yes." "That's a line. That's not yours." / "It's mine now." No term tonight. **Rune turned inward deliberately:** bones; a floor with nothing built on it; an instruction with no language; "the same kind of thing, to that instrument, as the sites were to Cleon's." Told to no one. The Arbiter unchanged. The instruments read wronger; the trend is up. The log (§10, "the whole year"). [OWNER-pending #58]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:90:38. **KEEP — The court (307th).** It lies low, and the plain is worn down to it. about 1,107 yards across (about fifty cords of the kit's twenty-stride cord) [M1 audit: 159 cords would be about 3,500 yards at Book 7's scale] [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6]. The stratum under everything. The first cut ("The others are copies"). The bearing ends, with no sixth. The council. **At the line:** every sigil dark at the same stride; the reactions: Lira's "Right."; Brom pricing the stump; Karis's "It's the first one."; Seln's count; Vastin's line (§10). Oryn steps in one stride: "Nothing. Everything, round it. Same as you." It is unanswered. Teague steps in one stride and steps back: "My crew's stood at four of these. It's stood at enough … Field's mine. This isn't field." The turning begins. Lira's fixed exchange. "Wait here."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:91:39. **KEEP — The centre (307th dusk).** 506 strides. Rune turned on the floor at a hundred strides gives the same reading. The eyes are paid. **No edge, no seam.** "Not the Quiet." "Not a fragment." "The same kind of made." He fit. It was not an accident. The third sentence goes unsaid. Oryn reads him at the line ("May I?"): "The same finding." Lira: "Well?" / "I'll tell you on the road. If there's road." He told nobody. The count. "Twenty-nine tomorrow." / "Thirty's the month."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:92:40. **KEEP — The ledger, the letter, and the dawn (307th night–308th).** Teague goes west carrying the letter; Oryn goes north; "Six. Six and no mule."; Vastin is unadmitted; "West." The closing prose (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:119:1. **Cael's working inventory during the cold term** [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] (≈6,000; first third). Through private practice in the ferryman's shed and the frozen meadow, the reader learns all ten fragments as costs and limits. Wind's burst and its locked landing beat. Pressure's narrow channel. The Iron read as "the workhorse". Compression's frame. Ember, one point at a time, with its burn (used at the Ring and the Stair in Book 7). [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator ruling] Shadow's idle draw and the seal's logic. Storm, its lanes and their bills (ten / ten / twelve) [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator ruling]. Anchor used both ways. Blade, short and sharp. Tide "ask first"; he has read himself three times and Oryn twice, each outward use after an ask and explicit yes. **Invent no new numeric ceilings. Preserve every numeric ceiling and bill fixed by canon.** [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 7]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:124:6. **Force, dry** (≈2,000). On the shale step (305th) he lines his frame without firing. The thirteenth "listens" and the ribs warn him. The first actual use comes at the pass.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:130:- **The week before the ferry (270th–276th)** (≈4,000). Tents return to the meadow. Teague's crew prepares for the road after the thaw. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] Oryn's first Lowmarch stop: patients at the plank, seen from the outside.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:134:- **The leg (299th–303rd)** (≈9,000). The Stair's bowl rim, where Karis checks a number for an hour. The cairn: Oryn chooses east. The Hall's marsh, where Cael read himself twice earlier at the Hall. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] Two dry camps. Two crews learning each other. The crest at dusk.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:142:| **Lira** | To find out what she is without a ladder | Asks Oryn to mend the ankle (her first ask since Norhold). Fights on through the arm's first warning (M2), then listens at the second. Keeps her registry paper in her coat and goes up as a hand. Looks at the whole ladder and it does not pull. Holds her question at the court ("Well?") and accepts "on the road". | 12 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:146:| **Oryn** | The route; to be nobody's recruit | Releases the arm only when Lira lifts the sling herself. Comes to Lowmarch unasked. Sets the station term in the log. Routes north. Rejoins as a stop. Asks every time. Walks on east at the cairn. Will not hear the leaf at her table. Turns north "the day I have to". | 11 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:147:| **Vastin** | To dig one thing up before he's done; to learn to navigate without authority | Walks three hundred miles alone. Carries the case unasked. Consents to be counted as a hand. Holds the wall with nothing behind it. Asks for the wall to be entered. Does not name the seals. Takes Oryn's order. Does not ask to join. | 14 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:157:The shale-back fence, the ice road, the silent yard, Lira's return to the floor, the ferry landing, the tail in Treswick, and the water at the seep (see A). Also Oryn's north circuit (cutaways only): Oxhollow's gate, a man with a wrist set wrong, a birth, and **a hold child's Kindling**, where Oryn watches a fourteen-year-old see a sigil nobody else can see. No patient dies under her hands (§13).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:161:Each person keeps their own comic habit. Brom says "It's a boot" and gives one-word essays ("They shoe by the tier"). Pike speaks ledger. Oryn: "Everybody says that now" and "I'm going to have to find another word". Lira finds an essay in a single word. "Noted" spreads through the cast like a borrowed tool, in the sequence locked in §13. Running jokes: the mule's empty chair; the mule as the only one of twelve who never knows what happened; the ferryman watching people use his river; Vastin's good manners from a man "served all his life and never once fed". When pain is in the room, humour stops performing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:171:| 3 | The Border Road | 13–19 | 34,000 | S4, S5, S6 | First fight and first wall; the records read three ways; the sum Cael does not write; Oryn routes north with the promise in the log. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:176:| 8 | The Sunken Span | 47–53 | 35,000 | S19, S20 (+the leg) | The leg on the page; the watch, the width and the thirteenth; the lamps finding and the crack. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:196:| **Oryn** | ≈7,000 (3) | M4: the north circuit (Oxhollow's gate; the wrist; a birth). M6: a hold child's Kindling witnessed from outside. M9: the night after the first death. | Her readings; the still place as "nothing, everything round it"; twelve then thirteen currents; the mechanism (her Tide was taken at her direction). | **The leaf** (she has not heard it). The Rune finding. Any patient dying under her hands before the pass. An explanation of "Same as you". No cutaway at the court itself. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:220:| 279 | The cut; **Vastin's knee (Oryn's month: day 1 = 280)**; 138 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:222:| 281 | Oryn north at first light; the rise; the last post (reading inward; confession) |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:240:| 300 | Cairn at noon (Oryn walks on); the Hall's marsh |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:249:Running counts that must reconcile: **Lira's arm** "fifteen days" at 280, "twenty-five" at 290, "twenty-seven" at 292 and "thirty-three" at 298 (counting the 266th as day 1). **Karis's hand** is eight days old on the 298th. **Cash:** 96 → 76 → 116 → 118 → 138 → 136 → 130 → 127 → 123. **Oryn's route:** count "days past the end of her road" from the cairn on the 300th (§12 C3).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:266:| **Tide (the tenth)** | Reading inward (M4): "a cord on a stone". Oryn's deep reading (M7). Her post-centre reading (M9) | "Ask first, every time"; Oryn's consent ritual at every reading (S18 montage, Cael at S18, S22, S24) | Same finding, certain |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:270:| **Oryn's Tide** | Thornwater; Millrace; the Span (a quarter-hour grey); the pass | Reserve at roughly the rate of damage; nothing inside the line; she cannot heal the dead | The first death is under her hands |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:277:- The cold-term inventory and practice [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] (fragment names, costs, the seal, "deployment notes").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:323:- **The cut (M3).** A hundred strides of road cut to a cart's width, with scree on both sides and a frozen runnel a stride wide down the middle. A sink lies fifty-five yards below [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] on the north side, iced and in shadow; there are eight hounds. Positions: Brom on stone at the south edge with a rock; Vastin a stride behind him; Lira on the south scree; Seln on the north scree, unseen; Cael twenty strides west, past the sink; Karis, Oryn and the mule at the east end. The decisions: the wall goes up and everything turns to the loudest thing; Brom and Lira work its south end silently; Cael bursts **away**, then goes still on the scree as the lock beat lands; the pack returns to the wall and breaks on it; the heap; the runnel. The opponent learns too: the den has learned the road. Costs to carry: Brom's foot; Vastin's knee (a month); Cael's burst bill.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:338:- **Two pages, no line.** The leaf and the lamps finding are never joined: not in dialogue, not in any interior (including cutaways), not in the narration. Vastin's sentence stops twice (in the chamber; on the shale). The words *terminal*, *circuit* and *infrastructure* are never used for Arbiters.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:370:21. **The court (S23–24):** Vastin: "I stood at a line for forty years," Vastin said, "and told people which side of it they were. I never once asked who drew it." … "This is where they drew it." / Karis: "It's the first one." / Lira: "Right." / Oryn: "Nothing," … "Everything, round it." … "Same as you." / Teague: "My crew's stood at four of these. It's stood at enough." … "Field's mine. This isn't field." / at the centre: "Not the Quiet." "Not a fragment." "The same kind of made."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:371:22. **Departures (S24):** Teague: "The thaw's past," / "Noted," / "After the next thaw." … "Whatever's on the next line. My crew comes." / Oryn: "The day I have to." / "Noted," / "Everybody says that." … "They'll carry. They'll hurt," … "After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say." / Seln: "Six. Six and no mule. Nothing behind. Nothing beside." / "West," Cael said. / "West," said Brom, and picked up the box. / "Twenty-nine tomorrow," / "Thirty's the month," [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:374:25. **Oryn at Millrace (S18):** "There's a place in you I can't read because it isn't *flow*. I've spent my life reading flow. Whatever that is, it's not the kind of thing my Path was built for." / "Then it's not mine." … "Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table." … "Lie still when I say. That's still the term." / "Sixth chair." / "On my terms. Which are the only kind."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:382:- Oryn (B7 edition `chapter-58.md:51–55`; `chapter-60.md:215,229`): `Find me at Thornwater.` / `Bring the map.` Her letter: `Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks. After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say. — O.` / `Six, by letter.` [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:384:- Teague and Pike (B7 edition `chapter-59.md:199,221–225`): `After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes.` / `Noted.` / `I've kept this ledger thirty years. First time it's been wrong about a crew by being too small.` [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:386:- The still-place inventory (B7 edition `chapter-60.md:39`): `One anomaly. Session nine. Tide-adjacent. Not an entry any more; a location. The still place. Read three times. Doesn't flow. Doesn't change. Everything goes around it. Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. Older than the log. Observation continues.` Oryn's order (B7 edition `chapter-55.md:289`): `Write it down and stop touching it.` The Tide rule (B7 edition `chapter-60.md:37`): `ask first, every time`. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 8]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:395:- **S5:** "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell." … "Draft nothing. Just look." / "Two copies of one ignorance." Close: "Six years," Karis said. "They measured all of it. They graded it — the sites are ranked by something, and it's the same something in the kit, and I can't read either one." … "Everything I can't read points at the same place." / "Treswick," / "The archive under it. Cleon." / "Who's Cleon?" / "The only historical-Path practitioner registered west of the Line. If the language is anywhere, it's under his hands. A day and a half." … "And then I find out whether I've been right for five years or wrong for five years, and I don't know which I'm more afraid of." [OWNER-pending #52]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:396:- **S6:** "I'm not an archive person." / "Leaving and routing are different verbs. I'm doing the second." / "You go inside, you don't go near the station. Not the steps, not the square. You promise me in that log of yours, because I've seen what the log does to you." / the log entry: "The fork. Oryn north; five holds; routing, not the other verb. Her term, given at the fire, taken in the log because that's the form she'll take it in: inside Treswick I do not go near the station. Not the steps. Not the square. Written here so she can read it, and so I can." / "Bring me whatever walks out of that archive with you. All of it." / "Not the steps," … "Not the square."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:405:- **S17 log:** "Karis cracked the grade. The sites are ranked by age and the bearing runs oldest-last — somebody laid them out in order, and the order runs into the deep edge, toward the first one they ever made. Second-tier's the fourth site, the one the Compact fenced. Third-tier's out past it, on the line, quiet for centuries. Teague's crew came after the thaw like he said — ten of us now, and he's still better at this than I am, and the ledger still says so. Two crews, one bearing, and a straightedge my guardian sent me because my grandmother said a man who catalogues everything eventually needs to draw a line through it. Turns out she was right about the line. Turns out the line was already drawn four hundred years ago. We're just the first to follow it to the end." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] Also: "Two words," … "Both of them ours." / "Noted."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:406:- **S19:** "Nobody declares. Nobody dies. They're seven people on a posting. Noted?" / "Noted," / "You'll die in there." / "We've been in three times," / win sentence: "The crews had removed the watch's ability to hold the approach by making the only safe retreat a line the watch would not cross and the crews would." / Teague's arm: "A third time on that arm and I'll set it in a splint. That's not a healer's opinion. That's a fact about a line." / "Noted," / "Everybody says that now," Log body: "Twelfth—no, count it again—thirteenth. Wind, Pressure, Iron, Compression, Ember, Shadow, Storm, Anchor, Blade, Tide, Iron Wall, Rune, Force. Thirteen things that aren't a Path, and I got three of them in one city and one bridge. Rate's climbing and I'm writing that down because Hesk taught me to note the trend. The Span's the fourth site and the Compact fenced it, years ago by the scale on the iron, and left men on it. They knew. They've always known. The bearing runs through it and keeps going, oldest-last, and the oldest one's out there in the deep edge, quiet since they built the machine. One more site. I've wanted to stand in the middle of it since Karis said *someone made this.* Tomorrow I find out what standing in the middle of the first one feels like."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:407:- **S20 close:** "It's here," Karis said. "Third-tier, documented four hundred years back — as old as the record, as old as the Architect, as old as the machine. The first one they made, or near it." / "And it's on the line." / "It's the *end* of the line. Oldest-last. Everything before it was practice, or maintenance, or — I don't have the word. This is the one that's been quiet since before quiet had a name." … "You still want to stand in the middle of it." / "More than I've wanted anything since I was fourteen." / "Why." / "Because every other site, my Path worked while everyone's died. I want to know what the *oldest* one does to me. I think it's going to tell me something the records can't." [OWNER-pending #57] / He was right. He did not yet know how right.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:412:- **Closing prose (S24):** "He had spent the whole year learning that the world was built to prevent him — four hundred years of tiers and registries and a machine that lit for everyone but him, all of it laid down so that what he was would never come again. And at the center of the first place they ever made, the oldest silence on the continent, the one built before there was a word for it, he had felt no exclusion and no prevention and no wall. He had felt at home. He did not have a word for that yet. But he knew, now, walking back out across a floor older than the system that had expelled him, that it was not an accident — that the place built to end him was the one place he fit — and that the difference between *the system was built to exclude me* and *the system was built to prevent me* had a third sentence past it, waiting, that he was not ready to write. Someone had made the pattern. He was, he was beginning to understand, the pattern. That was as far as he could say." [OWNER-pending #57] [OWNER-pending #58]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:440:- **C3 — Oryn's days past her road.** S20 has "two days past the end of the road that had been hers" (305th) and S23 "three days past" (307th). The cairn where her road turns north is on the 300th, which makes them five and seven days. **Edition: count from the cairn**, or drop the number.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:451:- **C14 — Calendar of the leg.** STATE_RUNNING's first Ch19 note put the cairn on the 301st; the closed prose puts it on the 300th, with the crest on the 303rd. **Edition follows the prose** (§6).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:460:- **Cael lies still for no one but Oryn,** and she has read him three times (sack, table, marsh's edge) until Millrace. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator ruling — in the edition's Book 7 Oryn's hands were on Cael for several surface reads that found nothing (the mountain; the ford at Oxhollow; the stake), for the long reading on the 100th (the table), and at the Hall on the 120th (the marsh's edge); Cael has read Oryn twice, each time after asking and an explicit yes.] **Oryn does not read Cael** before Millrace's deep reading; she reads his ribs' surface at most.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:466:- **"Noted" adoption:** Vastin's first is the 298th (the grade); Teague's first is the 303rd (the crest); Oryn's "Everybody says that now" comes on the 304th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:469:- **Oryn's hands** never come off a person with nothing done before the young one (no deaths on her north circuit).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:470:- **The mule** goes north with Oryn on the 281st and returns at Millrace on the 298th. From the fork to Millrace the boxes are carried on backs (ruling 16).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:482:**Names pending owner approval: none required.** Every new figure the expansion needs is carried by role: the axe-head hold's factor, the carter at the ice road, the ferryman and his boy, Oryn's route patients (at Oxhollow and unnamed holds), the hold child at the Kindling, the broker's men, and the hood in the tail. This keeps the audio load low in a book whose cast is already heavy with role-names (Teague's crew must stay unnamed by canon). If the author finds a recurring role that needs a name in the audio, it is listed here for approval before drafting, and drafted under the proposed name per the edition's policy (RUN-LEDGER 18:41).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:484:**Existing names stay exactly as canon has them.** Never "Halcenvane" on the page; use "the academy above Ostrand". The registry collisions are untouched (OWNER-DECISIONS #6). **Audiobook read-through list** (carried): Cleon/Cael (KLEE-on/KAYL; never in one spoken run); Span/Stair; Treswick/Ternhall (keep them out of one spoken inventory); the O-onset stack Oryn/Oxhollow/Ostrand; Pike/Fiske. Places minted by canon only: Treswick, the Deepstacks, the Sunken Span, "the court" (description), the shoulder hold, the cut, the pass. **Do not name new holds** on Oryn's route. Use Oxhollow or Thornwater, or none.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:490:Book 9 opens with: the court's centre (no edge; "the same kind of made"); the Rune finding that nobody else knows; the dark Arbiter; the instruments trending wrong; the crack; Vastin unadmitted (Book 9 stages his formal request and the 3–2 vote, with Seln deciding); Oryn's three future holds and "After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say."; Teague's "After the next thaw" and his grief; Cleon under Treswick; thirteen fragments; the leaf's copies with the gap drawn; the mule with Oryn; Cael remains nineteen at the Book 9 opening. Do not place or calculate his next birthday until the owner rules the series calendar. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] Book 9 owns the tomb in the deepest edge territory, the word "recurrence", the Compact's open fracture (Seln's documents), and the Quieting's first visible spread into a city's outer districts. **Do not pre-pay any of these in Book 8.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:7:## ENTRY — Movement 1, chapter 1 (Lowmarch lower inn; the hundred and thirty-first morning past the Line; after Oryn's letter and the Book 7 closing hearth scene; last ferry and rope-taking were day 130) [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 13]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:13:| Cael | Nineteen; no birthday this book. Ribs quiet since day 129. His Arbiter woke at Kindling, its plate lit eleven seconds late, the failed-safe word replaced the old name, and it went dark. He has no Path. Ten fragments at rest; the still place untouched since Oryn's order. **Birthday rule:** never place either birthday beside a season name, month order or count back (OWNER-pending #42/#48). [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 13] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:14:| Lira | Wind; Iron R1 formal. All eight left-forearm marks whole; arm slung high and holds nothing until Oryn says. Right ankle taped and unmended. Oryn's crossbow, hook and one bolt; cannot span it herself. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 13] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:18:| Oryn | Tide; Iron R4 provisional. Last located at Thornwater, with route work north next; grey jenny and thirty-foot three-strand rope with her. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 13] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:26:**Cael knows:** ten fragments with current costs/deployment notes; deployment since the Line is 27. The still place is a location under the breastbone, read three times, with all ten going round it and none through; `Not the Quiet. Not a fragment.` He has obeyed the no-touch order. Four sites lie on one map edge: Ring, Stair and Hall entered; fourth unentered, unnamed, undated and untested at 440 yards and two strides radius behind stake 34 repeated one per pace. The three entered sites stop live Arbiters while his already-dark Arbiter remains dark and his fragments answer. He has no Path; nobody knows why. He knows the kit's radius line, 41-kind index, stroke/bar and `third site confirmed on bearing`; Karis's `Someone made this pattern.` remains unanswered.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:28:**Who knows the integration mechanism:** Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Oryn — six. Oryn knows sources by Path and not by person except those she has touched; she does not know Seln supplied Shadow-adjacent. **Not** Vastin, Teague, Pike or Cleon.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:30:**Still-place sharing:** all six know the phenomenon. Cael said the label `the still place` to Oryn; the other four were told the three-sentence description without the label.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:34:**Brom knows:** the mechanism and still-place description; the three entered sites; and the fourth site's outside survey, repeated stake 34 and unknown effect. He refused entry without Oryn and without knowing what the larger circle would do.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:40:**Oryn knows:** the mechanism by Path, the full still-place telling and label, and the three entered sites on one bearing. She left at the day-122 fork and does not know the day-123 fourth-site survey or result at entry.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:61:- **Cael:** Hesk's brass folding straightedge; Hesk's satchel holding the current log, old volume, observation notebook, Hesk's letter/note, Ephram's and Vell's letters, both broker papers, Pike's bark and Oryn's bark.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:63:- **Animals/boxes:** brown mule with the five; grey jenny with Oryn. Three boxes at the back room's warm wall; reserve in the third.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:64:- **Weapon:** Oryn's crossbow, hook and one bolt with Lira; four bolts remain in the wold-wyrm.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:65:- **Letters:** received Hesk's brass/note and Oryn's bark. Sent west on day 130: Hesk and Vell (`The session still stands`), plus the clerk's packet. Ephram's reply is deferred to the first boat of the thaw.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:78:| 8 | Anchor-adjacent | unnamed hand | Perception absent at 14 feet, faint at 12, sure at 10. Purposeful contact unbinding at a knot is a deployment. A held point thins all other fragments. Two counted uses: Stair unbinding and Hall holding, once each way; Hall kerb trial not counted. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 16] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:80:| 10 | Tide-adjacent | Oryn | Partial; Iron; self and contact; clinical. Self-read three times; Oryn read twice, each after ask and explicit yes. Outward bills: right hand for an hour and most of a loaf; slow hand after the telling. `ask first, every time`. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 16] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:83:**Deployment since the Line: 27.** Trace: ford 1; Ring 12; Tide/Oryn ridge 1; Stair 9; Hall 3; Tide/Oryn marsh 1. Self-readings and the Hall kerb trial are excluded. **Invent no new numeric ceilings. Preserve every numeric ceiling and bill fixed by canon.** [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 16]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:93:| Oryn | Terms of service; a route she owns. Cael's three readings and full telling are paid. Her withheld answer was never a debt and still stands. Her rule is in her hand and his. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 17] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:105:- Oryn's old Book 7 debt: paid. Book 8's Millrace deep reading is a new event, not settlement of an entry debt. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 17]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:121:- **Seam with the locked Book 7 ratified** (Sol plan audit): day 131 at Lowmarch; the five; ten fragments; the debt to Oryn paid, not forgiven; the still place told and here neither read nor touched; the fourth site unentered and untested; the kit, the dead man's ledger and fifty-two sheets; the brown mule with the five.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:122:- **Deployment since the Line: TWENTY-NINE.** Twenty-eight on the 140th (the Iron read on frozen ground beside a trapped calf) and twenty-nine on the 161st (the read on the river ice): both in earnest. Shed and meadow work is logged "Trials. Not counted". Anchor's counted uses stay at two; Shadow twice and sealed; no Tide use (asked of Lira and refused); no self-reading; Oryn does not read Cael.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:125:- **The stroke and bar** is on stakes thirty-two and thirty-four only. Karis cannot read the index and does not know it is a grade.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:127:- **Thornwater, days 265–266:** Lira's arm released (OWNER-pending #56 "Five months and twenty days.", said by Lira); **Lira asks and Oryn mends the ankle** ("Lie still," Oryn said; "Thank you." said by Lira; "Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks."). Before this Lira had asked once, on the mountain in Book 7, and nobody since.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:145:- **Teague's wrist (flag):** the leather has been on it "since before the boy could lift a pack"; the joint is thicker than its fellow by the width of a finger; it "clicks"; "A Force paid where the line came out of him." The older healer binds it to her board at night and tells him to leave his Path shut till the thaw. A block lies on the second ledge of the cold road, with a herd lying up above it; he will shift it "as a carter would". The young one has brought him a hot cloth for it on every cold night since he joined. In his own window Teague is named as a Force for the first time in this edition. No Force is used on the page.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:147:- **The ice road (flag):** a four-wheeled cart behind two mules, eighty yards out, with a dozen barrels and two pigs of iron for the smith; the carter heavy and grey-bearded, unnamed; one barrel of fish lost. Hauled out on the ferry's own rope and drum by Oryn's brown mule. Pike: "That's said. It's not entered."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:155:- **Thornwater's yard (repair r1):** the mule finds Oryn first; she is on her heels at the bench's end binding an old man's hand, and her right hand goes out behind her to the mule's cheek; she looks the five over only after the old man is sent off, Cael first and briefly, then Brom's knot, Lira's boot, and last the sling.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:156:- **Thornwater (flag):** the ford in thaw is thigh-deep over the sill, with the white stones and the bar under water; Lira finds the ledge by the smooth water and the line of standing waves below it. The ankle "had knit as it lay in a river, crooked"; an hour. Oryn: "It stops being mine when you take it." She will not undo the older healer's knot and will look at the shoulder "beside her". The bowman comes down off his platform during the mending. The steading's woman counts for a sixth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:162:**Where everyone is.** Six at the lower inn: Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, and Oryn, who came down from Thornwater unasked because Lowmarch is her first stop after a thaw and the mill her second. Her brown mule is in the ferryman's shed. The mill's grey jenny is not mentioned after Book 7. Teague's five are at the upper inn; they do not appear after the 190th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:164:**Cael.** Nineteen. **Ten fragments.** **Deployment since the Line: twenty-nine** (twenty-seven at entry; the read on frozen ground at the calf, the 140th; the read on river ice, the 161st). All ten tried in the cold term and written up as *The ten, by use*: Wind (the lock cannot be shortened, only placed), Ember (the burn), Shadow (held, not opened), Compression (both heels; ground worth a load), Pressure (seen coming; narrow and deep; comes back), Blade (short; the steel pays), the read (ground or air; a pace and a half; the eyes), Storm (one lane; ten counts; a fourth untried), Anchor (a point held to thirty; ten, twelve and fourteen feet), Tide (asked of Lira; told no; not used). Shadow used twice in all and shut. Anchor's counted uses still two. Tide: Oryn twice, himself three times, nobody else. **The still place** has not been read or touched. **The instruments:** on the 168th the kit's cord (four knots to a length) measured the inn yard at forty-two strides for Karis, Lira, Brom and Seln and at forty-one and a piece for him, three times; the Ternhall brass read a hair short in his hand and Hesk's a hair long; he has touched none of the three since; his ruling is *hold*; Oryn has been told and has no answer. Nobody has offered a cause. He lost to Teague's spear three to none (148th) and three to one (158th). He has entered Teague as the better captain. He has not ruled on Karis's case. He has written *West, and inside*. Body: sound; knuckles skinned on the 140th; near sight lost for an hour on the 140th and for an evening on the 161st, and back.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:166:**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. No burst. Her long knife has an edge again (the 181st). **Left arm released on the 266th: she undid Oryn's knot herself.** All eight marks pale. "It'll be slow for a month and it'll ache in the wet for a year… Don't fall on it." It has held a boot and lifted a bench. **Right ankle mended on the 266th**, an hour on Oryn's plank; she stands on the ball of the foot. She wears the carter's great boot without its packing. She still has Oryn's crossbow and its one bolt (not mentioned as returned). She coached Cael's feet from the bench ("out" and "home") and the young one's. **She asked for the ankle on the 266th, and said "Thank you." to Oryn afterward; before that she asked nobody for anything in this movement.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:168:**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. No declaration. **Right shoulder still in the older healer's webbing;** Oryn would not undo another woman's knot and will look at it beside her. He set forty-one posts left-handed and re-set two of Teague's. He fetched the carter out of the river lying flat, with the bill's hook. He keeps a second dead slip (the fence) inside his shirt. He lays six bowls and takes none back.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:174:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four. She released the arm only when Lira took it; mended the ankle; answered Lira's thanks with "Route's whole… The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks."; left the shoulder to the woman who tied it. She has seen the map with four rings and the line ("That's a line.") and has been told of the fourth site: twice the size, fenced, unentered. She has been told of the cord and the edges. **She has not read Cael** and has said that she will know what she is reading for before she does. At the word *station* she shut her mouth on a sentence and said nothing. She did not sit in the sixth place. She does not know that Seln is Shadow's source.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:180:**Objects and money.** **A hundred and eighteen marks in hand** (96 − 20 for the cold stay; + 40 for the fence; + 5 for the roof; − 3 for the mule's shed). The reserve sealed and unopened. Owed: sixty yards of four-strand rope to the ferryman, wanted with the first boat; one reed hurdle; a letter to Ephram. Stake thirty-two has still never been driven. Both brass edges are in their cloths.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:191:Packet 002 already carries day 270, the six, Oryn's first post-thaw stop, Lira's two uncertain arms, Brom's bound/unread shoulder, the one-week ferry prediction, and Karis's unanswered case (`packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:18-20`). Its author must additionally inherit:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:193:- **Cael and the fragments:** deployment is 29, not 27; the calf and river-ice reads are the two counted additions. Shadow remains exactly twice and sealed; Anchor's counted uses remain two; Tide was refused and unused; the still place remains untouched (`manuscript/chapter-02.md:225-229`; `manuscript/chapter-04.md:239-243`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:211-217`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:189-201`). His near sight recovered after both read bills, and his day-140 knuckles are old minor damage by day 270 (`manuscript/chapter-02.md:217-225`; `manuscript/chapter-04.md:191-209`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:194:- **The anomaly:** the cord reads forty-two strides in four hands and forty-one and a piece in Cael's, three times; Ternhall is a hair short and Hesk a hair long only in his hand; the tools are sound; Karis has preserved one hair; ruling `hold`; no cause or inference (`manuscript/chapter-05.md:3-155,259`). Oryn knows these facts and has offered no theory (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:189-201`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:196:- **Lira:** her right ankle is newly mended; she walks on the ball of it and wears the oversized carter boot without its old stuffing. Her left arm is released but slow for a month, aches in wet for a year, and is not to be fallen on (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:127-151`). She still has Oryn's crossbow, hook, and one bolt; no return occurs (`manuscript/chapter-02.md:7`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:283`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:197:- **Brom:** the right shoulder remains in the older healer's four-yard drover's knot. Oryn declined to undo another healer's work and will inspect it beside her (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:139-143`). His hook was used on the ice rescue but remains with the crossbow kit (`manuscript/chapter-04.md:139-153`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:200:- **Oryn:** she knows the fourth-site description, the map line, and the instrument anomaly, but has not read Cael and will not until she knows the purpose (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:163-209`). She did not take the sixth chair (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:223-225`). Her grey jenny remains at Thornwater; the brown mule is with the six at Lowmarch (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md:131-147`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:65-77,217`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:205:**Movement 1 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Sol recheck of repair r1: CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES; all four tracked passages RESOLVED against the source; no new tracking; every binding ruling above borne out by the surviving prose. Two fixes applied by the coordinator: ch3, the author's own "his Path" (of Teague) now reads "the Force"; ch6, Seln's sentence after Karis's protected speech now gives the asset-restriction as locked Book 6 ch58 states it — **the paper executes when an enrolled name is written in a book inside a district, and must be served within the hour** (not "a certificate inside the Line"). The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report after the fixes. Final: 30,941 prose words; gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (9 protected). Purse 118 marks; deployment twenty-nine; day 270 at Lowmarch.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:212:- **Deployment since the Line: THIRTY.** One use added: the Iron read in earnest on the bank at the landing on the 277th (the post's foot and the old sill), paid in near sight until the afternoon; logged twice. Pressure, Anchor and Wind were refused at the landing; Wind and the read refused in Lira's bout; Tide unused; Shadow held, twice and sealed; Oryn has not read Cael.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:217:- **Speakers (protected):** "Archmarshal" is Cael's; "What follows you," is Lira's; "More than four." is Karis's; "She's right. Go and lie down, and don't take the stairs fast," is Oryn's (Karis owns the order to bed). The long table's close is verbatim. "Nothing that can cross the Line"; the rim of the Stair "is not mine".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:221:- **Lowmarch:** the mule's stool at the board's end (Oryn stands beside it); Pike's new cloth, Teague first, the five carried **eleventh** by place; Oryn's bench a yard past Pike's right-hand post; the first boat took people only; the hauling rope has two yarns gone and the stern strap is improvised; the sixty yards of cordage are still on the western bank and the rope debt stands; the hurdle is paid. Ephram's letter went west on the afternoon boat. **Purse: 118 marks.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:222:- **Oryn's swallowed sentence** has now been shut in three times (the 268th, the 271st, the night of the 277th).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:232:- **The mule's stool (flag):** a three-legged milking stool from the keeper's kitchen, set at the board's end on the 271st with the sixth bowl. Oryn will not sit on it; Lira names it; Vastin asks whether the place is taken and is told whose it is.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:234:- **Oryn at Lowmarch (flag):** her bench is a form set along the wall under the eave, a yard past the right-hand post of Pike's plank, by the door of the keeper's wash-house, where she works with the door open. Nine on the first morning. She takes payment in kind. "I'll not spend on what grease will do." She does not go up the bank to the older healer.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:242:- **The flat (repaired):** a seat-courier's flat of waxed leather, "as broad as a man's shoulders and no thicker than two fingers", stamped *BY SEAT COURIER. BY HAND.*; six rows, a year to a row, the newest uppermost, each in a tape; a pocket in the lid. **The abstracts:** printed forms; four signs and a number at the head (the Stair's sheet has the dead surveyor's four signs and thirty-two); a column for the day in the office's reckoning; a measure given in lengths, knots and strides; and a narrow right-hand column whose printed head says that it is for **the anomaly**. **In every clerk's hand, in every one of six years, that column holds the single word *Total*, and nobody has written a second word beside it.** There is no figure and no sum. Karis counts more than four different groups of signs in the newest row, on her fingers, and will not say a number until she has checked it in daylight. No sheets are counted.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:252:**Where everyone is.** Seven under the lower inn's roof: Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln; Oryn, who is on her road and at her bench by first light; and **Vastin, in the loft over the tap, at a copper a night**, who is on nobody's sheet and has asked for nothing but a bed. Teague's five are at the upper inn, with forty sacks of salt on the bank. The brown mule is in the ferryman's shed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:254:**Cael.** Nineteen. **Ten fragments.** **Deployment since the Line: thirty** (the read on the ground at the landing, the 277th). Shadow used twice in all and shut; held at dusk on the 272nd and the 277th. Anchor's counted uses still two. Tide: Oryn twice, himself three times, nobody else; he did not ask to read the knee. **The still place** has not been read, touched or named. He has not touched the cord or either brass edge for a hundred and nine days; the ruling is *hold*. His near sight went at the landing and was back for print by the afternoon. **He has not ruled.** He will say it "at the plank in the morning, in daylight" and ask for hands. He has not touched the copied page; his hand lay a hand's width from it for the whole of a lamp. **He has not read the technician's date**: he was at the table's far end; he knows that it is a registry year and a day, and that it is the line at which Seln stopped; he chose not to go up the table and read it. He lost the bout to Lira, two touches to three. He has written to Ephram. He kept back his own question to Vastin (why the second reading was declined). He has told Vastin nothing of what he carries.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:256:**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. No burst. **Left arm: the eighth day out of the wool on the 273rd. It told her once, in the bout, and she did not stop.** It is slow; it ached after rain. She did not fall on it. Right ankle sound in the great boot. Her certificate is in her coat. She still has Oryn's crossbow and its one bolt (not mentioned in these chapters). She sat last at the table; she asked "Why us." and "What follows you,"; she read the technician's sheet aloud, without its figures.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:264:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four. A bench under the eave since the 272nd. She saw the bout and said nothing. She has not asked about the knee, and Vastin has offered it to nobody; she seconded Karis's order to bed with one line about the stairs. **She has not read Cael.** She has shut her mouth three times on the same sentence. She did not sit on the stool. She does not know that Seln is Shadow's source.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:270:**Pike's book and the cloth.** **Eleven lines.** The season line's number still blank. **Eleventh on the new cloth**, painted on the 272nd. Vastin is "nothing yet" and is not entered. Oryn is on no slip.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:272:**Objects and money.** **A hundred and eighteen marks in hand**, unchanged. The reserve sealed. Owed: **sixty yards of four-strand rope** to the ferryman (the cordage is on the western landing; his one hauling rope has two yarns gone). **The hurdle is paid.** **The letter to Ephram is sent.** The three boxes are at the hearth's end, roped. Stake thirty-two has still never been driven. On Karis's table: the flat (the sheet inside it), the broker's paper beside it, Seln's wand beside that, and the copied page at the far end.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:286:- **What each knows.** All six and Vastin have heard no key, the citation/title/place, suppressed survey records and the technician's visible line/bar (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:149–193`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:201–257`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:59–151`). Karis has not finished the records and cannot read the index or bar (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:223–253`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:129–135,285–289`). Seln has done an unexplained sum and said only “I have read it”; Cael does not know the sum (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:137–153`). Vastin does not know the integration mechanism, directive, objection, what Cael carries, or what lies under the bar (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:129–131`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:119–129`). Nobody connects the date to anyone (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:137–153`). Oryn has not read Cael and has not asked to read Vastin's knee (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:29–47`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:287:- **Vastin's physical state and status.** Brown frieze coat, ash stick, bad knee, raw hands and a left hand that does not open flat; no age; no Iron Wall shown; not joined and has asked only for a bed (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:197–201`; `manuscript/chapter-09.md:115–143,187–191`; `manuscript/chapter-10.md:231–271`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:19–23`). He sleeps in the loft over the tap, up the keeper's stair, after beginning the climb fast and finishing slowly (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:263–271`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:193–219,297`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:290:- **Ledger state.** It is the night before day 278; crew purse 118 marks; deployment thirty; ten fragments; Shadow still sealed after two prior uses; Anchor still two counted uses; Tide unused here; still place untouched (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:151–153`; `manuscript/chapter-09.md:263–265`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:291–295`). Cael has not touched the page and has promised a daylight ruling at the plank with hands (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:223–241,267–299`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:292:**Movement 2 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1: the 24 coordinator-applied fixes kept and their joins smoothed; the page made a copy; the layer cut to four facts (Lira and Brom say what it changes: there is nobody to ask); *Total* made the anomaly column's entry; the technician's sheet read out by Lira with a date and no figures, filed at and laid back at the end of the second row; Seln's stillness re-entered in a new order; receipt and night log made literally true ("Read in part. Understood in no part."); the completion report's five strokes and count of six; ch7's opening oriented. Sol recheck: CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES; the tracked passage RESOLVED; every binding ruling above borne out; the day arithmetic confirmed (ice 111 days; the wrist 124; the sling 170; the rim 163; the cord 109; the report 175). Three fixes applied by the coordinator: ch7 "a healer's Path" → "a healer's craft" (no possessive before Path in narration); ch8's bluff memory cut back to what Book 5 shows; ch10 "through a frame shop" removed. Rulings from the recheck: **Lira reading the sheet aloud is the author's staging and stands** (the map protects the wording, the sum and the withholding, not the reader); the two descriptions of the cited record agree. The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report. Final: 30,105 prose words; gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (11 protected). Purse 118 marks; deployment thirty; the night before day 278 at Lowmarch.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:298:- **Entry seam with Movement 2 ratified** (Sol plan audit): day 278 at Lowmarch; purse 118; deployment thirty; the papers with Karis; Vastin off the sheet and following; the ferry for people only; the cordage on the western bank **refused as three-strand** — sixty yards of four-strand are still owed to the ferryman.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:300:- **Deployment since the Line: THIRTY-TWO**, both on the 279th at the cut: one grain of Ember at the mark (thirty-one; the heat came home along the left arm) and one Wind burst **away**, ten strides, to the north bank inside the wall (thirty-two). Pressure, Anchor, Edge, Storm and the read refused there. Shadow held, twice and sealed; Tide unused; no self-reading; Oryn has not read Cael. **Ten fragments: nothing came of standing two feet from the wall; the eleventh has not come.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:301:- **The cut (the author's staging stands; BOOK_MAP §8 allows it).** A hundred strides, a stride of ice down the middle, scree on the south, a low north bank, the sink fifty-five yards below it. Eight hounds (five seen, three hidden). The den had learned the road: it runs to where a declaration ENDS. Karis, Oryn and the mule were at the foot; Vastin, a stride behind Brom, stepped out and **declared Iron Wall** — a plane across the road from a line struck with his stick, wall to wall, two feet from Cael, rooted (he may not lift a foot), loud, spending him to the floor. Brom's rock (twice), Lira's knife with the left hand holding, Seln in the heap; five dead; **three went through the rotten ice of the sink and did not come up**. Costs: Brom's right foot (two toes, ten days from the 279th); **Vastin's right knee** (four holes shut by Oryn after "May I?" / "Yes"; the joint bound with laths; **a month** from the 279th: stick, no kneeling, no running, no wall). Karis's sixth line: *It goes to where a declaration ends, if it has learned that the declaring moves.* Twenty paid; **purse 138**.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:303:- **The spring (the 280th).** Six rows counted twice by two people. Five columns on every abstract: the day in the registry's reckoning; the station (eight points); the measure; *Instruments* ("Cord true. Edge true. Level true." on every line for six years); the anomaly (*Total*). **Karis matches FOUR sign-groups to the hide by their measures (three alike to the stride, one double) and gives no number of places; no fifth place is described** (held for the 298th). The measures have not changed in six years. The remark *Behaves as device. Cannot be.* stands in a ruled space on the Stair's sheet in the fourth row; **its hand is not identified**; the space for remarks is gone from the next year's printing. **The grade:** a ruled square at the head of every sheet with the same stroke and bar on all four matched places, drawn no larger on the place whose measure is double; in the field it is on stake thirty-two and on the fourth site's thirty-fours only. Karis: a class, unread; "Two copies of one ignorance." Nobody says who set it or why. Karis stopped her lamps sentence with the ruler line and did not finish it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:306:- **The fork (the 280th evening; the 281st).** Oryn: "I'm not an archive person."; her past (a house for the sick in a city inside the Line; the column for the patient's tier; a woman from the river sheds whom she mended off the sheet; she walked out of a gate and has not been through one since — the author's, kept); "Leaving and routing are different verbs. I'm doing the second."; Seln's "Three weeks"; **the station term, written in the log and read back (verbatim)**; she priced all six, Vastin as long as the rest; "That's on me. It's the one thing I'm walking up that road owing, and I'll pay it." (the reading she has not given Cael); "Bring me whatever walks out of that archive with you. All of it."; "Not the steps," … "Not the square." She went north with the brown mule, her linen and the crossbow with its one bolt: five gates, the ford, Millrace in three weeks.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:307:- **Loads from the fork:** boxes on Brom (good shoulder), Lira (both arms) and Cael; Karis the flat and the hide; **Vastin took up the tarred kit case unasked** and has walked beside Cael since the rise. Brom carries Oryn's empty bowl.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:312:All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol): editorial; cold read; source-distance (3 tracked passages, none dense; probe 2% / 15%); plan / canon / protected-text audit (REPAIR; 102 exact fixes). Coordinator rulings against the audit, after checking the source and the locked Book 7: the cut's staging, the Ember use and the count of thirty-two KEPT (BOOK_MAP §8: private staging the author owns; the audit's 39 re-staging fixes declined); Oryn's past KEPT; Cael's touch of the page KEPT; the slip left as the packet quotes it; "every bar of a fence" KEPT (Book 7 ch58). Accepted from the audit: the six markers' speakers (two filled with the plan's own clause only); the loads for Movement 4; no fifth place or number; no second calendar; the remark's hand unidentified. Eleven fixes applied by the coordinator; the rest recomposed by the author. **Repair r1 in progress with the same author.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:317:- **The slip and Pike's rule.** The clearance slip came over in the bag on the 277th; Pike drew a road between two heaps beside it. Twenty, "at the hold's own gate, on the factor's thumb, when the factor's walked it". **Pike will not write a clearance taken until a healer is said** (his own rule since his second year, when one of a crew of four bled for two days on a hurdle). His sixth line: *And a healer; of her own road; at her own price.*, the first column he has had for Oryn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:318:- **Oryn's round this thaw.** West with the six as the slip's healer; from the fork-stone north to "five gates up along the hill-foot", one with a child that she was to have heard a cold term ago; then "down the far water to the ford, and over, and on to the mill from above". Three weeks puts her at Millrace.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:322:- **The four hands.** Flat, palm down: *stand*. A shut fist: *seen*. Two fingers: *come on*. A hand turned over empty: *nothing*. The doctrine in one line: "Nobody declares unless they're meant to be loud. One of us, once, in a place that we've chosen beforehand."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:324:- **The shoulder hold and its factor.** A foot-track from a cairn below the spur; a plain bar in a wall as thick as a cart; a small clean yard, a long low house, a salting-shed with empty hooks. The factor: spare, grey, a leather apron, a slate on a cord, a sheep-crook, pale eyes; a thumb-mark like a crook; **no name and no pronoun on the page**. Three carts, a carter and two mules lost since the frost.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:328:- **Bodies.** Vastin: four holes and a tear below the right knee, shut by Oryn; the joint bound with linen and two laths; **the bad knee is the right**. Brom: the right boot torn; two toes bruised, bound together, ten days.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:329:- **Oryn's past (kept by the coordinator as written; the order of telling changed in r1).** "I'd my rank off a board at the foot of a bed." A house for the sick "inside a wall", forty beds, six healers; her Iron fourth rank is provisional because she "never stayed to have it confirmed". **A sheet on a board at each bed's foot: name, complaint, what had been spent, and a column for the patient's tier.** In a week of fever the spending went down the column from the top; a woman from the river sheds with no tier went to the bottom of the heap; Oryn went to her at night, off the sheet, and it was enough (**nobody died**); the woman who kept the house said that a healer who spends off the sheet has stolen from whoever stood next on it. Asked where, she will not say: "They keep the same sheet at the foot of every bed inside the Line." She walked out of a gate in the coat she stood in and has not been through one since.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:337:- **The loads from the fork (r1).** Boxes on Brom (left shoulder), Lira (both arms through the beckets) and Cael. Seln carries none: he goes ahead with his hands empty. **The tarred case was left leaning on the fork-stone; Karis stopped forty strides up; Vastin went back for it unasked, after Oryn was out of sight, hooked its strap with his stick without kneeling, and slung it above his sound leg.** He told Cael so at once: "I waited until she could not be put to the trouble of forbidding it a third time." "It is a cord, a mallet and one stake."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:340:- **Roles (all unnamed):** the shoulder hold's factor and "the hold's woman"; the broker and his clerk on the western landing; the keeper of the house for the sick, the Gold with the wrist and the woman from the river sheds in Oryn's account.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:347:**Where everyone is.** Six going down off the rise: Seln in front, Lira, Brom, Karis, and then **Cael with Vastin walking beside him on the ditch side** (from the top of the rise; nobody asked him to and nobody told him no). Oryn and the brown mule went north from the fork at first light and did not look back. Teague's five are east of the river.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:349:**Cael.** Nineteen. **Ten fragments; no eleventh.** **Deployment thirty-two.** Left palm stung by Ember. He ruled on a job and has made no vow. **He has read the technician's date, laid it against the first line of his own file, and knows it for the day of his own Kindling. He has not written it, has told nobody, and has put no verb to it.** He said "You do now" to Vastin at the hold. He has written in the log, at Oryn's asking, that inside Treswick he does not go near the station. **He has laid his hand on the page once, on the rise, and Karis has it again.** He has seen the light on the crown and turned from it. He carries a box. He asked "Who's Cleon?" and has the name.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:351:**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. No burst. **Arm: the sixteenth day out of the wool on the 281st.** It held a hound by the scruff while the right hand struck; it votes; **she carries a box on her back with both arms through its beckets.** Oryn: slow for as long again; don't fall on it. **She no longer has the crossbow.** She knows that Cael has put something away and has not asked.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:353:**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. No grey at any point. Right shoulder still in the older healer's knot (if it tells him anything he is to put the load down and leave it down). **Right foot: two toes bruised, bound; ten days from the 279th, eight left on the 281st.** One box on the left shoulder. He has the purse and Pike's thumbed slip. He lays seven bowls and will carry Oryn's empty.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:359:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four, provisional. On Pike's slip as its healer. She asked Vastin and had an explicit yes; shut four holes; bound the joint; two fingers on his wrist. She has priced all six and given Vastin as long as any. **She has not read Cael**: "It's the one thing I'm walking up that road owing, and I'll pay it." She has told the house, the column and why she left, and will not say where. She has her term in his log and has read it there. Gone north with the mule, her linen, and her crossbow with its one bolt; five gates, the ford, then Millrace in three weeks. She does not know that Vastin is carrying the kit's case.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:361:**Vastin.** No office; **no age stated**. **Iron Wall declared once, on the 279th, in the cut**; spent to the floor. **Right knee: bitten, shut, bound stiff; the 281st is the second day of thirty**; on the stick; no kneeling, running or walls. He qualified every instruction. **He has not sat in front of the crew since the cut.** **He carries the tarred kit case (cord, mallet, stake thirty-two) on the shoulder above his sound leg, taken up unasked at the fork-stone after Oryn had gone, and has told Cael so.** **He walks beside Cael from the top of the rise.** He said the town's name at the spring, the first to say it since the page. He knows the four hands, the doctrine and where a post stands. He has heard the daylight reading whole. **He does not know that the date means anything to anybody**, the mechanism, what Cael carries, the instruments' behaviour in Cael's hand, or what is under the bar; nothing has been said of a directive or an objection. He has not asked to join and nobody has spoken of it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:367:**Objects and money.** **A hundred and thirty-eight marks.** The reserve sealed. **Owed: sixty yards of four-strand rope to the ferryman.** Three boxes on Brom, Lira and Cael. The kit's case with Vastin. Stake thirty-two never driven. The cord and both edges untouched by Cael since the 168th. Hesk's book has the term on the 280th's leaf and no line for the date.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:371:**Who knows what.** The mechanism: six, as before. The daylight reading: the six at the slab, and Oryn by hearing. **The date: Cael and Seln, each alone.** Nobody has interpreted the sequence, said who classed the places or why, or joined the remark to anything or anybody.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:381:- **Knowledge:** Cael and Seln alone know that the unprinted date matches Cael's Kindling day; neither has said or written it, neither has interpreted the sequence, and neither knows for certain what the other concluded (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:3–31,59–65,85–149`). Karis knows both men have read the sheet but not what they made of it (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:143–149`). Vastin heard the records reading but does not know the arithmetic, integration mechanism or Cael's fragments (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:159–205`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:266`). Oryn heard the archive discussion from the basin but not the date conclusion (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:229–231`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:56`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:382:- **Bodies:** Vastin's right knee is shut, lath-bound and on day two of Oryn's thirty-day month on the 281st; stick, no kneeling, no running, no wall, and he has finally accepted being priced equally (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:27–65`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:151–169`). Brom's right two toes are bound with eight days left on the ten-day term, and his right shoulder remains in the older healer's knot; he must put a load down if it speaks (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:75`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:131–139`). Lira's arm remains slow and is on day sixteen out of wool (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:119–129`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:383:- **Oryn:** she and the brown mule are north of the fork on the reverse circuit; she has her linen and crossbow with one bolt. Her stated route is five gates, the ford and Millrace, where she expects the six in three weeks; she still owes Cael the proper reading and expects “all of it” from the archive (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:63–81,171–219`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:384:- **Money/objects:** purse 138; reserve sealed; sixty yards of four-strand still owed; Pike's thumbed slip is in Brom's shirt; no cordage was bought (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:149–165`; `manuscript/chapter-16.md:99–101,187`). Oryn's empty bowl is Brom's to carry (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:221–223`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:385:- **Progression:** ten fragments, deployment THIRTY-TWO (coordinator ruling: one Ember grain at the mark and one Wind burst away, both at the cut); Shadow sealed, Anchor still two, Tide unused, no self-read, no eleventh (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:133–163,223–227`; `manuscript/chapter-16.md:205–211`). Vastin has shown Iron Wall once; Cael witnessed it but did not acquire it (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:55`; `packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:52`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:388:**Movement 3 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1 (ch13, ch16–19; ch14–15 untouched): the eleven coordinator-applied fixes kept and their joins smoothed (Seln on the north bank beside the factor; Cael had not known that he would say "You do now,"; Vastin names the town); no number of places and no fifth place (Karis counted groups, not places; four matched to the hide; the other sheets' corners turned down, uncounted and undescribed); the second calendar cut (Seln knew the day because he had copied that line of Cael's file twice; Cael laid the date he knows against the sheet's, a figure at a time, twice); three tracked passages re-ordered; the ruler line verbatim at the stopped lamps sentence; the remark's hand unidentified; Brom counts the spring's three findings on his fingers; the loads and the closing file made to meet Movement 4 (**Vastin took the kit case against the letter of Oryn's "you're not to" and told Cael so at once; Oryn does not know**; he walks a shoulder off Cael's left from a dozen strides down the rise). Sol recheck: CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES; all tracked passages RESOLVED; every binding ruling borne out; the settled rulings (the cut's staging, thirty-two, Oryn's past, the hand on the page) confirmed in the surviving prose. Two fixes applied by the coordinator: ch16 "Two days ago, at a board" (was three); ch18 Seln "has spent fifteen years among the seat's paper" (he copied for twelve). The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report. Final: 34,751 prose words (about 2% over; accepted — the added scene carries the loads and the seam); gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (16 protected). Purse 138 marks; deployment thirty-two; day 281, near noon, going down off the rise toward Treswick.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:394:- **Entry seam with Movement 3 ratified** (Sol plan audit): day 281 going down off the rise; six and no mule; the loads; deployment thirty-two; ten fragments; purse 138; bodies; the papers with Karis (the flat, the hide, the copied page in oilcloth, the dead surveyor's ledger, her notebook).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:396:- **The reading inward (the 281st): the fourth and fifth self-readings**, with Tide, ROUND the still place and never in; **not counted** ("Myself, twice: not counted, as before"); a palm on a gatepost while it was open is a trial. Finding (protected): "He had been putting a cord on a stone and writing down *no length*." — the tenth feels only what flows; where nothing flows it returns nothing, and that nothing is the instrument's limit, not a finding about the place (a gatepost and the middle of himself come back alike). **He needs an instrument for what does not move.** He read Oryn's order for the leave he wanted, has logged that, and **owes her the telling at the mill before anything else is said**. Lira asked and is entered as having asked. **Deployment since the Line: thirty-two; ten fragments; none acquired.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:404:- **Oryn (cutaways):** at her first gate north (unnamed) she re-broke and set, with his leave, the wrist of a carter of Oxhollow that had knit wrong over the cold term (spent to greyness; a day lost); at her second (unnamed) she turned a child lying across and a daughter was born alive at first light on the 284th. No patient died. She has heard of no leaf. She still owes Cael the reading and is a day behind her round.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:430:- **Oryn's north road.** The first gate lies a day and a half north of the fork: a small hold with a wall of field-stone, a gate of oak bars, and a gate-house and bench on the wall's outer face; she has sat there on thirty rounds and never been through the gate. **The carter:** of Oxhollow, big, red-bearded, there for the hay; his right wrist was broken under a wheel a week after she passed Oxhollow before the snow, and strapped at Oxhollow's gate by the keeper's wife with a wet strap and two spoons; it knit a thumb's breadth out. She would not part it tired or without his word; he gave it in the morning; she re-set and knit it in an hour and was grey; six weeks in the binding; paid in oats. She spent her one day in hand there. **The second gate,** nine miles on, reached after dark on the 283rd: a boy of three whose chest she was to have heard a cold term ago, and who had mended himself; the keeper's son's wife in a gate-house built outside the wall, in labour since first light with the child lying across; "May I?" / "Yes. Yes. Do it."; she turned it from outside over some hours, giving it what she had kept for the road; **a daughter, alive, at first light on the 284th.** Nobody died. In her own head she has called the place in Cael "a stone" and "a join" and has decided that it was neither; she has no word.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:431:- **Small things.** Brom carries a flint, a steel and charred rag. Brom stood over Karis with a bowl on the 283rd. Oryn's empty bowl rides under the lashing of Brom's box. Children in the tar yard play at gates ("Then I'm the gate"). A house for the sick inside the second wall hangs its hours on a slate at the door: *First bell: buff. Second bell: blue. Cards, after the fourth, at the side door, as the house's means allow.* (Vastin: the ninth article of a schedule.)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:432:- **Roles (all unnamed):** two carters at the pull-in; the three gate keepers and the book-keeper at the outer gate; a broker's clerk; the ropemaker; the two smiths and the hired Ember; the inn's woman; an old woman porter at the kerb; a girl with eggs; the cook-house boy; Seln's porter; a yard-man; the clerk; Oryn's patients, the carter, the old woman who catches the hold's children, the mother and the keeper's son.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:435:*(Refreshed after repair r1, 2026-10-11. No fact of the calendar, bodies, money, loads or deployment changed in repair; the lines for Cael, Lira, Vastin, Cleon and the clerk are as the repaired text stands, and the markers are gone.)*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:437:**Calendar.** The forenoon of the **two hundred and eighty-fourth day past the Line**, under Treswick, on the head of the stair inside the iron door. Days on the page: 281 (the rise's foot; the posts; the three-mile pull-in), 282 (the bridge; the outer gate; the district; the inn; the district's edge; Seln's report), 283 (the cook-house at noon; the route; the evening), 284 (the inn yard at dawn; the second bell; two gates; the lane; the cut; the yard; the clerk; the door). Oryn: the first gate at dusk on the 282nd and the morning of the 283rd; the second gate from the night of the 283rd to first light on the 284th. No season, month or weekday name; no figure for the technician's date; no count of years since the Kindling.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:439:**Where everyone is.** Five inside the iron door: Karis, Brom, Lira, Vastin, Cael, with Cleon at the stair's head holding one lamp. The clerk is outside it with his lantern. **Seln is above ground, on no card, where he can see who comes to look at the door**; nobody saw him on the climb. Oryn and the brown mule are at the second of her five gates, north along the hill-foot, with three gates, the ford and Millrace ahead and her day in hand spent. Teague's five are east of the river (not on the page).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:441:**Cael.** Nineteen. **Ten fragments. Deployment thirty-two.** He has read himself a fourth and a fifth time (the 281st), round and not in. **Finding:** the reading feels what moves; the place has nothing that moves; the reading's nothing was never an answer; he needs an instrument for what does not move, and knows of two (the station, which he has promised to stay away from, and the man under the town). He has entered that he read Oryn's order for the leave he wanted, and that she is to be told so at the mill before anything else. **He has told Vastin** that the place was read twice that day and came back with nothing, and that what he reads with cannot read what does not move; **not what reads, or how.** Lira has read the log's entry. He has not told anybody the date, and has not written it. **He has not set foot on the square or the steps and has not looked at the crown**; the term has cost him something for the first time (the lane with four alleys). He has seen Cleon at five strides and was not looked at; he is afraid that the man will "look up". He wrote *Entered by count. That's the door.* in the log on the night of the 282nd, and said the #53 line that night as his own rough figure. He went into the registry as one of *four* in a green book, with his eyes on his boots. Body: sound; a box-strap's mark on his neck.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:445:**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. No grey. Right shoulder in the older healer's knot (it has not spoken). Right foot: five days left on the 284th; he favours it on hills. One box, with Oryn's bowl under its lashing. **The purse: a hundred and thirty-six.** Pike's thumbed slip in his shirt. He has looked at four-strand and will take it "going out". He lays seven bowls.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:451:**Vastin.** No office; no age stated. **Right knee: the fifth day of thirty on the 284th**; on the stick; no kneeling, no running, no wall. It did nine miles on the 281st and twenty-two steps down on the 284th; the stick slipped once and he caught himself on the wall with the left hand. **He has sat three times.** He has told Cael the rest of why he declined the second reading: the Ostrand reason stands as the cause, and beside it his private relief at never learning what a plate would say (glad of a right act for a wrong reason). He holds what Cael gave him and has not asked what read it. He does not know the mechanism, what Cael carries, the sum, or what is under the bar; he does no date arithmetic. He has said once that he has papers he will not show. He consented to be the fourth before he was asked and went through three counts as a hand, looking at his boots, "very ill" and then a little better; the clerk looked at him after the line was blotted, opened his mouth, and did not ask. He has not asked to join and nobody has spoken of it. He carries the kit case, still against the letter of Oryn's instruction; Oryn does not know.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:453:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four, provisional. Two gates done of five. She parted and re-knit a carter's wrist at the first (asked; told yes in the morning) and turned a child at the second (asked; told yes). **Nobody has died under her hands.** She is spent to grey and a day behind her own reckoning. She has not been through a gate. She has the mule, her linen and the crossbow. She owes Cael the reading and has thought about it twice; she has heard of no leaf and knows nothing of what happened on the road's edge.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:461:**Who knows what.** The mechanism: six, as before (Oryn among them); not Vastin, Cleon or the clerk. The inward finding of the 281st: Cael, Lira (from the log) and, in its outline, Vastin. The why of the declining: Cael and Vastin. The sum: Cael and Seln, each alone. Nobody has interpreted anything.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:468:- **Who is below.** Inside the iron door are Cael, Brom, Lira, Vastin and Karis, with Cleon at the stair head; the unnamed clerk and his lantern remain outside. Seln is above ground, not on the 284th card or count, positioned to see who comes to the door. Oryn and the brown mule are at the second unnamed gate north (`ch25:87–117`; `ch26:183–279`; `AUTHOR-REPORT:101`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:469:- **Loads and papers.** Boxes remain on Brom, Lira and Cael; the kit case remains on Vastin; Karis has the flat, hide/calfskin, copied page in oilcloth, dead surveyor's ledger and notebook. The fifty-two first copies are back in their box in order; Oryn's bowl is under Brom's lashing; Seln retains his closed case; Cleon has the two-cornered card (`ch24:199–225,275–293`; `ch25:89–117,229–237`; `ch26:195,213,261–267`; inherited M3 custody at `STATE_LEDGER:306–308`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:474:- **Cael's state.** Ten fragments; deployment thirty-two. He has made the fourth and fifth self-readings, both around/not in, and concluded that Tide reports only current and cannot read the still place. He owes Oryn an admission at Millrace. Lira has read the log. The square/steps/crown promise still holds and has now cost him something (`ch20:95–215`; `ch21:49–65,227–247`; `ch26:9–25,175`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:476:- **Other live state.** Lira's Iron-first paper remains unshown; the ladder no longer pulls. Karis has recognized the bridge's dark stone under the registry and has not yet stated a conclusion. The sixty yards of four-strand remain owed and Brom intends to buy them going out. Oryn has delivered a live daughter, is spent and a day behind her circuit, has heard of no leaf, and still owes Cael the reading (`ch22:125–127,215–283`; `ch24:219–231`; `ch25:3–83`; `ch26:47–79,137–145`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:478:**Movement 4 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1 (a bounded line repair; nothing re-staged): the nine coordinator-applied fixes kept and their joins smoothed (the boulder image made to agree with "*no length*"; Karis looks at three boxes and a case before "Four hands."; the cook-house questions after the restored exchange are of method only; "Four." given to Cael at the parapet); Vastin's refusal recomposed to locked Book 6 (the Ostrand case stated as the cause, twice, and not taken back; beside it "I had kept my hand off a door for a sound reason, and I was thankful of it for a poor one"; entered "on a form which has no line for why"); the two tracked passages in ch26 re-ordered (Lira prices the ladder aloud and shoulders the box before Cael understands; the clerk writes *four* and blots it before he looks at a face, then opens the door, looks at Vastin, opens his mouth and shuts it); Wind's ceiling removed; **Cleon's name comes to Cael at the cook-house counter and is then read on the card — nobody has said it aloud**; second tellings of the name-versus-count idea trimmed. Sol recheck: CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES; both tracked passages RESOLVED; every binding ruling borne out; the day arithmetic confirmed (161 days since the last self-reading; four days since the board; 282 days since the first sill; Oryn's gates). One punctuation fix applied by the coordinator (a broken dialogue join in ch21). The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report. Final: 35,179 prose words; gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (12 protected). Purse 136 marks; deployment thirty-two; ten fragments; the forenoon of day 284, inside the iron door under Treswick.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:484:- **Entry seam with Movement 4 ratified** (Sol plan audit): the five inside the iron door on the 284th with Cleon's one carried lamp; Seln above ground and off the count; the loads; purse 136; deployment thirty-two; bodies.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:493:- **THE ELEVENTH.** In that quiet minute **Cael acquired Iron-Wall-adjacent, from Vastin** — it did not fill, it *set*, "as a post is stood in its hole"; its prompt is *This far?*; he has told it no each time. **Not deployed. Not told to Vastin.** The protected lines are Cael's own cataloguing, printed once in italics (not a system block): "Iron-Wall-adjacent. Vastin. Partial. Iron family. Held. … Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Eleventh." **Eleven fragments; deployment since the Line: thirty-two.** Vastin: "I put the wall in front of it anyway. I'd like that entered…" ("it" is what Cael is, which he could not read) / "It's entered," — and Cael has entered more than the man knows: **a debt he cannot yet pay** ("Not told. I can't tell the taking without telling the rest, and the rest is six people's"). Lira has read the log.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:494:- **Costs.** **Karis's LEFT palm** cut on a step's edge: seven stitches, Brom's, bound in a strip of his shirt (no healer inside the gate will touch a hand without writing a name; she writes with the right). **Vastin's right knee has gone again on the eleventh day of Oryn's thirty** (a wall on it, against her order, which he heard word for word and asks that she be told): a lath cracked, re-splinted with a slat from Brom's box, twice its size; on the night of the 290th he cannot stand or hold a bowl. Brom: both shoulders. Lira: the right shoulder bruised; day twenty-five out of wool.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:509:- **What Seln's truth cost.** He had been on the yard's bench since the first bell as a porter with a hired frame. By standing and speaking he showed his face to a registry's clerk and joined it to the four and the card. He watches from **the roof of the last building above the cut's head, which has a parapet**, from the 286th. His reason, said in the loft: his own rule of the 282nd, which he had not meant to except himself from.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:521:- **Vastin.** At the yard on the 286th he held the dray's mule by the cheek-strap with the left hand and gave no order. On the 287th he moved toward the lamp four times (Lira counted); on the 288th twice; on the 290th not at all. On the 288th he began to post a watch and stopped ("That's one"). On the 289th he held three tall books at Lira's word, qualifying it ("I cannot undertake to carry them to a table"). His three heads on the night of the 290th: the knee (he had Oryn's words in his mind as the stick came down, and asks that she be told that he heard her); what the six came for (they looked past him at Cael); and that he knows no more of what Cael is than the plate did.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:532:**Where everyone is.** Six in the loft: Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Vastin (on a pallet under the blanketed gable window, unable to stand), and Seln on the ladder's head. Cleon is under the registry with fifty-two sheets on three tables, the board against the third, and tomorrow's card written and given. The clerk has written *the same* on six days. Oryn and the brown mule are north on her round (not on the page in this movement). Teague's five are east of the river (not on the page).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:534:**Cael.** Nineteen. **Eleven fragments. Deployment thirty-two.** He has stood unfiled in the middle gallery. He has been the lamp since the 285th and has knelt two feet from Rune in use for five days; nothing has come of that. He has begun to put the light where the looking will go. He wanted the Path tried on himself, wrote that he had not said so, and has not said so. He has the eleventh (Iron-Wall-adjacent), has read its lines, has told it no three times, and has not used it. **He has not told Vastin**, and holds that he cannot without telling the mechanism, which is the six's. He has not set foot on the square or its steps and has not looked at the crown; he has walked the lane with its four alleys fourteen times. He has ruled that the cut is not climbed at dusk again and has ruled nothing else for the morning. Body: sound; a tarred case struck his ear.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:544:**Vastin.** No office; no age stated. **He stood a wall on the eleventh day of thirty.** The knee let go sideways when he released it; one lath cracked; Brom has bound it again with a slat; it is twice its size; he cannot stand or hold a bowl on the night of the 290th. He knows what Oryn said it would cost. He gave his name, rank and office at the yard hatch on the 285th and was not written. He has apologised to Seln and been told to be nobody. He has asked for the wall to be entered and has been told that it is. **He does not know** the mechanism, what Cael carries, that anything was taken from him, the sum, or what is under the bar; he does not know what the six in hoods hoped to see and has said that he does not ask. He has not asked to join and nobody has spoken of it. Whether he heard Seln speak of the roof is not known.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:564:- **The eleventh and its entry.** Iron-Wall-adjacent, from Vastin, partial/held/defensive/rooted, tier equivalent unknown, deployment none. Cael has read it, refused its *This far?* three times, deployed nothing, and told only the log; Lira has therefore read it. Vastin has not been told. Cael recorded both Vastin's requested wall entry and more than Vastin knows (`chapter-32.md:237–257`; `chapter-33.md:149–175,205–227,291–299`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:105,125`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:565:- **Vastin.** Right knee, original day eleven of thirty: gone sideways again, re-lathed with one slat from Brom's box, twice its former size; on the night of the 290th he cannot stand or hold a bowl. He knowingly heard and broke Oryn's no-wall order and asks that she be told he heard. He has no office on the page, no stated age, and still knows nothing of the mechanism or eleventh (`chapter-33.md:129–145,185–227,285`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:115`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:573:**Movement 5 CLOSED (2026-10-12).** Same-author repair r1 (ch27–31; ch32–33 untouched apart from the eleventh's lines set in italics): the eight coordinator-applied fixes kept and re-joined — **ch27's scene at the Hall's table now turns on Cleon** (Cael's "Then what is it?" goes to Karis, who does not answer; Cleon, eyes shut at his desk, says the "Being believed" unit to himself in the hearing of five; Karis tells Brom who has believed him; Cleon opens his eyes for "Give me a week."; **Karis then asks the five in her own words — "I should like his week" — and Cael says it is hers**); ch30, Cleon re-sets his own week from the 287th (half the first went on his own page each morning; that is put by); ch31's opening keeps only her side of being believed; Seln's line at the hatch whole, with the narration noting that he said nothing that was not in the clerk's own book or at his ledge, "and he had said *we*, which lay in no book at all"; Cleon's close whole with the author's joins. The tracked passage re-ordered (Cleon gives his table orders over his shoulder with his finger on his line; when Cael looks again the chair is empty and the leaf lies face up, unmarked); two physical anchors in the cipher proof; restated method compressed; first-use anchors added. Sol recheck: **CLOSE, no line fixes**; the tracked passage RESOLVED; every binding ruling borne out; the coordinator's ruling on the eleventh's lines (Cael's own cataloguing, in italics, not a system block) treated as settled and consistent on the page. The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report. Final: 35,987 prose words; gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (17 protected). Purse 134 marks; deployment thirty-two; **eleven fragments**; the night of day 290, in the loft at Treswick.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:579:- **Entry seam with Movement 5 ratified** (Sol plan audit): the loft on the night of the 290th; eleven fragments; deployment thirty-two; purse 134; Vastin's knee re-splinted; Karis's left palm stitched; the fifty-two sheets on their three tables.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:580:- **THE TWELFTH.** On the 291st, at Cleon's "There," (his finger at the end of the Stair's fifth row), **Cael acquired Rune-adjacent, from Cleon** — "given, not taken": it did not pour or set, it *turned*. Protected, Cleon's, in this order: "A record sits … An instruction *leans* … This is a stair."; then Karis's "The strata lean too."; then "There,". The protected lines are Cael's own cataloguing, printed once in italics (never a system block): "Rune-adjacent. Cleon. Partial. Rune family. A made thing's lean … Deployment: none. Twelfth." with *He looked away. Kept.* and *Not a man.* **Twelve fragments; deployment since the Line: thirty-two.** It gives single words (*goes*, *sits*, *bears*, *nothing*); it costs the eyes afterward (paid on the stair, Vastin guiding him); made things only.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:581:- **How the twelfth behaves (ruled against the audit).** **It leans at every made thing, unbidden, outward** — the board, a rope-walk, a bridge, a hinge, a table — and Cael is learning not to look ("it looks before I've said that it may"). That is the plan's own wording ("the twelfth leans at every made thing … He learns not to look"; "catches himself reading made things everywhere") and stands. **It has never been turned inward, on Cael's own still place**, and he refused that turn once, deliberately, until Oryn has been asked. **The first INWARD turn is unbidden and belongs to Millrace (Movement 7).** It has never been used on a person, the crown or the leaf. A few unmeant outward glances (the rope-walk on the night of the 291st; Hesk's dividers; the inn table) are not counted as deployments.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:582:- **Who knows the twelfth:** Lira first, on the stair ("Twelfth. His. Lean."); Brom, Karis and Seln; **Cleon, told by Cael at the bell, in the order he has it** ("You did what." / "That's not in the classification system. That's not *supposed* to be possible. That's — " / "No. I'll not say that one. Not down here. Not to you."). Cleon knows how this ONE fragment came and nothing of any other. **Not Oryn; not Vastin.** **Cleon's warning** (protected, whole: "I'm going to pretend you didn't tell me that … Everything I read is *made* … If that fragment ever reads something for you that shouldn't be *made* and reads it anyway — … Don't tell me. Don't tell anyone. Just remember I said it.") is known to Cael and Cleon only and **is in no book**. "Cael did not tell anyone. He remembered." Cleon looks away from the boy on purpose from then on.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:585:- **The 292nd.** Hesk's parcel (the dividers; **Hesk's note, verbatim**) came by the carrier with the cut hat; Cael has not opened them on any distance. The dinner: four marks, seven cups poured and two kept under saucers (Karis; Oryn): **purse 130**. Protected, **Cael's, said to Vastin**: "Out here you count who's owed a seat … It's a different ledger." Seln read a slip, burned it and said "Closed."; what was on it is not given. **The first inventory written inside walls.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:587:- **Oryn's fourth gate** (unnamed hold): she watched a girl's Kindling from a bench, with no office, plate or clerk, and laid hands on nobody. She is two days behind, will not come late to the mill, and will read Cael "as deep as she went", asked first. She has heard of no leaf and no twelfth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:588:- **THE LEAF (the 293rd).** A single leaf of horn-coloured skin between beech boards from the bundle on Cleon's shelf; twenty-six lines on its face in the floors' letters; a list on its back, **not gone into**; a place four or five letters wide scraped pale, with one upright stroke left. **Karis read it aloud ONCE** (protected, whole, in the record's voice: "In the years of the unmaking … that they should not come again."). Her one account: "It's a title, not a name; the name's gone."; ***The Architect*** (spoken once, by her; the word on Vastin's copied page); by the year at the leaf's head, in the old town's count, **about four hundred years ago**; the purpose is the un-bound. "Older," she said. "Made. Us." **Heard by Karis, Cleon, Cael and Vastin; nobody who heard it quotes it.** Karis has all twenty-three letters (her first word that was not a number was *and*; the covered six-sign word was *set*).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:593:- **Still withheld:** the eleventh from Vastin (the debt entered as heavier); the twelfth from Oryn and Vastin; the deep-layer date (Cael and Seln, each alone, unsaid, unwritten); what is in Seln's case; the back of the leaf.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:613:- **The refusal to turn it inward (r1).** One present choice, near the bell, after he has seen that he must tell Cleon: Oryn's order (*Write it down and stop touching it.*), which he "had got round… once already, at a waypost" and does not get round now. Cleon's limit is not recited beside it; it stands in the notice (*Not a man.*).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:619:- **The meal.** Brom's ruling ("A parcel's come the breadth of the country to a hayloft, and found it. That's eaten on"); four marks at the half-door; the lower room; a goose, a pie, a white loaf, baked apples, cider; seven cups poured, two kept under saucers (Karis, above with her letters; Oryn). **Purse 130.** **(r1) The cups line is Cael's:** Vastin says of the two absent women, "I have kept the count at a great many boards. I should have struck both"; Cael answers with the protected line, across the table; Vastin: "I see that it is… I was never shown the book." Brom fills his cup. (Vastin's remark over the dividers and Brom's "That's so" are cut.)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:622:- **Oryn's fourth gate** (unnamed; r1: her scene now opens "On the evening of that same day, the two hundred and ninety-second, and four gates north of a fork-stone"; nine on the bench, the third of them a grandfather): a larger hold, stone to a man's head with split oak above. The hold's old woman, who keeps its days, rings the fourteen-year-olds on a threshing floor of beaten clay "at the first light after the moon's full", with a hazel stick. No office, plate or clerk. The girl (unnamed; a plait; a sheepskin too big) steps in; her eyes go to a place a hand's breadth from her cheek; she listens; her knees give a little; she tells her grandmother in her ear. Oryn sits forty yards off with her hands in her sleeves and lays a hand on nobody. "Whether it needed the ring, Oryn had never learned. Nobody at any of those gates had been willing to try it without." She has watched forty such. **Her decision:** the fifth gate has its day, the ford an hour, and she will not come late to the mill; and the reading she owes will go "as deep as she went", asked first. She is two days behind.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:629:- **The fire, as re-joined (r1).** Lira reads once; Cael turns his face away and watches eight bowls cool; she folds the page and says her line **to the fire**, before anything else; then the hole and the ruled box ("There's a stroke in the hole." / "Yes."); then she puts her thumb on the place through the paper and looks across at him. What her line does to him is told while Brom reads. **Seln (only "I'll keep it a while longer." fixed):** "There is a house on that hill which would give a great deal to have it laid upon its ledge; and I have asked myself on a good many nights what it was that I kept it out of… I had only ever seen that house from the inside of its own books. It stands upon this. I know now what the office is for, which I did not know at noon; and I had rather know it and carry the thing, than carry it blind." No count of years; the case on his chest, shut; nothing in it named. **Cael sits** on the fifth bucket when Seln hands the page back, so that Vastin's "Who's sitting across the fire" is so, and **gets up off it** for pole two. **Vastin's joins:** "I held that for the whole of my service, and was easy in it. Above Ostrand I was shown that the fault was meant. I called it corrupt; I put down a seal upon that word, and walked three hundred miles on it, and thought that I had come to the floor." He lifts his eyes from the fire only for the last piece. Before "I would have.": "He could have left it there, and it would have been true." **Pole two's joins:** "He had breath left for three words." / "It was Lira, and she had not taken her eyes off him since he got up." / "He stopped there, since the rest of it was not a plan."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:634:*(Refreshed after repair r1, 2026-10-12. No fact of the calendar, bodies, money, fragments or deployment changed in repair. The sixteen markers are gone; the speakers of three restored units are as the coordinator ruled.)*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:636:**Calendar.** The night of the **two hundred and ninety-third day past the Line**, in the long loft at Treswick. Days on the page: 291 (the ladder; the carts' street; the beam; the hatch; the gallery; the inside; the twelfth; the telling; the stair), the night of 291–292 (the tail), 292 (below; the parcel; the meal; the inventory; the light), Oryn at her fourth gate from dusk on the 292nd to first light on the 293rd, 293 (the leaf; the chronicle; the copy; Vastin's afternoon and stair; the street; the yard fire). No season, month or weekday name; no figure for the technician's date; no count of years since the Kindling.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:638:**Where everyone is.** Five in the loft (Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln at the ladder's head) and Vastin in the end stall beneath. Cleon has gone back up through the blue gate; the leaf, the chronicle and the board are under the registry; the fifty-two sheets lie on their tables one night more. Oryn and the brown mule are between her fourth gate and her fifth. Teague's five are east of the river (not on the page).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:640:**Cael.** Nineteen. **Twelve fragments. Deployment thirty-two.** The twelfth is acquired, read, told to Cleon, and held shut; three unmeant glances, not counted; never on a person, the crown, the leaf or himself. He keeps Cleon's warning and has told nobody. He has ruled that the twelfth is not turned inward until Oryn has been asked. He has not set foot on the square or its steps and has not looked at the crown; one unsteady moment was seen on the loft's boards and entered fourth on the page of the inventory, ruling *hold*. He has stood at the blue gate's groove by night and gone back down. He has heard the leaf, carried its copy, and said pole two aloud on his feet at the fire; it is not in the log. **Vastin is still not told of the eleventh**; the debt is entered as heavier. He owes Oryn two tellings at the mill (the readings round the place; the twelfth). Body: sound; tar on his palms; eyes recovered.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:654:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four, provisional. Four gates done of five; two days behind. She watched a Kindling from a bench and laid hands on nobody. Nobody has died under her hands. She has heard of no leaf. She has decided not to come late to the mill and to read Cael as deep as she goes, asked first.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:662:**Who knows what.** The mechanism: six, as before; **Cleon knows how one fragment came**; not Vastin or the clerk. The twelfth: the six (Oryn not yet) and Cleon. The warning: Cael and Cleon. The leaf: Karis, Cleon, Cael and Vastin by ear; Lira, Brom and Seln from the page; not Oryn, Teague or Pike. The unsteady light: Cael and Lira (from the log). The sum: Cael and Seln, each alone, unchanged.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:669:- **Leaf audience and wording discipline.** Karis, Cleon, Cael and Vastin heard the record once; Lira, Brom and Seln read Karis's page; Oryn has not heard it (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:3–29,95–105,251–269`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:3–37,53–103`). Nobody who heard it quotes it. The surviving public reductions are *made*, *for a kind*, Lira's existence conclusion, Vastin's *aimed/category/person*, and Cael's built-to-prevent conclusion (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:179–189`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:37,135,187` after fixes 10, 12 and 14).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:670:- **Fragments and knowledge.** Twelve fragments; deployment thirty-two. The eleventh remains unused and known to Lira through the log but not Vastin. The twelfth is known to Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Cleon; Oryn and Vastin have not been told. Cleon knows how this one fragment came but no other acquisition history. The warning is known only to Cael and Cleon and is in no book (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:197–239,279–339`; `manuscript/chapter-36.md:15–63`; `manuscript/chapter-37.md:219–227`). **Coordinator ruling (overrides the audit here):** the twelfth leans at made things UNBIDDEN and OUTWARD in Movement 6 (the board, the rope-walk, the bridge, the dividers, the inn table), and Cael is learning not to look; a few unmeant outward glances are on the page and are not counted as deployments. It has never been turned INWARD, and he refused that turn once, deliberately, until Oryn has been asked. Movement 7's beat is the first INWARD turn, and it comes unbidden.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:686:- **Entry seam with Movement 6 ratified** (Sol plan audit): twelve fragments; deployment thirty-two; purse 130; the loft and handcart to the 295th; the leaf's back unread; Vastin's knee day fourteen on the 293rd; Karis's stitched palm; Brom's arms; Lira's days out of wool; sixty yards of rope owed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:691:- **The cut revisited (the 296th).** Protected, **Vastin's**: "Here."; he stood on the bound leg once with the stick off the ground; Brom, low: "Held,"; "Two words," … "Both of them ours." (Vastin's, one speech — the two words are "Here" and "Held"); Cael: "Noted" — the first time he has given that word to this man. **A horseman kept a mile behind from the cut to the dark; a riderless horse stood in the alders on the western bank on the 297th.** No face, no name; Seln "can put it no higher". Nothing was seen east of the river.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:692:- **Lowmarch (the 297th).** Pike's twelfth line is the clearance (*Eight. Twenty; paid.*); the thirteenth, protected: *Treswick. Survey read. Bearing.*, with price and outcome left empty and said to be empty. **Cael read it the right way up, from Pike's side of the bench.** Pike put a DAY against the season line (nothing printed; "Eleventh. And dated."). **Teague's term, taken as a contract** (protected: "Ten of us on a wall's count. Your six and my four." … "Contract. Not more than that. I'll not have it called more." / "The wall's still the wall." — all Teague's): **ten on the count — Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Vastin; Teague, the tall man with the spear, the bow, the young one; NEITHER healer**; shares and costs by the count; **the field is Teague's** (Cael: "It's yours. I'd have asked you to take it."); the reading is Karis's ("You'll be asked."). The wall has a month on it and is not stood before the month is out. No hand was offered; the cloth still reads first and eleventh.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:696:- **THE GRADE (the 298th).** By laying Cleon's drawn copy on her own, Karis has four of the six signs: the word is ***set***. The fourth line: the mark, over those who are kindled and what is set; three. **Three marks:** a stroke alone (a box ruled and EMPTY — no sheet carries it; no first-tier site appears); a stroke with one bar (stake thirty-two, the dead surveyor's book, every sheet of the four places); a stroke with two bars (six sheets of a FIFTH place). Protected, Karis's: "A mark is a grade. The one they give a boy at fourteen says what he's *for*." … "The one on a sheet says how *old* the thing is."; "Somebody laid them down in order"; "It's observation. I'm telling you what the paper says. Not what it means." **Ages, each counted from the office's first sheet for the place: the Fallow sixty-one, the Stair ninety-four, the Hall a hundred and thirty-eight, the place behind the iron two hundred and six**; the fifth place has two unread signs where its figure should be ("older than two hundred and six", no figure). The paper says how long ago a first sheet was drawn and nothing of who walked there since. **Vastin's first "Noted."** Protected, Teague's: "Oldest last." … "Then that's where we're going." Hesk's dividers were **opened by Karis on Cael's loan** ("They're lent. I'll not open them."): the office's run from the fourth place to the fifth is "three days past the iron, a little less"; its compass point and its figure in lengths are unsaid. Stake thirty-two is back in the tarred case, never driven.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:697:- **The log of the 298th** (protected, whole, once; the grandmother is Cael's, Hesk's late wife): "Karis cracked the grade … Turns out the line was already drawn four hundred years ago. We're just the first to follow it to the end." **"Four hundred" stands nowhere else in the movement**; the centuries and the figure are Cael's own inference, put on his own page.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:698:- **Millrace (the 298th evening).** "Eleven off the ridge." (the woman with the net, as in Book 7) / "I know." (Oryn). Oryn to Vastin: "Stand there."; he stood an hour without a clause. Protected: "Nineteen days," (Vastin) / "Then it's eleven more." (Oryn). Oryn's terms: three holds owed yet on her round; "I'm a stop on my own route."; on nobody's count. "Sixth chair." (Lira) / "On my terms. Which are the only kind." (Oryn); she sat. **Readings, each asked first:** Brom's LEFT shoulder mended (a quarter-hour; she was grey), the right re-tied shorter by the older healer ("That'll do"); Lira's arm ("You listened when it told you the second time." / "Once." / "Once is once more than I priced." — "It's an arm."); Karis's palm ("Who sewed this." — the seven stitches drawn; "Write. Don't lean."); Vastin's knee — he told her of the alley wall himself; "It held in a cut," (Oryn); new linen and two laths; **the month stands as counted**; "Noted," (Vastin) / "That's new." (Oryn) / "It's a useful word." (Vastin) / "It's his." (Oryn). **Purse 127** (meal and a flitch, one mark).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:699:- **What Oryn was told before she read him:** the two self-readings of the 281st and why; **the eleventh** (Vastin's, in the stair; he does not know); **the twelfth** (from "a man under the registry"; made things only; "Not a man."). Her ruling: nothing is turned "on my plank"; the road is his own.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:700:- **THE DEEP READING.** "May I?" / "Yes." Forty minutes, to her own floor; she found the eleventh ("stands in the stream like a post") and the twelfth ("a little flat thing behind your eyes") unprompted; her current went round the still place from every side. **At about the three hundredth breath the twelfth turned inward, unbidden: *Still.* Then *Set.*** He kept his jaw and hands loose and did not let the next word come. Oryn felt only "Something turned over … out at the edge of you. One of yours, in its sleep," and dismissed it. **Her finding, protected, whole:** "There's a place in you I can't read because it isn't *flow*. I've spent my life reading flow. Whatever that is, it's not the kind of thing my Path was built for." **The two findings do not agree, and the two words are told to NO ONE** — not Oryn, not Lira. Lira offered the leaf; protected: "Is it a finding?" / "It's a leaf" … "Then it's not mine." … "Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table." … "Lie still when I say. That's still the term." **Oryn has not heard the leaf.** The eyes paid in the dark. Lira knows that something unasked came and has said that she will wait; the log gives four reasons for writing nothing ("Four is not mine to write") and the ruling *hold*. **Cleon's warning "has begun to lean".**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:701:- **Dawn, the 299th.** "Twelve," … "And a mule." (Seln). The mule carries the three boxes, the flat, a sack of meal, Oryn's pannier and canvas. Karis pinned a clean sheet to the hide's eastern edge, pricked the divider's point on it, and ruled the pencil line from the fourth ring through the point and a hand's breadth past ("I am not going to draw a stop that the paper does not give me").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:702:- **Bodies at dawn on the 299th.** Vastin: **day twenty of thirty**, Oryn's linen and two laths, stick, walking. Brom: both arms up to the shoulder. Lira: the arm released. Karis: stitches out, linen on, not to lean. Teague: the right wrist in linen under the leather. Cael: sound.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:717:- **The road east:** an east wind; Vastin walks the rise and turns once at its top; Brom touches Oryn's bowl at the fork-stone; the spring's slab is open to the wind and no paper is laid out; Seln stands at the basin with his back to the slab, and nothing is said.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:721:- **The cut on the 296th (43:47–97).** Water in it and no glass; the white crack is gone. "Here," is **Vastin's**, said to the wet stones; he lifts the stick a hand's breadth and stands on the bound leg for a breath and a half; **Brom, on his stone, says "Held,"** (mine: the second of the two words); "Two words. Both of them ours." is **Vastin's**; Cael answers "Noted," and has never before given him that word. The three wrecks have been broken up.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:727:- **Pike (44:101–163).** The twelfth line: *Clearance; the cut below the shoulder hold. Eight. Twenty; paid.* The thirteenth is the protected line, its last two columns empty and said to be empty. **The season line is dated:** a day in its ruled space by his own book's reckoning, nothing printed; "Eleventh. And dated." **As repaired, Cael reads the line as it is written without marking where he stands; Pike's "You're on my side." comes after the season line, and Cael then sees that he has read two leaves the right way up over the stump of an arm.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:732:  - Two copies of the fourth line laid one on the other give Karis four signs of six, and the word is *set*, which stands four times on the Stair's floor "always behind a sign that bears". The line: the mark, over those who are kindled and what is set; three. Stake thirty-two, the dead man's first page and the Stair's abstract lie together under the window. **Karis:** "A mark is a grade. The one they give a boy at fourteen says what he's *for*." (45:45).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:736:  - **Stake thirty-two goes back into the tarred case** in Vastin's hands (45:117); it has still never been driven.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:738:  - "Somebody laid them down in order," is **Karis's**, said to the hide; Lira's "Who?"; Vastin's drawn breath; **Karis:** "It's observation. I'm telling you what the paper says. Not what it means."; **Vastin's first "Noted,"** (45:173). **Teague:** "Oldest last." — Karis nods — "Then that's where we're going."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:740:- **Millrace (45:247–313), as repaired.** The woman with the net and Oryn's "I know." (KEPT). "Stand there." is Oryn's; Vastin hangs no clause on it; "Nineteen days," **Vastin**; "Then it's eleven more." **Oryn**. Teague speaks to Oryn for the first time; her answer in my words (three holds owed yet on this round, lying their way "for a day and some"; "You'll not count me, and you'll not send me. A crew doesn't write a well on its sheet because the road happens to pass it.") and then the protected "I'm a stop on my own route." A mark's worth of meal and a flitch: **127**. Brom sets her bowl before an upturned keg; "Sixth chair," **Lira**; "On my terms. Which are the only kind." **Oryn**; she sits.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:741:- **The readings (45:317–409), as repaired.** Brom: the older healer unties her own knot; Oryn shuts the wrench in the left shoulder (the arm to the height of his chin); the right is re-tied in two yards; "That'll do." Lira: the protected three lines are Oryn / Lira / Oryn; "It's an arm." Karis: the seven stitches drawn; "Write. Don't lean." Vastin: he has stood at the post the better part of an hour; he tells her of the wall himself; "It held in a cut," **Oryn**, "And then you asked it for a second, with eleven days on it"; the slat off, two new laths, the month as counted; "Noted," **Vastin** / "That's new." **Oryn** / "It's a useful word." **Vastin** / "It's his." **Oryn**, who does not look round at the boy, and whose mouth goes down at one corner.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:742:- **The two tellings (46:3–63):** unchanged. Oryn is told the eleventh as well as the twelfth; "But not on my plank."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:743:- **The deep reading (46:67–177):** unchanged in substance; the twelfth and the eleventh are named by their labels at the points of decision. *Still.* *Set.* A next word, not let come. Oryn's half-notice stands.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:744:- **After the reading (46:181–237), as repaired.** The scene opens with her hands already off and Oryn on her feet; **she gives the finding standing, and only then finds the keg**; the greyness is what the saying cost. Lira reminds her of "all of it" and offers the paper; "Is it a finding?" **Oryn** / "It's a leaf," **Lira**, who adds only that somebody wrote it down, that one of them can read it, and that it is not about a body; "Then it's not mine." — Oryn's reason in my words (a plank and two hands; a sheet at the foot of every bed that "was never once the patient") — "Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table." The paper is not unfolded. Her last word to Cael as she sends them to bed: "Lie still when I say. That's still the term."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:756:**Cael.** Nineteen. **Twelve fragments. Deployment thirty-two.** He was a lamp for ten days and has entered it. He did not look back at the crown from the bridge. He has told Oryn the two self-readings of the 281st, the eleventh and the twelfth. He has told nobody the two words (*still*; *set*), the warning, or the date. He holds Oryn's finding word for word and has not written it; he has written that one thing came under her hands, unasked, and four reasons for not writing what. He has told Lira that something came and that he has no name for it. He walks at Teague's left and has said aloud that the field is Teague's. He lent the dividers twice and did not open them. *He has marked, beside the protected log, which of its claims are the paper's and which are his own.* The eleventh's debt stands. Body: sound; the eyes paid on the night of the 298th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:758:**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. No burst. The arm is "an arm" (day thirty-three out of the wool on the 298th); Oryn: she listened the second time it told her. She said "Sixth chair." She offered the leaf and was declined. *She knows from his eyes that the twelfth looked at something on the night of the 298th; she did not see him change on the plank.* She has agreed to wait.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:760:**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. No grey. Left shoulder mended by Oryn; right re-tied by the older healer in two yards; both arms come up to his shoulders on the 299th. *He said "Held," in the cut.* The rope debt is paid; the thumbed slip is with Pike. **The purse: a hundred and twenty-seven.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:762:**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three; no point struck. She holds her own copy of the leaf's back and Cleon's drawn copy. She has the fourth line (the mark; those who are kindled; what is set; three), the three boxes with the first empty, *the four series years (61, 94, 138, 206: years counted from the first sheet that the office holds for each place)*, a fifth place of the two-bar mark with no figure, and the office's run to it. She has not said the compass point or the figure in lengths aloud; five lines of the list are unturned. Left palm: stitches drawn, in Oryn's linen; she writes and draws with it. The hide has a clean sheet pinned to its eastern edge, with a prick at the divider's point and a line ruled a hand's breadth past it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:766:**Vastin.** No office; no age stated. **Right knee: day twenty of thirty on the 299th**; Oryn's linen and two new laths; the month as counted. He rode on the level and walked every hill, the cut and the notch. *"Here," and "Two words. Both of them ours." are his;* he stood on the leg once with the stick up. He kept and signed the tally. He sat before the six and laid no copper. He took Oryn's "Stand there." without a clause, gave her "Nineteen days," and stood an hour. He has said "Noted" twice (the grade; the knee). *He put stake thirty-two back into the tarred case, which he carries.* He is on Teague's count as one of "your six"; that is a count for a contract; he has not asked to join and nobody has spoken of it. *The factor made him no offer.* He does not know the mechanism, the eleventh, the twelfth, the two words, the date, or what is under the bar; he knows that he is not told, and that it is "six people's".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:768:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four, provisional. Nobody has died under her hands. She has read Brom, Lira, Karis and Vastin, each asked first, and Cael, asked first, for forty minutes, to her own floor; her finding is given (46:189), standing. She knows of twelve and whose the eleventh and twelfth were; she felt "something turn over, out at the edge" and thought nothing of it. **She has not heard the leaf** and has not been shown the grade. *She has three holds owed yet on this round; her road lies with theirs for a day and some and then turns;* she is on nobody's count and is sent by nobody; she has sat in the sixth place.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:770:**Teague and his crew.** The contract is taken: ten on the count; shares and costs by the count; the field his; the reading Karis's. *"The wall's still the wall." and the Force line are his.* His wrist was used once, on a cart, and is wrapped in linen under the leather. He has not said "Noted." The tall man, the bow and the older healer have said nothing to the six. What his four have been told: that an office's survey was read at Treswick and gave a bearing; that the wall has a month on it; the four figures on the hide and "three days past the iron". Not told: the leaf, the list, the mechanism, any fragment, the date, who Vastin was.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:772:**Pike's book and the cloth.** Thirteen lines; the thirteenth with its last two columns empty. The season line is dated (a day; no figure). Eleventh on the cloth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:778:**Objects and money.** **130 → 128** (the 295th: the rope, two marks) **→ 127** (the 298th: meal and a flitch, one mark). Coppers are small money: Vastin's three to the dray's carter; the ferry's fare waived. The reserve sealed in the third box. The rope debt is paid. On the mule: three boxes, the flat, a sack of meal, Oryn's pannier and canvas. With Karis: the hide with its pinned sheet, the Ternhall brass, her notebook, Cleon's roll, the sheet of three boxes, Vastin's copied page. With Cael: Hesk's book, the dividers shut in it, the fair copy of the leaf. With Vastin: the tarred kit case, *with stake thirty-two back in it, never driven*.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:780:**Who knows what.** The mechanism: six, as before; Cleon knows how one fragment came. The twelfth: the six (Oryn now among them) and Cleon. The eleventh: Cael, Lira (the log) and Oryn; not Vastin. The warning: Cael and Cleon. **The two words: Cael alone.** That something came on the plank: Cael; Lira (by his eyes and his word); Oryn only as "one of yours, in its sleep". The leaf: unchanged (not Oryn, Teague or Pike). The list's fourth line and the grade: the six and Vastin; Teague in part. The date: Cael and Seln, each alone.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:782:**Open threads.** Two findings that do not agree, and one of them in nobody's book. A warning that has begun to lean. A box ruled for a mark that no sheet carries. A fifth place with no figure and two signs unread in its corner. Five lines of a list spelled and not turned. A compass point and a measure that Karis has not said aloud. A line ruled past a point. A debt to a man who walks a stride behind Brom. A horse in the alders. A wrist in linen. Oryn's road, which runs with theirs for a day and some.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:785:- **Inventory and order:** twelve fragments; deployment thirty-two; Seln ahead, tall spear, Teague with Cael at his left a stride back, Lira, young one, Karis plus both healers and mule in the middle, Brom, Vastin a stride behind, bow last (`chapter-44.md:281–291`; `chapter-46.md:337–341`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:788:- **Oryn:** knows both self-readings and why, eleven and twelve and their sources/limits, and that Cael had not deliberately turned the twelfth inward; has not heard the leaf or seen the grade; was refused nothing she was owed, but Cael keeps *still/set*, Cleon's warning and the date. She sensed only “one of yours” turn and dismissed it (`chapter-46.md:9–63,171–175,221–227`). Her own finding is known to Cael and Lira because it was spoken before both (`46:193–219`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:789:- **Cael's two findings:** Oryn's exact finding is held but not copied; *still* then *set* is Cael's alone; the next word was suppressed; the four reasons and “hold” are in the log without the words (`chapter-46.md:197–211,267–289`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:791:- **Dividers and stake:** Karis has opened Hesk's dividers twice on the office distance, on Cael's leave; Cael has not opened them and they end shut in his book (`chapter-45.md:129–143`; `chapter-46.md:323–335`). Stake thirty-two is back in Vastin's tarred case and has never been driven.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:792:- **Bodies/counts at dawn 299:** Vastin day 20 of 30, Oryn's linen/two laths, stick; Brom's left shoulder mended, right re-tied, both arms to shoulder height; Lira's arm released; Karis's stitches out, linen on, scar promised, do not lean; Teague's wrist wrapped; Cael's eyes paid in the dark (`chapter-45.md:295–377`; `chapter-46.md:233–239,299–317`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:793:- **Money/load:** purse 127; reserve sealed in third box; mule carries three boxes, flat, meal sack, Oryn's pannier and canvas; Cael carries fair leaf copy and dividers; Karis has hide/pinned sheet, notebook, Cleon roll, three-box sheet and Vastin copy (`chapter-45.md:283`; `chapter-46.md:303–307,321–335`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:795:- **Other live threads:** Cleon remains below with skin leaf, chronicle and board; Seln's case stays shut on his chest, contents unnamed; Vastin's debt and ignorance stand; Pike has thirteen lines and a dated season-space with no printed date; rope debt is paid; Oryn's road is her own and will diverge (`chapter-41.md:213`; `chapter-44.md:137–157,205–211`; `chapter-46.md:31–47,337–341`).

