+### Coordinator's specific readings
+
+**a. Lira/plank — AMEND.** Draft `chapter-51.md:59` contradicts closed `chapter-46.md:151–169,241–265` and STATE_LEDGER:758. Fix 14.
+
+**b. Deployment thirty-three — AMEND to thirty-two.** Closed Movement 7 ends at thirty-two (`chapter-46.md:287`; STATE_LEDGER:756). BOOK_MAP §7 assigns Force's first/only stone use to the pass, and the Movement 8 seep beat assigns the finding to Teague's field reading and hands. The deliberate read at `chapter-48.md:247–251` is a deployment under this edition's own earnest-use rule; the calf precedent does not license an added use. Remove it and repair `chapter-48.md:327`, `chapter-49.md:271`, `chapter-51.md:349`, `chapter-53.md:137,273`. Movement 9 must inherit thirty-two.
+
+**c. How “four hundred years back” is earned — AMEND.** The source does not print a derivation; it reconciles index, office ages, wall lean, radius, stake count, office distance and map point, then gives one conclusion (`source chapter-20.md:31–37,129`). The draft instead identifies the two signs as a year abbreviation, compares them to the leaf's head, says “same hundred,” enumerates eleven candidates, and places the leaf's year among them (`chapter-52.md:129–145`; `chapter-53.md:161–173`). That is page-level date arithmetic, lays the fifth-place sheet against the leaf's date, and over-explains what the fixed S20 line alone may state. It also exceeds closed Movement 7, which knew only two unread signs and Vastin's “old style” (`closed chapter-45.md`; STATE_LEDGER:762). Keep only recognition that the signs are old clerk-year form, a private off-page reckoning, and the fixed close; fixes 21–22 and 27–29.
+
+**d. Karis's “five years” — AMEND.** Both occurrences (`chapter-53.md:175,221`) are unsupported authorial durations. OWNER #18 removed Book 8's five-year counts since Kindling and BOOK_MAP §12 C2 bars numeric academy-era spans. Closed text supports long exclusion and shut presses, not exactly five years. Fixes 29 and 33 use nonnumeric duration.
+
+**e. Annual sheets and present keeper — SPLIT.** The present Compact watch, three physical ages of iron, trodden perimeter and stock of bars may stand (`chapter-49.md:193–217`; `chapter-51.md:155–169`) because the protected log identifies the Compact as having fenced and posted the site. The Stair sentence “There is one to a year” must not: closed Movement 7 says the corner figure is years from a first sheet and proves nothing about yearly visits (draft `chapter-47.md:43–47`; closed `chapter-45.md:85–90`). Recent spade work may remain as Compact administration, not mysterious agency. Fix 1. Cut only Karis's souvenir bar (fix 17).
+
+**f. Cairn and intervals — KEEP.** See sections 2–3. The locked chock-stones after the Hall remain at `chapter-48.md:109–117`; a second, plan-required cairn before the Hall is not contradicted by Book 7. The faster return is explained at `chapter-47.md:249–253` and the map's fixed dates govern.
+
+**g. Watcher east of river — KEEP.** The bay rider is a keeper's second-hand report, no face/name, and is learned on the 300th (`chapter-47.md:225–231`). Closed Movement 7's no-sighting status at dawn 299 remains true.
+
+**h. Vastin over iron — KEEP.** He refuses a wall, not standing; the plan names him among five (`chapter-49.md:33–49`; `chapter-50.md:205–211`). “To the grain” demonstrates the established site rule; the 307th court can locate/draw the same rule without being pre-empted (`chapter-50.md:315–319`).
+
+**i. “Nobody declares” — KEEP after marker restoration.** The watch carries east knowledge of silent Iron taking bolts, silent Force shifting timber outside, and five bodies standing inside; it sees no working inside (`chapter-50.md:35–65,99–105,181–299`). That is exactly the packet lock.
+
+**j. Who is told — AMEND Oryn only.** Lira knows at `chapter-51.md:55–75`; Brom knows at `chapter-53.md:135–151`; Karis and Seln may inherit it through Lira/log as the report states. Oryn's across-iron refusal at `chapter-51.md:179–195` is situational, but the packet requires her later telling. Fix 25. Teague and Vastin remain untold. “Bronze” is protected and may be connected to Cael's earlier refusal.
+
+**k. Force lined dry — KEEP.** Alignment without the command is expressly required; Lira and Brom seeing it changes no count (`chapter-53.md:75–151`). The ribs warn and first use remains the pass.
+
+**l. Karis cutaway — AMEND.** `chapter-53.md:189–227` physically lays out the two pages, calls them two rulers, characterizes the leaf as a dead man's account with the name scraped, and publishes “Second page.” Those sentences do join the pages even while denying the inference. Keep only that she knows a six-word sentence exists and refuses to speak/write it; fixes 30–34.
+
+**m. Small sums and custody — KEEP except bar.** Four marks from the purse, one copper for the mule, Brom's three personal coppers, the old stave and trestle stick all reconcile (`chapter-47.md:223–229`; `chapter-48.md:13–17`; `chapter-51.md:45–49`; `chapter-49.md:183–189`; `chapter-52.md:3–9`). Cut Karis's removed bar (fix 17).
+
+## 7. Names
+
+No named person, animal or place outside the plan appears. The authorized existing names are Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Vastin, Oryn, Teague, Hesk, Cleon, Pike, Ternhall, Treswick, Denvash, Lowmarch, Millrace, the Fallow, the Stair, the Hall and the Sunken Span. Common nouns such as “the sink,” “the shelf,” “the step” and “the gap” are descriptive labels, not new proper names (`chapter-49.md:77–97`; `chapter-52.md:29–37`).
+
+The following remain deliberately unnamed and must stay so: the south-hold keeper; the man on a bay; the people behind the two barred holds; the seven watch members (one empty-handed practitioner, two bowmen, four stave carriers, one coughing); Teague's tall man, broad man, young one and older healer; the miller's man; and the brown mule. No owner name is required for Movement 8.
+
+## 8. Next-movement inheritance not already complete in MOVEMENT-009
+
+Movement 9 must inherit the following surviving particulars in addition to its packet:
+
+- **Fragments and knowledge:** thirteen fragments; deployment thirty-two. The thirteenth is Force-adjacent from Teague, partial Bronze, unused; it listens along a braced heel-to-palm line and costs back along that line. Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and—after fix 25—Oryn know of it; Teague and Vastin do not. Teague is the second unpaid acquisition debt, beside Vastin. The twelfth has leaned outward at the west pier and at fourteen made sheets, never inward here. The two words *still/set* remain Cael's alone (`chapter-50.md:121–157`; `chapter-51.md:55–75,311–351`; `chapter-52.md:71–101`; `chapter-53.md:75–151`).
+- **What went east:** seven hooded watch members left singly with a day's start. They saw Brom take two bolts on silent Iron, Teague move the barricade with silent Force, and five people—including a boy and an old man on a stick—stand and walk inside the line. They saw nothing work inside and nobody die. They carried the broken bow; the sound bow and one stave remained at the post (`chapter-50.md:35–65,99–105,181–301`; `chapter-51.md:7–11`).
+- **Bodies:** the broad man's right shin is knit, boarded and stick-bearing; his crossbow stock is split. Teague's right wrist/elbow are in linen to the shoulder on a slat and the hand is unreliable; a third use would mean a splint. Brom has a breastbone bruise and ridged left-forearm bruise through a week of colours. Cael has a ten-day left collar-bone welt. Vastin's right knee is day twenty-six of thirty. Two men—Vastin and the broad man—are on sticks (`chapter-51.md:15–37,79–175`; `chapter-52.md:3–9`; `chapter-53.md:17–67,265`).
+- **Teague's crew:** they know five people crossed and stood whole and that a boy did it with a stick; they do not know mechanism, fragments, leaf, lamps page, slips, date, Vastin's former office, or “behind it.” The young one follows where he is looked at; the tall man and older healer still have not spoken to the six (`chapter-50.md:181–299`; `chapter-51.md:79–175`).
+- **Three record objects/pages:** (1) Karis holds the torn lamps-finding leaf in the back of her notebook, filed on its own; (2) Cael holds the folded fair copy of the chamber leaf in Hesk's book/coat, still not quoted; (3) the technician's sheet remains at the foot of the second row in the flat, its deep-layer date known separately to Cael and Seln and said/written by neither. No line joins (1) and (2), and Cael added no page of his own (`chapter-52.md:181–221`; `chapter-53.md:263–275`).
+- **Map point and notch:** the fifth point is a thumbnail ring around the prick, uninked until corded. The bearing runs through the square notch; Seln looked from a mile, saw no fire, person, movement or heel-mark, disliked the absence, and will look again from nearer at first light before Teague moves (`chapter-52.md:149–157`; `chapter-53.md:233–261,281–289`).
+- **Oryn:** five days past the noon-300 cairn; she stayed for Brom's week, Vastin's knee and the large edge, with three holds still owed and word already sent. She has not heard the chamber leaf. She now knows thirteen and the rib cost but does not know *still/set* (`chapter-47.md:195–245`; `chapter-53.md:25,265`; fix 25).
+- **Seln:** he has looked at the pass and said only “I looked at it.” His case remains shut on his chest, contents unnamed (`chapter-49.md:187–219`; `chapter-53.md:233–261`).
+- **Day, bodies, money and load:** night of the 305th; twelve people and the brown mule; purse 123; no purse spend after the four marks. The mule bears three boxes, the flat, meal, Oryn's pannier and canvas. Karis has the hide/pinned sheet, brass, notebook, Cleon's roll, three-box sheet, Vastin's copied page and nine pier sheets; Cael has Hesk's book, shut dividers and folded fair copy; Vastin has the tarred kit case with cord, mallet and never-driven stake thirty-two. The two slips are re-pinned under the oldest row's knot, seals unnamed (`chapter-52.md:41–69,225–283`; `chapter-53.md:263–289`).
