+# Plan audit — Movement 8, “The Sunken Span”
+
+## Verdict: REPAIR — bounded line repair
+
+The movement is structurally sound: the seven-day leg, the four fight exchanges, the no-death win, the Span inspection, the blanket work, the three cutaways, and the handoff to the pass are all present in the required order. It is not ratifiable as printed because ten protected-text markers remain, the seep adds a forbidden thirty-third deployment, the 305th pages perform and display date arithmetic the edition expressly withholds, Karis's cutaway joins the leaf and the lamps finding in her interior, one annual-visit inference contradicts closed Movement 7, Lira remembers a plank reaction that the closed chapter cut, Oryn is not given the thirteenth as the packet requires, and the protected S19 log has a word-level italics error. These are local repairs; no chapter or fight restaging is required.
+
+After the fixes below, the movement ends with thirteen fragments, deployment **thirty-two**, purse **123**, twelve people and the mule under the shale step on the night of the 305th, Oryn five days past her cairn, and Teague and Vastin still untold of the thirteenth.
+
+## 1. Continuity with closed text
+
+### Entry seam and carried state
+
+The draft correctly inherits dawn on the 299th: twelve and a mule; Seln ahead, the tall man, Teague with Cael at his left a stride back, Lira, the young one, Karis and the healers/mule, Brom, Vastin, and the broad man; Teague's contracted ten exclude both healers; purse 127; Vastin day twenty of thirty and walking; Teague's wrist in linen; twelve fragments and deployment thirty-two; Karis alone handles the dividers; stake thirty-two is back in the tarred case (`chapter-47.md:3–31,53–81,185–191`; closed `chapter-46.md:299–341`; STATE_LEDGER:756–793). The mule's load and the six's objects also agree at entry (`chapter-47.md:3–15`; closed `chapter-46.md:303–307,321–335`).
+
+The two Movement 7 findings remain correctly limited. Cael does not disclose *still* or *set*, and Oryn's distinct finding is not converted into mechanism knowledge (`chapter-47.md:185–191`; `chapter-53.md:71,117`; closed `chapter-46.md:151–175,197–227,267–289`). Lira's line at `chapter-51.md:59`, however, says he “went as stiff as you did on a plank.” Closed text says she knew something came because his eyes paid, while his jaw and hands stayed loose; the ledger expressly says she did **not** see him change on the plank (closed `chapter-46.md:151–169,241–265`; STATE_LEDGER:758). Fix 14 keeps her observation at the timbers and removes the false remembered body reaction.
+
+### Bodies, injuries, people and knowledge
+
+- The draft advances Vastin correctly from day twenty on the 299th to day twenty-six on the 305th (`chapter-47.md:185`; `chapter-53.md:265`), keeps the right knee in linen/laths and him on a stick, and never gives him an age (`chapter-47.md:7–13`; `chapter-49.md:33–49`; `chapter-53.md:23–35`). His crossing at `chapter-50.md:205–211,315–319` does not spend the court line: Book 7's closed rule is that every ordinary Path dies inside a site, and Movement 9 may make the same fact evidentiary at the drawn stride.
+- Teague's right wrist and then elbow take the Force recoil (`chapter-50.md:99–113`); the arm is in linen to the shoulder on a slat by `chapter-53.md:61–69`. The protected warning is missing only because marker 7 remains (`chapter-51.md:15–23`; fix 10).
+- The broad man's right shin—the good leg—is broken, set, knit, boarded and later borne on a trestle leg (`chapter-50.md:325–367`; `chapter-52.md:3–9`; `chapter-53.md:17–57`). That follows the edition plan, although the superseded source used the bad leg (`source chapter-19.md:115–127`). The unheard consent on the 304th is to Oryn, not “to the six”; his first word to the six remains “Aye” on the 305th (`chapter-50.md:337–343`; `chapter-53.md:27–47`).
+- Brom's two bolt bruises and “week of colours,” Cael's left collar-bone welt, Karis's bound left palm, and Oryn's quarter-hour grey are all carried (`chapter-51.md:25–37,49–53`; `chapter-53.md:51–57`). Nobody dies and there is no gore (`chapter-50.md:99–105,299–301,325–367`).
+- Teague's four see five bodies stand and walk inside the line; they are not told the mechanism, a fragment, the leaf, the lamps finding, the slips, the date, or the doctrine “behind it” (`chapter-50.md:181–299`; `chapter-51.md:79–175`). No wall drill occurs. Teague's “place behind my shoulder” thanks at `chapter-53.md:63–67` is a personal field observation, not the pass-morning doctrine.
+
+### Objects and money
+
+The purse moves 127 → 123 by four marks at the hold on the 300th (`chapter-47.md:223–229`). That is compatible with BOOK_MAP's “123 by the 304th”; the map fixes the resulting balance, not the purchase scene. The copper for the mule's bucket and Brom's three personal coppers are explicitly separate small money (`chapter-48.md:13–17`; `chapter-51.md:45–49`). The reserve remains sealed and no contrary spend appears.
+
+The watchman's cut stave is Seln's thirteen-day carry from the alley and is lent to Cael (`chapter-49.md:183–189,273`; closed `chapter-43.md:47–97`). The second stick is cut from the watch's trestle (`chapter-52.md:3–9`). The two slips can have remained unseen under the oldest row's tape: the spring work counted and re-taped rows, but did not open a clerk's tag under the knot; Vastin's mistaken-tag explanation closes the seam (`chapter-52.md:225–249`; closed Movement 3 record-handling). Keep the slips.
+
+The bundle of new bars may remain part of the posted watch's kit (`chapter-51.md:155–169`), but Karis's removal of one with Teague's leave (`chapter-51.md:331–333`) creates unnecessary custody not carried by Movement 9. Fix 17 leaves the bars at the post.
+
+### Quiet-ground law and declarations
+
+Locked Books 5–7 establish that every ordinary Path dies at the site line while Cael's adjacent fragments remain (`universe-bible.md:154–155`; closed Book 7 site crossings; `chapter-50.md:181–211`). The draft obeys that law: Lira, Karis, the young one and Vastin lose what they carry; Cael's fragments remain and none is opened (`chapter-50.md:181–211,235–299`). Vastin's “To the grain” is therefore required continuity, not a reveal spent early (`chapter-50.md:315–319`).
+
+“Nobody declares” remains intact in the edition's operative sense. The watch sees Brom's silent Iron under his coat and Teague's silent Force against a timber outside the line (`chapter-50.md:35–65,99–105`); it sees five bodies stand inside and sees nothing work there (`chapter-50.md:181–299`). No one names a Path, throws one at a person, or answers the watch's white light. The Compact can consequently learn that the crew walks out declaring-capable and that bodies stand inside, without learning what works inside. The watch's own demand and low white light (`chapter-50.md:15–27`) are compatible author-owned staging.
+
+## 2. Movement plan, sequence locks and owner flags
+
+### Beat and withholding audit
+
+The required order holds: Stair bowl and one-hour rim (`chapter-47.md:29–81`); cairn at noon on the 300th and Oryn east (`chapter-47.md:195–245`); Hall marsh and two dry camps (`chapter-47.md:249–307`; `chapter-48.md:3–105`); seep with Teague's reading, the boy stopped wordlessly, and water obtained (`chapter-48.md:131–327`); crest at dusk on the 303rd (`chapter-49.md:3–177`); watch/fight on the 304th (`chapter-50.md:3–367`); Span at noon and nothing on the crown (`chapter-51.md:179–353`); blanket, lamps page and slips on the 305th (`chapter-52.md:41–285`); one fire, dry Force frame, Karis and Seln cutaways, and the protected close (`chapter-53.md:3–293`).
+
+The material withholdings mostly hold: the technician's registry date is never printed; the seals are unnamed; Seln's case is shut on his chest and its contents unnamed (`chapter-49.md:187–219`); no one uses *terminal*, *circuit* or *infrastructure*; the broad man's first word to the six is correctly delayed; the tall man and older healer do not speak to the six; Teague and Vastin are not told the thirteenth. The exceptions are the 305th displayed date-reduction (`chapter-52.md:129–145`; `chapter-53.md:161–173`) and Karis's interior joining the leaf and lamps page (`chapter-53.md:189–227`), repaired by fixes 21–22 and 27–34.
+
+The thirteenth is acquired once in Cael's plain italic catalogue, with Tier A 14 word-for-word and no system heading (`chapter-50.md:121–129`). Recoil reaches wrist then elbow, and Teague is not told (`chapter-50.md:99–129`; `chapter-51.md:55–75`; `chapter-53.md:117,147`). The dry stance is not a deployment: no word is given, the ribs warn, and the first use remains the pass (`chapter-53.md:75–151`; MOVEMENT-009.md pass sequence). The seep read is different: it is a deliberate use in earnest and must be removed (section 6; fixes 2–7, 16, 23, 35).
+
+Five cross stake thirty-four in the required order—Cael, Lira, Karis, young one, Vastin—while Teague, tall man, Brom and broad man remain on the shelf (`chapter-50.md:181–215`). The pinch is eleven seconds; the broad man falls at four; Teague does not turn; seven go east singly and nobody pursues (`chapter-50.md:235–303`). “We've been in three times” is Cael's source speech and is true of the established six as a crew, not a claim that the young one or Vastin personally made three crossings.
+
