editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-53.md:221:She wanted to. She let herself know that as well, since it was true, and since a refusal that costs nothing is only a habit. She had stood for five years on the wrong side of shut presses. She had never in her life been so near to a thing, with a pencil in reach.
